            score = 122,
            author = "sandyra",
            text = "For those trying to hunt down:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=8704 from The Hinterlands (Personal stats: Killed some stalkers, some trolls, some owlbeasts (about 20 all told)... Then killed my first ooze at Skulk Rock, and it dropped)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=8623 from Tanaris (Personal stats:  Went into Zul'Farrak like all other posters recommend, killed some twenty or thirty trolls and scarabs, and it dropped from one of the troll corpses)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=8705 from Feralas  (Personal stats:  As recommended by many other posters, Feral Scar Yetis - dropped on my first kill)\n\nOnly available if you have not already completed the quest.\nYes these still drop in Mists of Pandaria.\nYes it can drop off ANY mob in the respective zone, however https://www.wowhead.com/item=8705 has the highest drop rate from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=5292 IF you haven't already done the quest.\nIt WILL eventually drop - some days RNG is your best friend, other days you want to repeatedly punch a kitten (or other obscenely fluffy creature) just to illustrate how cruel the universe can be.\nThe command to check if you have completed ANY of the distress beacon quests is here (special thanks to MrsSushi (http://www.wowhead.com/user=MrsSushi) for locating the updated version of this which is still working as of patch 5.3):\n\n/run local z={\"Tanaris\",\"Hinterlands\",\"Feralas\"}for k,v in pairs({{351,648},{485,836},{25475,25476}})do print(z[k])for i,q in pairs(v)do print(\" #\"..i,\"\\124Hquest:\"..q..\"\\124h[\"..q..\"]\\124h\" ,IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(q)and COMPLETE or INCOMPLETE)end end\n\nYou will see lines of dialogue that look like this:\nTanaris\n#1 [351] Complete\n#2 [648] Complete\nHinterlands\n#1 [485] Complete\n#2 [836] Complete\nFeralas\n#1 [25475] Incomplete\n#2 [25476] Incomplete\n\nAfter completing all three escorts, you can then acquire the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=3721 and get your https://www.wowhead.com/item=10398.\n\nHappy hunting!",
            date = "2011-11-05T21:50:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=485#comments:id=1564093",
        },
        {
            id = 1255,
            score = 37,
            author = "powdahound",
            text = "You can find the robot at 49,38 in the Hinterlands. It's in the lake that lies west of Skull Rock.",
            date = "2006-09-30T17:49:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=485#comments:id=1255",
        },
        {
            id = 63935,
            score = 37,
            author = "11563",
            text = "I'm going to post this message on all three of these \"Find\" quests, just in case someone doesn't see it on one of the other two.\n\nIf you plan to do these quests in a group (which is very helpful, as any escort quest) everyone must first have completed the \"Find\" part of the quest, which means you have to find the chicken, choose \"Complete\" and then be *offered* the next part of the quest, which is the actual escort part. But do not accept this part until everyone has done the \"Find\" part, otherwise it won't be offered to them as escort quests normally are, because technically you are not on the same stage of the quest yet.\n\nSo just complete the \"Find\" part, then when the next part is offered, decline it until everyone is ready to accept it.",
            date = "2007-04-08T15:17:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=485#comments:id=63935",
        },
        {
            id = 960986,
            score = 33,
            author = "536923",
            text = "This is true. According to a GM, if one of the beacons quests were accepted, the other beacons would not drop.  If you did not accept the quest and left the beacon in your bag, then they others would drop.  If the quest is in your log, other beacons will not drop.\n\nI couldnt get another beacon, i specifically tried for days, untill i spoke to a GM about it.",
            date = "2010-01-30T22:37:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=485#comments:id=960986",
        },
        {
            id = 551162,
            score = 24,
            author = "227695",
            text = "took me no more than 20 minutes farming wolfs in hinterlands as an 80 level.\n\nalso: OOX-09/HL distress beacon this \"HL\" means HinterLands\nthe same is with OOX-17/TN distress beacon this \"TN\" comes from TaNaris\nand the other OOX-22/FE  is about FElaras",
            date = "2009-01-07T08:58:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=485#comments:id=551162",
        },
    },
    [486] = {
        {
            id = 1867100,
            score = 22,
            author = "Deathbat",
            text = "Follow the path Northwest out of Dolanaar, and keeping following the road until you see 2 rangers on nightsabers mounts; Huntress Yaeliura (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=10606) and Moon Priestess Amara (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2151), who will have the quest The Road To Darnassus (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=487) for you.\n\nJust behind them, there is a path that works its way into the trees. This is the path you want to follow. As you follow this path, you will discover The Cleft. Here, you'll find Gnarlpine Ambusher (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2152) to complete the quest of The Road To Darnassus as you make your way towards Ursal the Mauler.\n\nJust follow the path of lights uphill and it will lead you right to Ursal the Mauler, who stands at the front of a cave at cords 51.7/39.3\n\nHope this helps!",
            date = "2013-06-16T03:17:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=486#comments:id=1867100",
        },
        {
            id = 160944,
            score = 11,
            author = "KevinHawkins",
            text = "The area is very densely populated with lvl 10-11 mobs, but should be quite easy to do anyway. You should be able to kill two of them at a time without problems, so just churn your way through them and kill the Ursal. Being a wanderer he is, he doesn't even have to come with an add, which makes him extremely easy to kill.\n\nGood luck.",
            date = "2007-09-30T15:34:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=486#comments:id=160944",
        },
        {
            id = 249023,
            score = 11,
            author = "66648",
            text = "The \"backdoor\" is located directly west of the big glowing pink \"strange fruited plant\", up a narrow ravine you can see on your minimap (squeeze past a tree).\n\nOnce you hop down that gorge, though, you probably won't be able to hop back up, so prepare to hearth or fight your way out. You can pull single mobs fairly easily from here, but the pathfinders are range casters.",
            date = "2008-03-06T12:36:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=486#comments:id=249023",
        },
        {
            id = 1272820,
            score = 11,
            author = "752652",
            text = "Pick up the quest from Sentinal Amara & guards on the cat mounts, patroling the road West of Dolanar. Then follow up the side road now called 'The Cleft' - if you follow the path up dealing with the Gnarlpine Ambushers as you go, follow the path up the rise, then round to the right. at the top of the hill there is a cave, Ursal is just inside.",
            date = "2011-01-02T07:36:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=486#comments:id=1272820",
        },
        {
            id = 1924575,
            score = 10,
            author = "LeaHavoc",
            text = "Path begins at  49, 45, you will see two elves mounted on sabers (one is a quest giver), this is tha path you follow, the cave entrance is at 52, 39.",
            date = "2013-12-08T22:31:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=486#comments:id=1924575",
        },
    },
    [487] = {
        {
            id = 57796,
            score = 6,
            author = "entropicdragon",
            text = "Note that the quest text refers to \"Sentinel Amara Nightwalker\", which is different from the questgiver's name, Moon Priestess Amara. Odd...",
            date = "2007-03-26T23:58:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=487#comments:id=57796",
        },
        {
            id = 526113,
            score = 6,
            author = "bobahop",
            text = "If you plan to be an Herbalist I'd recommend getting it before doing this quest. There is plenty of Silverleaf amongst the Gnarlpines, which is fairly common elsewhere, but there is also Earthroot on top of boulders around them, which I haven't found to be as common. Bring some empty vials and when you find the herbs you can buff yourself with Elixer of Minor Defense (adds 50 armor for 1 hour) and Elixer of Lion's Strength (increases strength by 4 for 1 hour.) Not that you'll necessarily need them, but if you're lower level, they might be nice to have.",
            date = "2008-12-23T05:34:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=487#comments:id=526113",
        },
        {
            id = 1074704,
            score = 2,
            author = "168278",
            text = "Kalimdor Loremaster   +1",
            date = "2010-07-06T17:19:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=487#comments:id=1074704",
        },
        {
            id = 184704,
            score = 1,
            author = "Melris",
            text = "easy done with Druid 9 lvl , the coordinates are correct , it's near to the road leading to Darnassus !",
            date = "2007-11-14T22:54:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=487#comments:id=184704",
        },
        {
            id = 5904773,
            score = 1,
            author = "DaemoniKira",
            text = "In the Dragonflight quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=77201, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=208537 has the player help her conduct a touching ceremony for the new wellspring in the new World Tree, [zone=15105] (located in the Dragon Isles). The player is instructed to choose a single item to contribute as a token of the Night Elves for this ceremony.\n\nAmong the list of potential offerings is \"A smooth stone from the road to Darnassus.\" It would seem this is a reference to the [storyline=568] Storyline quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=487, given by https://www.wowhead.com/npc=2151.\n\nI thought this was a touching tribute, considering the various deep and metaphorical meanings of such a tribute -- a great many people walked this road to Darnassus, and would have walked over this stone, smoothed with time and wear. Unfortunately, it is currently unknown whether https://www.wowhead.com/npc=2151 survived the burning of Teldrassil and the ensuing Battle for Azeroth (according to Wowpedia (https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Moon_Priestess_Amara) and Warcraft Wiki (https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Moon_Priestess_Amara)).",
            date = "2024-07-25T10:22:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=487#comments:id=5904773",
        },
    },
    [488] = {
        {
            id = 207398,
            score = 20,
            author = "entropicdragon",
            text = "I'm surprised nobody's actually mentioned the followup... it's Seek Redemption (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=489), given by either Syral Bladeleaf (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=2083) or Sentinel Kyra Starsong (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=2081), both in Dolanaar.",
            date = "2007-12-26T04:53:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=488#comments:id=207398",
        },
        {
            id = 1613192,
            score = 15,
            author = "Kenyon",
            text = "This quest gives NO REPUTATION GAIN, but it's worth noting that the the followup quest does give a rep gain-- a whopping 500 rep with Darnassas, at that. So do this quest, if only for the rep gain of the one that you can pick up in Dolanaar afterward.\n\n(Working on Ambassador on a level 20 for kicks for the 2nd time, and wish I had done this on my other level 20. 500 rep is a lot of rep to miss out on.)",
            date = "2012-01-18T15:56:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=488#comments:id=1613192",
        },
        {
            id = 1688928,
            score = 6,
            author = "TimeTraveler",
            text = "Don't be fooled by the yellow mark in the mountains, the quest giver is off the road half way between Dolannarr and Sea Breeze Village. No idea why that mark is there except that is is the locarion of a Horde satyr.",
            date = "2012-07-16T20:54:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=488#comments:id=1688928",
        },
        {
            id = 13638,
            score = 3,
            author = "9167",
            text = "You can find Zenn Foulhoof at the coordinates 60, 56.  He is just east of Dolanaar.  There is no reputation gain or loss with this quest, although you become an enemy of Teldrassil until you complete the follow-up quest.",
            date = "2006-12-11T18:33:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=488#comments:id=13638",
        },
        {
            id = 781177,
            score = 3,
            author = "Rainyd",
            text = "Got no reputation as a lvl 6 NE Druid.\n\nBut on the bright side the drop rates for the items of this quest appear to have been significantly increased (or I'm just lucky).\n\nI got a good 85% drop rate I'd say.",
            date = "2009-07-17T16:57:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=488#comments:id=781177",
        },
    },
    [489] = {
        {
            id = 937315,
            score = 47,
            author = "Uinri",
            text = "Ironically, in order to redeem yourself for slaughtering animals, you must go into the forest and collect pine cones next to more dangerous animals that will force you to slaughter them again.",
            date = "2010-01-04T11:18:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=489#comments:id=937315",
        },
        {
            id = 13651,
            score = 20,
            author = "9167",
            text = "You can find the Fel Cones around Zenn Foulhoof or even further around Starbreeze Village.  Try to look around the bases of very large trees.  Some coordinates to try are 58, 55 and 59, 56.",
            date = "2006-12-11T18:45:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=489#comments:id=13651",
        },
        {
