        {
            id = 1224353,
            score = 9,
            author = "84423",
            text = "I was not able to obtain this quest until after finishing Ursal The Mauler (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=486).",
            date = "2010-12-11T10:11:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=997#comments:id=1224353",
        },
        {
            id = 352822,
            score = 1,
            author = "177712",
            text = "If you want to be boringly accurate, exact coordinates are 60.90, 68,50\n\nFollow-up quests are very simple. This one and the following two should only take about 20 minutes to finish if you get a good clear run.",
            date = "2008-08-14T14:21:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=997#comments:id=352822",
        },
        {
            id = 5904727,
            score = 1,
            author = "DaemoniKira",
            text = "In the Dragonflight quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=77201, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=208537 has the player help her conduct a touching ceremony for the new wellspring in the new World Tree, [zone=15105] (located in the Dragon Isles). The player is instructed to choose a single item to contribute as a token of the Night Elves for this ceremony.\n\nAmong the list of potential offerings is \"A sachet of https://www.wowhead.com/item=5391 from Darnassus.\" It would seem this \"sachet of rare earth\" is at least a reference to the \"package of rare earth\" the player must bring to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=2080 in the Night Elf starting quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=997.\n\nI thought this was a really touching tribute, considering https://www.wowhead.com/npc=2080 did not survive the burning of Teldrassil by Sylvanas in the lead-up to Battle for Azeroth.",
            date = "2024-07-25T09:33:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=997#comments:id=5904727",
        },
        {
            id = 11848,
            score = 0,
            author = "8271",
            text = "This quest is a farely simple quest. You deliver a bunch of sand to Denalan. Denalan is directly south of Dolonaar. Then once you past sentinel Kaya (a wounded sentinel). You fall down a cliff. Then you head to the lake and head left then you will find a hut by Lake Al'Ameth.",
            date = "2006-12-08T23:14:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=997#comments:id=11848",
        },
    },
    [998] = {
        {
            id = 287390,
            score = 8,
            author = "GoGoGodzilla",
            text = "Cleansing one of these will make it into a Cleansed Windblossom (http://www.wowhead.com/?object=164884) which you can loot to receive  Windblossom Berries (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=11950).",
            date = "2008-05-13T14:06:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=998#comments:id=287390",
        },
        {
            id = 1626316,
            score = 3,
            author = "Rhynchelma",
            text = "This quest is no longer in game as far as I can see.",
            date = "2012-02-14T11:41:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=998#comments:id=1626316",
        },
        {
            id = 1110563,
            score = 2,
            author = "611130",
            text = "The zone of Felwood (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=361) has a series of repeatable quests that begin with the quests  Cleansing Felwood (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4101) and at least one of the follow up repeatable turn in quests (for the salve):\nSalve via Skinning (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4106), Salve via Disenchanting (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4107),  Salve via hunting (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4108), Salve via Mining (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4109), and Salve via Gathering (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4110).\n\nOnce you have some Cenarion Plant Salve (http://www.wowhead.com/item=11516) you can do the quests:\n Corrupted Songflower (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=2523) which leads to Cleansed Songflower (http://www.wowhead.com/object=164882) which gives Songflower Serenade (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=15366)\nCorrupted Night Dragon (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4119) which leads to Cleansed Night Dragon (http://www.wowhead.com/object=164881) which gives Night Dragon's Breath (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=11952#c0z)\nCorrupted Whipper Root (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=4117) which leads to  Cleansed Whipper Root (http://www.wowhead.com/object=164883) which gives you Whipper Root Tuber (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=11951)\nCorrupted WIndblossom (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=998) which leads to Cleansed Windblossom (http://www.wowhead.com/?object=164884) which gives Windblossom Berries (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=11950)\n\nIt is worth mentioning that when cleansed the plants will stay that way for something like 2 hours. Their quests can only be completed like every 10-15 minutes though.\nThis means you can get these buffs/items pretty consistently  for 16 levels (the starter quest can be accepted at level 48, and the buffs continue to give the buff through 63) as long as you aren't dying very frequently and you actually do enough quests in felwood to keep your cenarion salve in stock (don't throw away any corrupted soul shards)\n\nA lot of other Vanilla unique buffs seem to be unavailable after 63 as well ( Fengus' Ferocity  (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=22817), Mol'dar's Moxie (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=22818) , Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=22888),  Slip'kik's Savvy (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=22820), and Spirit of Zandalar (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=24425)), seems that's when they want you to give up on azeroth buffs.",
            date = "2010-08-29T19:22:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=998#comments:id=1110563",
        },
    },
    [1036] = {
        {
            id = 1218082,
            score = 94,
            author = "wpgbubba",
            text = "\"Good-Boy\" Bruce, a worgen, at 41,61 in Sothern Stranglethorn vale (the bloodsail camp at the end of the path just north of Booty Bay tunnel by a crate) now gives the quest. The dialog is the same.",
