        {
            id = 390055,
            score = 1,
            author = "45715",
            text = "As of 28. of September, 2008 it is commonly known that there indeed WILL be a Wrath of the Lich King collector's edition(which I myself happen to have pre-ordered :D)\nIt will contain a book of artwork from WotLK like every collector's edition before it, a soundtrack CD and Behind the Scenes DVD, again nothing new.\nAnd yet another of Blizzard's stunning and creative surprises is even more WoW TCG cards. Oh the creativity.\nIt was creative in TBC, but now it seems like they are all out of ideas; yet another mousepad with a map on it..\nWhat would truly have been awesome would've been a plastic \"ice glacier\" with the Northrend map on it. But I guess that is just dreaming. (To clear confusion: This is my suggestion alone, as far as I have read this has NEVER been discussed and never was the idea.)\nNow, what I bet you are all waiting for in my flow of useless information: The new minipet shall be Frosty, the Baby Frostwyrm.",
