    [5943] = {
        {
            id = 437183,
            score = 43,
            author = "11375",
            text = "This quest DOES count as Kalimdor Loremaster! Was my last one :P",
            date = "2008-11-10T06:14:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5943#comments:id=437183",
        },
        {
            id = 1763965,
            score = 26,
            author = "1038935",
            text = "[spoiler]TL;DR: 2 Que (quest=5943)-sts (quest=5821) gone for good, 2 Ven (npc=12245)-dors (npc=12246) MIA, 3 re (item=3734)-ci (item=5489)-pes (item=12227) currently unobtainable,\nand a touching letter from Game Master Evinderminus regarding Cork (npc=11625), Rigger (npc=11626), & the Kodos (npc=11564).\nAnd Auction House Statistics for the recipes are now at the end of the comment.\nPS - I intend to re-update when the recipes are once again available in-game.\n(Updated: 2013/03/01)[/spoiler]\n_________________________\nSapperwix [Quality Assurance]: [referring to https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5943]\n\"This quest and its related NPCs have been removed from the game.\"\n[Bug]Gizelton Caravan (page 2) - Forums - World of Warcraft*\n(*Now a 404 error. \"There was a PAGE here. It’s gone now. (http://us.battle.net/wow/en/forum/topic/5592458834?page=2)\")\n\nThis effectively also removes https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5821.\n\nFaid:\n\"...currently impacted are:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=12246 which is the only source for\nRecipe: Big Bear Steak (item=3734)\nRecipe: Lean Wolf Steak (item=12227)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=12245, the only source of\nRecipe: Lean Venison (item=5489)\"\nClockwork Riot: Recipe Vendor MIA - Some recipes no longer obtainable! (http://www.clockworkriot.com/2012/09/recipe-vendor-mia-some-recipes-no.html)\n\nEgdod:\n\"I spoke today, 10/1/12, with a GM who said that hope may not be lost for those of us looking to get our hands on the missing recipes sold by the Desolace/Gizelton Caravan vendors.\n\nThe GM could not offer a time frame for the fix, but did refer to this as bug, and said the following:\n\n\"Part of the caravan was intentionally removed. Those two [https://www.wowhead.com/npc=12246 and https://www.wowhead.com/npc=12245] weren't supposed to be so it is something we are looking in to.\"\n\nEnigmatic, I know, but it does suggest that these vendors may reappear with recipes intact.\"\n[Bug]Gizelton Caravan (page 2) - Forums - World of Warcraft*\n(*Now a 404 error. \"There was a PAGE here. It’s gone now. (http://us.battle.net/wow/en/forum/topic/5592458834?page=2)\")\nPS - I will edit this post as soon as I learn more. *fingers crossed that the bots come back*\n\nUpdated (2012/11/18):Noshika (npc=12245#comments:id=1752164):\n\"It looks like this has been removed from the game. I received a GM confirmation.\n\nHail and well met, Noshi!\n\nA thousand apologies for not being able to speak with you in-game, friend. It's been a little crazy since we imported all of these Pandaren Monks into the office and they started chewing up all of our computer cords. :< Evinderminus, here! I just wanted to drop by and leave a little information concerning the Desolace Caravan NPCs.\n\nOver time, the World of Warcraft changes. It was seen with the Shattering of the Cataclysm, and every major world event before. When such things happen, sometimes NPCs move on. This is the case with the NPCs you're looking for, sadly. They have gone to seek their fortune elsewhere, perhaps far beyond the oceans, away from this war-torn world. That you remember them is touching, however, and I will be sure to inform the Gizelton boys that you send your regards. We hope that you'll find other items in the world that are equally interesting, perhaps that remind you of these NPCs.\n\nI sincerely hope that this experience with Blizzard Entertainment has been helpful! May you continue to enjoy your stay in our world!\n\nBe well, strike true, and may your lewt be phat!\n\nGame Master Evinderminus\nCustomer Services\nBlizzard Entertainment\nwww.blizzard.com/support (http://www.blizzard.com/support)\"\n\nA.H. Statistics*\n*Prices and Percentages are hyperlinked to show the corresponding items' tooltips.\nUndermineJournal (http://theunderminejournal.com) Market Prices are:\n02 Dec . 23 Dec . 05 Jan . . 12 Feb . . 24 Feb . . 01 Mar\n323G . . . 602G . . 324G . . . 727G . . . 498G . . . . 646G (item=3734),\n777G . . . 969G . . 932G . . 1,461G . . 1,747G . . 1,121G (item=12227),\n798G . . 1,047G. . 944G . . 1,239G . . 1,486G . . 1,950G (item=5489).\n\nOverall Realm Availability (%)\n02 Dec . 23 Dec . 05 Jan . . 12 Feb . . 24 Feb . . 01 Mar\n6.22% . . 4.30% . . 6.45% . . 4.98% . . . 5.27% . . 4.79% (item=3734),\n3.13% . . 2.15% . . 2.54% . . 1.66% . . . 2.05% . . 1.56% (item=12227),\n3.12% . . 3.13% . . 4.20% . . 3.03% . . . 2.44% . . 2.54% (item=5489).\n\nUS Realm Availability (%)\n02 Dec . 23 Dec . 05 Jan . . 12 Feb . . 24 Feb . . 01 Mar\nNo Data . . 5.89% . . 8.33% . . 6.91% . . . 6.91% . . 5.89% (item=3734),\nNo Data . . 2.44% . . 2.24% . . 1.22% . . . 2.03% . . 1.63% (item=12227),\nNo Data . . 4.67% . . 5.49% . . 3.25% . . . 3.05% . . 3.05% (item=5489).\n\nPPPS - Still waiting to hear about the recipes. Will update soon.\nEdit (2012/11/24): added \"tl;dr\" & added wowhead links to Faid & Egdod quotes.\nEdit (2012/12/02): added A.H. Statistics.\nEdit (2012/12/25 - 2013/03/01): Updated Market Info. Still looking for news about the availability of these recipes.",
            date = "2012-11-17T21:10:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5943#comments:id=1763965",
        },
        {
            id = 232550,
            score = 25,
            author = "126358",
            text = "This is the second of two quests on the caravan trade route between Kormek's Hut and the Gelkis Village. It is also the harder of the two. After returning to the Gelkis Village, the caravan sets up shop and rests for 10 minutes. Then it departs headed east along the road and stops just outside the entrance to Mannoroc Coven. At this point the quest becomes available for only 4 minutes. If it is not recieved within that period, the caravan continues east along the road and then north past the Kolkar Village and finally west to Kormek's Hut. You have to then wait for the caravan to complete it's circut before you can pick up the quest (which takes approx. 40-60 minutes! depending on the quests being picked up or not along the way)\n\nFor the quest, you are attacked by three seperate mobs as you pass through Mannoroc Coven heading east. All three mobs spawn the same units and they are as follows :\n\n1 Lesser Infernal (level 36-37)\n1 Doomwarder (level 37-38)\n1 Nether Sorceress (level 39-40)\n\nAfter the third mob is defeated, the quest objective is completed and you can head directly to Scrabblescrew's Camp to recieve your reward.",
            date = "2008-02-10T04:30:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5943#comments:id=232550",
        },
        {
            id = 125338,
            score = 15,
            author = "Cross88",
            text = "When the quest becomes available he will yell his location and ask for assistance.\n\nReminded me a lot of a player when he did that. :)",
            date = "2007-07-23T05:30:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5943#comments:id=125338",
        },
        {
            id = 1072208,
            score = 12,
            author = "423524",
            text = "I waited for the caravan to perform its entire travel route twice on a day that I was very bored. Both times the times of departure and arrival were very close within 1 or 2 minutes, I’m pretty sure you will have success at finding the caravan if you attempt at the times I have posted.\n\nThe Caravan stops in 2 main locations in Desolace. There is a Northern location and a Southern location. There are also 2 different brief stopping locations where 2 separate quests are given.\n\nThe quests are escort quests and will be somewhat difficult if they are done at the levels they are meant for.\n\nNorthern Stopping Location:\n\nThe northern stopping location of the caravan is a bit north of KORMEK'S HUT.\n\nKormek's Hut stopping location exact coordinates are:\n\n60.29, 38.12 (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=405:603381)\n\n(For me both times) The approximate time that it arrived for me was 55 minutes after the hour through the exact hour mark (xx:55 - xx:00).\n\nThe caravan waited at the Kormek's Hut location for approximately 10-12 minutes from the time that it arrived and started leaving on the southern bound route approximately 5-7 minutes after the hour mark (xx:05 – xx:07).\n\nQuest Location #1\n\nThe [Bodyguard for Hire] quest is given by Cork Gizelton at the exact coordinates of:\n\n66.48, 37.55 (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=405:665375)\n\n(For me both times) The caravan arrived at this location approximately 9-12 minutes after the hour. (xx:09-xx:12)\n\nThe Southern Location:\n\nThe Southern Caravan stopping point is just a bit southeast of where the roads cross near the southern entrance to the area. The coordinates are:\n\n40.45, 79.32 (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=405:404793)\n\n(For me both times) The approximate time that the caravan arrived at this location was 25-28 minutes after the hour. (xx:25-xx:28)\n\n(For me both times) The time the caravan left on northern bound route approximately 34-35 minutes after the hour. (xx:34-xx:35)\n\nQuest Location #2\n\nthe [Gizelton Caravan] quest is given by Rigger Gizelton at the exact coordinates of:\n\n45.42, 75.40 (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=405:454754)\n\n(For me both times) Caravan arrived at this location approximately 36-38 minutes after the hour. (xx:36-xx:38)\n\nJust some helpful suggestions:\n\n1.  At the main stopping locations North and South there are little robots that spawn while the caravan is there. They sale some decent cooking recipes and even a few scrolls.\n\n2.  If you already have the recipes learned and have extra inventory space buy up all the cooking recipes that you can while you’re there, it’s easily worth it. They will sale on AH for nearly 10x their cost without fail. Some of them sale for 20-30x the robots price.\n\n3.  Please for the love! People who complain about the coordinates and just want a URL, go get the curse client and get a coordinates addon like mapster or go get the Tomtom addon and stop whining! It’s 50 quadrillion,billion,zillion times better! That’s not even saying for all the other addons that you will be able to get and will eventually need if you ever want to run raids!\n\n4.  Also since I know there are so many skeptics out there about getting a virus or keylogger from these addons, I want you to know I’ve been using them since the day I was on my 10-day trial run of WoW over 3 years ago. I’ve never had a virus, keylogger, worm or whatever you want to call it from any of these programs THEY’RE 100% safe to use! I use two very reputable virus/malware scanning programs and they have never found a problem with any of the WoW addon programs I have installed. So if it’s hard to find anything with the information I provided then blame yourself for not getting an in-game coordinates addon like tomtom.",
            date = "2010-07-03T16:08:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5943#comments:id=1072208",
        },
    },
