    [9397] = {
        {
            id = 21395,
            score = 40,
            author = "dJe781",
            text = "You can find the spot at (29,81) in Hellfire Peninsula. Don't forget to open up the nets next to the little house to make the Female Kaliri Hatchling pop.",
            date = "2007-01-18T14:40:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9397#comments:id=21395",
        },
        {
            id = 62434,
            score = 17,
            author = "Fixit",
            text = "As you stand around 26,62, in front of the Den of Haal'esh, looking south at four Haal'eshi Talonguards patrolling the entrance, you are probably wondering whether you have to fight through the bird-creatures, all the way down into their chasm and then all the way back up to get to the nests at the end around 28,79 (or so).\n\nYou don't. That's the sucker's way!\n\nFirst of all, check around the entrance for small nests. I found one guarded only by two owls (actual birds, not humanoids), at 25,71, just to the west and above the entrance. It only had a male bird so it didn't complete my quest but you might get luckier. It was also gone 20 minutes later when I checked but it might be there for you, give it a look. And keep your eyes open as you go, for the small nests with the tiny red glow at the center.\n\nThe fast way to get to the final hut at 28,79 is to go around the chasm. Look to the east of those four Haal'eshi Talonguards patrolling the entrance. Up on the rocks there's another Talonguard. At level 60 I was easily able to walk past the four ground-level guards and kill the guy on the rocks. By then riding on the rocks, to the east of the chasm, I made it all the way to around 30,78 without aggroing another mob.\n\nFrom there I just had to kill about 4 casters to get to the little hut with the two nests, one of which had my female.\n\nThis quest goes well with Magic of the Arakkoa (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9396) and, since you're going east around the birdmen anyway, The Great Fissure (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9340).",
            date = "2007-04-05T08:26:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9397#comments:id=62434",
        },
        {
            id = 419990,
            score = 8,
            author = "163895",
            text = "I opened approximately eighty, yes, eighty of these nests. I spent about 2 1/2 hours opening nests, and got over 100k exp from just killing the birds and other monsters around the area. This is officially the stupidest, most frustrating quest I have ever done. I never did get the female hatchling...",
            date = "2008-10-25T19:21:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9397#comments:id=419990",
        },
        {
            id = 175853,
            score = 7,
            author = "27676",
            text = "Along the top there is also a mob named Avruu - http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=17084\n\nHe drops a quest item. Might as well do this while you're here too.\n\nHe has a very quick respawn time so you can't miss him.",
            date = "2007-10-28T02:51:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9397#comments:id=175853",
        },
        {
            id = 168864,
            score = 6,
            author = "93672",
            text = "when you go to do this quest, make sure you do at the same time this one : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9396",
            date = "2007-10-15T04:25:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9397#comments:id=168864",
        },
    },
    [9398] = {
        {
            id = 110052,
            score = 14,
            author = "50009",
            text = "I found a bunch of Alphas at 40.73 through 37.69 just West of Gor' gaz outpost.  Make sure to hug the walls of the mountain.",
            date = "2007-06-23T21:22:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9398#comments:id=110052",
        },
        {
            id = 18075,
            score = 7,
            author = "Lustral",
            text = "Both the Alphas and Whelps can be found in their greatest quantity east of Falcon Watch within the Great Fissure.\n\nBeware of the the Crust Burster variants there.  They're easy to aggro while killing Stonescythe's, and they reburrow periodically, sometimes leading to more adds.",
            date = "2006-12-27T09:13:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9398#comments:id=18075",
        },
        {
            id = 237856,
            score = 4,
            author = "101789",
            text = "Tip: When fighting the both the Alpha's and the whelps and you get the \"Stonescythe Alpha (or whelp) defends himself in desperation\" notification, stop attacking until until the \"Desperate Defense\" buff goes away, otherwise they get \"Desperate Rage\", which is an enrage that stacks up to 5 times and increases their damage by 10 and their attack speed by 5% per application and this can stack up to 5 times, so it quickly raises their damage by 50 and attack speed by 25% if you aren't paying attention.",
            date = "2008-02-17T06:11:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9398#comments:id=237856",
        },
        {
            id = 210112,
            score = 3,
            author = "53607",
            text = "BTW here in this fissure is where you do the group quest called The Rock Flayer Matriarch. It is the cave in the fissure at 34,62.",
            date = "2007-12-30T21:28:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9398#comments:id=210112",
        },
        {
            id = 21344,
            score = 2,
            author = "Amberley",
            text = "Within the fissure, there are small hills, and rocks potruding from the salt bed. It appeared to me, that the Whelps spawn near the rocky potrusions, and the alphas on top of the hills.\n\nAlso, in the cave with Blacktalon, alpha's spawn.",
            date = "2007-01-18T12:08:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9398#comments:id=21344",
        },
    },
    [9399] = {
        {
            id = 17442,
            score = 36,
            author = "7344",
            text = "The taskmasters can be found at Cenarion Post (15, 54).\n\nEach Taskmaster (lvl 63) has between 2 and 3 Dreghood Brutes with him. When you attack the Taskmaster they will help him fight you. Don't kill these guys, there being forced to attack you, as soon as the Taskmaster is dead they are free.",
            date = "2006-12-19T16:38:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9399#comments:id=17442",
        },
        {
            id = 77976,
            score = 12,
            author = "48842",
            text = "Focus all your attack on the Taskmaster. The Dreghood Brutes do only trivial damage and will stop attacking after the Taskmaster falls. Infact they will attack another Taskmaster when freed if one is closeby.",
            date = "2007-05-05T01:29:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9399#comments:id=77976",
        },
        {
            id = 105240,
            score = 7,
            author = "entropicdragon",
            text = "If you pull two taskmasters simultaneously, all of the adds of both of them will despawn immediately after the first one is killed.",
            date = "2007-06-16T02:57:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9399#comments:id=105240",
        },
        {
            id = 241814,
            score = 4,
            author = "Salvito",
            text = "While you are there, at 15,58 is \"Naladu\" http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10403   1st  of a 4 parter series.\nOh, watch out for the elite which patrols the area.",
            date = "2008-02-23T05:22:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9399#comments:id=241814",
        },
        {
            id = 748734,
            score = 4,
            author = "380599",
            text = "After you kill the taskmasters the 63's attacking you will turn into a regular worker that will not attack you. Finished this quest in less then a minute @ level 62.\n\nEasy quest. Just kill the mob fast and you will be fine",
            date = "2009-06-16T23:15:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9399#comments:id=748734",
        },
    },
    [9400] = {
        {
            id = 566453,
            score = 210,
            author = "123744",
            text = "I originally posted this under the Rep page and under the final quest page but I thought it would be appropriate for the up and comers to see what they have to look forward to.  This is easily the best quest chain in the entire game.  Have fun doing it.  I've done it 3 times now and a 4th pretty soon.  Please rate me up, this took a long time to compile and code,  Thanks.\n\nThis Quest Chain starts in Hellfire with The Assassin.   This requires you are able to speak to Nazgrel (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3230) which means you will have to have done at least some of the level 58 outland Quests*.\n\n1. The Assassin (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9400)\n2. A Strange Weapon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9401)\n3. The Warchief's Mandate (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9405)\n4. A Spirit Guide (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9410)\n5. The Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9406)\n6. Messenger to Thrall (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9438)\n7. Envoy to the Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9441)\n\nAlso given at this point are the following, but may not be necessary to complete the Hero chain.  They are very nice rep rewards for each so you may want to do them since you’re there anyway.\n\0091. A Debilitating Sickness (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9442)\n2. Administering the Salve (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9447)\n\nThe next part leads you to Jorin Dead Eye  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18106) in Garadar, Nagrand.\n\n1. The Impotent Leader (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9888)\n2. Don't Kill the Fat One (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9889)\n3. Success! (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9890)\n4. Because Kilrath is a Coward (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9891)\n5. Message in a Battle (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9906)\n6. An Audacious Advance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9907)\n7. Diplomatic Measures (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10107)\n\nTakes you to Nagrand to Find Lantresor of the Blade  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18261) which gives you the Blademaster Chain\n\n1a. Armaments for Deception (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9928)\n1b. Ruthless Cunning (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9927)\n2a. Returning the Favor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9931)\n2b. Body Of Evidence (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9932)\n3.   Message to Garadar (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9934)\n\nYou will also need to complete The following Unrelated Quests.\n1. The Totem of Kar’dash  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9868)\n\nwhich is a simple escort quest beginning with the Mag'har Captive (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18210) in one of the buildings of Sunspring Post.\n\nThe second part involves Altruis the Sufferer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18417) who is right by the Mag’har captive so these are good quests to do together.\n\n1. Survey the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9991)\n2. Buying Time (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9999)\n3. The Master Planner (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10001)\n4. Patience and Understanding (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10004)\n5. Crackin' Some Skulls (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10009)\n6. It's Just That Easy? (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10010)\n7. Forge Camp: Annihilated (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10011)\n\nThis unlocks the final sequence which returns you to Garrosh  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18063).  He sends you finally to visit Greatmother Geyah  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18141).\n\n1. A Visit With the Greatmother (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10044)\n2. Material Components (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10045)\n3. To Meet Mother Kashur (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10081)\n4. The Agitated Ancestors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10082)\n5. A Visit With The Ancestors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10085)\n6. When Spirits Speak (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10101)\n7. A Secret Revealed (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10102)\n8. Auchindoun... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10167)\n9. What the Soul Sees (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10168)\n10. Return to the Greatmother (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10170)\n11. The Inconsolable Chieftain (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10171)\n12. There Is No Hope (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10172)\n13. Thrall, Son of Durotan (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10175)\n14. Hero of the Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10212)\n\nCongrats on you Uber new Gear and Exalted Rep.\n\nSmall disclaimer.  This is a compilation from a lot of peoples work using information from Allakazam (http://wow.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?source=live;wquest=10212), Wowhead  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10212), WoWWiki  (http://www.wowwiki.com/Geyah), and the Armory  (http://www.wowarmory.com/item-info.xml?i=28175).  This took many hours to complete since the info was so scattered so please rate me up if possible.\n\nRaimi, 70 Undead Warlock,\nTitianna 70 Belf Priest\nHeghbathl 70 Belf Tankadin\nSentinals\n*\n1. Through the Dark Portal  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9407)\n2. Arrival in Outland  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10120)\n3. Journey to Thrallmar  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10289)\n4. Report to Nazgrel  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10291)\n5. Eradicate the Burning Legion  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10121)\n6. Felspark Ravine  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10123)\n7. Forward Base: Reaver's Fall  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10124)\n8. Disrupt Their Reinforcements (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10208)\n9. Mission: Gateways Murketh and Shaadraz (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10129)\n10. Mission: The Abyssal Shelf  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10162)",
            date = "2009-01-17T10:51:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9400#comments:id=566453",
        },
        {
            id = 1429384,
            score = 116,
            author = "Monoxiety",
            text = "You must first complete the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10124 in order to start https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9400. Confirmed.",
            date = "2011-05-28T13:18:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9400#comments:id=1429384",
        },
        {
            id = 12719,
            score = 58,
            author = "Sware",
            text = "The quest coined as \"Mankirk in Outlands\", where you find the dead body of an assassin with the name \"Fel Orc Corpse\".\n\nTo find the corpse, go the top road leading out of Thrallmar and follow the path that goes past the Pools of Aggonar. Keep going past the pools and when you reach a wooden-spike barricade go past it and turn to your right around the corner should be the dead orc corpse.\n\nPosting screenshots soon.",
            date = "2006-12-10T11:47:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9400#comments:id=12719",
        },
        {
            id = 20888,
            score = 42,
            author = "10501",
            text = "33, 43 according to a friend.",
            date = "2007-01-16T20:05:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9400#comments:id=20888",
        },
        {
            id = 153684,
            score = 31,
            author = "45196",
            text = "If you want to skip thrallmar's quests in order to complete them only when you'll be honored, you have to do this chain anyway, 'cause you will need mag'har reputation when you'll go to nagrand (starting mag'har reputation is unfriendly, so you wont be able to talk to npcs). To unlock this chain, you have to do this other one till u reach point 9 (first bombing mission):\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9407\nCompleting the 9th step will give u access to this quest:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10388\nNow go back to Nazgrel: Tha assassin chain will be active. Dont waste rep on other quests/chains.",
            date = "2007-09-16T08:25:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9400#comments:id=153684",
        },
    },
