    [9726] = {
        {
            id = 9469,
            score = 43,
            author = "8199",
            text = "A Quick notes to new Feral Druids: You must have Friendly(?) rep with Sporregar in order to even get this quest. Kill Bog Lords in the Dead Mire and keep all the tendrils(http://www.wowhead.com/?item=24291) for rep. You'll also be getting Unidentified Plant Parts(http://www.wowhead.com/?item=24401) which you should definately keep for cenarion expidition reputation which you will want to get revered with.(Rep Rewards: http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=17904)\n\nThe next quest, The Ring of Blood(http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9977) You'll need a good group of five. Usually groups are willing to help one another to make it easier. Yields the Staff of Beasts.\n\nThe final quest reward staff is from a quest chain. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10408 At that URL you'll find the end quest which once again is elite and quite difficult. Yields Fleshling Simulation Staff. Each staff should be enough to tide you over for a few levels.",
            date = "2006-12-07T19:37:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9726#comments:id=9469",
        },
        {
            id = 10114,
            score = 27,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Confrimed, must have friendly with Sporeggar.  All mobs are located near the pump at Marshlight Lake(bloodscale enclave).",
            date = "2006-12-07T22:56:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9726#comments:id=10114",
        },
        {
            id = 30038,
            score = 23,
            author = "17137",
            text = "i found a lot of slavedrivers and enchantress at 25.36.\nenchantress's are at underwater too..",
            date = "2007-02-03T12:38:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9726#comments:id=30038",
        },
        {
            id = 34606,
            score = 17,
            author = "Kathucka",
            text = "This quest is much easier while in a group, as you'll be prone to getting multiple naga attacking you.  Also, as the goal here is simply to kill a certain number of naga, it goes much more quickly in a group.\n\nWatch out for the water elemental sentries.  If left alone too long after spotting you, they'll call for help over a wide area.  You can get six naga attacking you at the same time if that happens.  Fortunately, the sentries have low health, so they can be killed quickly.\n\nThe female naga (Enchantresses) are much less common than the male ones.  Seek them out first.  They channel arcane missiles, which can be interrupted.  Watch out for their \"Circle of Ice\" spell.  It gradually forms a ring of ice blocks on the ground around you.  If you're in the middle of the ring when it completes, it hits for huge damage and roots you in place.  Just move out of the way when you see the ice blocks.\n\nThe male naga (Slavedrivers) will call nearby slaves for help.  If you kill the naga, the slave will evade and run back to its spawn point.",
            date = "2007-02-12T10:14:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9726#comments:id=34606",
        },
        {
