        },
        {
            id = 23096,
            score = 103,
            author = "14360",
            text = "This is a repeatable quest from friendly to exhalted.",
            date = "2007-01-23T05:34:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9727#comments:id=23096",
        },
        {
            id = 646990,
            score = 44,
            author = "309394",
            text = "As I suspected, this does not count toward Mysteries of the Marsh (http://www.wowhead.com/?achievement=1190).",
            date = "2009-03-18T14:44:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9727#comments:id=646990",
        },
        {
            id = 104244,
            score = 39,
            author = "ziggymac",
            text = "You guys are missing the important part when comparing.\n\nFertile Spores can be gathered without being on a quest, and therefore stockpiled.\n\nThe naga only count for 12 of each at a time before you have to run back and turn in.\n\nFertile Spores are by far faster for rep gain. And you can exp grind on them, too, if you find a high-density Sporebat population.",
            date = "2007-06-14T11:10:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9727#comments:id=104244",
        },
        {
            id = 259499,
            score = 33,
            author = "45375",
            text = "I think this changed with 2.4\nPrior to 2.4 it was 12 Enchantresses and now it is only 6.",
            date = "2008-03-25T18:05:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9727#comments:id=259499",
        },
    },
    [9728] = {
        {
            id = 21894,
            score = 33,
            author = "11505",
            text = "It is a 100% drop rate. Carefull with the draenei looking guys, the nagas \"call\" them far away for help. However once the naga dies they reset if they got called far from their inicial spawn point.",
            date = "2007-01-20T03:35:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9728#comments:id=21894",
        },
        {
            id = 21691,
            score = 23,
            author = "12977",
            text = "Around 62, 68 on Nagas.",
            date = "2007-01-19T17:33:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9728#comments:id=21691",
        },
        {
            id = 8214,
            score = 14,
            author = "6934",
            text = "These can be collected from all Naga in the zone.  Suggest pairing this with the elite Wanted quests or Balance Must Be Preserved (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9720 )",
            date = "2006-12-07T03:14:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9728#comments:id=8214",
        },
        {
            id = 155751,
            score = 12,
            author = "dairylee",
            text = "Possibly one of the hardest quests I've done since I travelled to the outlands. I did it solo with a level 61 Shadow Priest, killing the Naga's wasn't a problem but isolating them and making sure I didn't attract more than one at a time was the hard part. Good job they had a 100% Drop Rate.\n\nI went to 62,68 and stayed on the outside of the camps patrolling the shallow water looking for lone Naga's I could pull. If the Naga called a minion to help him I just concentrated on the Naga and as soon as he died the minion would vanish.",
            date = "2007-09-20T15:43:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9728#comments:id=155751",
        },
        {
            id = 387385,
            score = 7,
            author = "Prokos",
            text = "Since this doesn't have a followup, you can just ignore it and you'll probably have it finished when you've done the other quests.",
            date = "2008-09-25T06:00:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9728#comments:id=387385",
        },
    },
    [9729] = {
        {
            id = 1825169,
            score = 67,
            author = "Furglelover",
            text = "This is unquestionably the longest escort quest in the entire game. While you can combine it with the repeatable quest Now That We're Still Friends, which also involves killing Naga, it takes so long it really isn't worth it. I am convinced it has been lengthened since the last time I levelled a character through Zangramarsh years ago. While It does give rep for Sporregar, it is not part of a chain, from a purely time management perspective or power levelling you'd be much better off just grinding through Coilfang Reservoir dungeons to gain rep with them. In addition, picking up five Sanguine Hibiscus in Underbog grants 250 rep with them when turned in for the repeatable quest Bring Me Another Shrubbery!",
            date = "2013-03-09T07:06:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9729#comments:id=1825169",
        },
        {
            id = 56345,
            score = 50,
            author = "33684",
            text = "These items are are excellent if you're below, say, 64.\n64-67, they're decent.\n68+ they're D/E or vendor food.\n\nBlizzard either needs to lower the rep requirement to honored or at the very least, revered, or buff the items significantly.\n\nIt's unfair to force players to farm Sporeggar rep pre-70, putting their leveling to a grinding halt, or give them sub-par items at 70.",
            date = "2007-03-24T11:42:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9729#comments:id=56345",
        },
        {
            id = 1595335,
            score = 42,
            author = "916943",
            text = "As of patch 4.3 I can confirm this is quest is available upon honored reputation instead of exalted!",
            date = "2011-12-13T06:18:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9729#comments:id=1595335",
        },
        {
            id = 472393,
            score = 21,
            author = "201933",
            text = "Reference to The Hulk. Hulk smash!",
            date = "2008-11-26T18:38:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9729#comments:id=472393",
        },
        {
            id = 1048205,
            score = 19,
            author = "Kabookiejoe",
            text = "counts towards mysteries of zangarmarash",
            date = "2010-05-29T09:55:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9729#comments:id=1048205",
        },
    },
    [9730] = {
        {
            id = 21101,
            score = 62,
            author = "4247",
            text = "Coords: 65, 68",
            date = "2007-01-17T17:12:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9730#comments:id=21101",
        },
        {
            id = 27201,
            score = 25,
            author = "4786",
            text = "He's immune to fear, I learned that the hard way.",
            date = "2007-01-29T14:34:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9730#comments:id=27201",
        },
        {
            id = 297691,
            score = 6,
            author = "128231",
            text = "Solo'd as a level 63 BM Hunter, and I found him to be slightly easier than his Bloodscale counterpart.  Here's how I did it.\n\nFirst, I cleared a small area to make sure I could back up and move around a little if I needed to.  I pulled with an Auto Shot and when I had him in the clear, I sent my Cat in.\n\nI popped Beastial Wrath, Mend Pet and let her Growl twice for some aggro.  Then, popped my trinket and started an Auto Shot/Steady Shot weave keeping Mend Pet active AT ALL TIMES.  Mend Pet easily outhealed the damage done until he switched to his polearm.  Then things got a bit iffy because he started hitting harder than the Mend Pet could heal.  But thanks to my Cat, I was able to get him down to about 15% before my Cat died.  Since I was at max range (and the Naga is immune to Concussion Shot) I started a small kiting method getting off a final Steady Shot, then weaving Serpent Sting and Arcane Shot.  Didn't take long at 15% to kill him.  Solo'd the two Nagas, turned in and earned a good 25,000 experience.  Not too shabby.\n\nHere's my Cats' stats in case someone is curious:\n\nLevel 62, Loyalty Level 6 Cat\nGrowl Rank 7\nBite Rank 8\nClaw Rank 8\nDash Rank 3\nCobra Reflexes\nAvoidance Rank 2\nNatural Armor Rank 8\nGreat Stamina Rank 3\nRank 2 of all 5 Schools of Magic\n\nHope this info helps someone!",
            date = "2008-05-31T15:31:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9730#comments:id=297691",
        },
        {
            id = 219347,
            score = 4,
            author = "shexna",
            text = "64 Feral druid soloed it. not 100% easy, but very doable, no pots or other buff used.\ni went bear. when i got low on health (35%) i bashed and healed, back in bear, when i got to 35% again i used frenzied regeneration, at 35% third time, bash was ready again, and after that he died.\n\nbe carefull, he does a knockback, only did it once in my fight, pushed me 15yard or so.\n\nin bear he hitted for 250 or so, in cat he hitted for around 550.",
            date = "2008-01-16T20:23:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9730#comments:id=219347",
        },
        {
            id = 293274,
            score = 4,
            author = "140992",
            text = "yeah... i got handled as a 63 elemental shaman.  needed a 70 hunter to help me out",
            date = "2008-05-23T14:54:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9730#comments:id=293274",
        },
    },
    [9731] = {
        {
            id = 8193,
            score = 92,
            author = "6934",
            text = "All you need to do is swim to the entrance to Coilfang Reservoir - tloc 50, 40(swim down about 100 feet).  Quest rewards are excellent, especially for the amount of effort required.",
            date = "2006-12-07T02:31:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9731#comments:id=8193",
        },
        {
            id = 1495137,
            score = 37,
            author = "potatoe",
            text = "quoting http://www.wowhead.com/item=24330#comments:id=16553:reply=110508\n\nNote that you need to be on the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9720 before it will drop. It is a followup from https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9716 available from the NPC https://www.wowhead.com/npc=17841 at level 61.\nEven though the questitem says only level 59 is required, you still need a quest which is level 61 minimum.",
            date = "2011-08-14T19:46:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9731#comments:id=1495137",
        },
        {
            id = 1877932,
            score = 19,
            author = "846285",
            text = "After reading most of the comments I thought I couldent get the quest item anymore sense I had already completed the quest they say is required to get the item to drop. But while I was doing a Sporeggar quest I pulled a bunch of mobs and killed them. The schematic dropped but not off an overseer ( I have previously finished the Pump quest). I dont know what to make of it. Mine dropped off a Naga Enchantress North of Sporregar.",
            date = "2013-07-17T16:00:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9731#comments:id=1877932",
        },
        {
            id = 962476,
            score = 16,
            author = "Kizrak",
            text = "This quest requires level 61 to complete, despite the shown required level of 59. This is because in order for the drain Schematics to drop, you have to be on a quest that requires you to be 61.\n\nFound this out as I was trying to get the ring for my 60 rogue.",
            date = "2010-02-01T19:27:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9731#comments:id=962476",
        },
        {
            id = 22316,
            score = 10,
            author = "Annai",
            text = "Folks need to watch out for the crazy amounts of ravenous fish (forget the actual name) around the shores here. I jumped in the water at the wrong point and was badly mauled. They're like the fish in ZG, only non-elite, but there are *many* of them and can overwhelm you. If you can manage it, get up on one of the pipes and run to the middle to avoid fish.",
            date = "2007-01-20T22:33:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9731#comments:id=22316",
        },
    },
