            text = "The number of Clefthoofs needed has been dropped from 30 to 12.",
            date = "2009-04-14T21:36:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=676614",
        },
        {
            id = 65535,
            score = 8,
            author = "Nerissa",
            text = "I looked at the number required and died a little inside. 3 times the number required for the earlier STV chain. (Which is structured the same way)",
            date = "2007-04-11T13:29:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=65535",
        },
        {
            id = 12535,
            score = 5,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Head down to the grassy area just North of the Ring of Trials and you'll find the best area to get quick kills.  The area is also rich with Windroc's -- I suggest pairing the quest with http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9854.",
            date = "2006-12-10T01:29:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=12535",
        },
        {
            id = 172562,
            score = 5,
            author = "93908",
            text = "I like to try and get as many quests done as possible at each area, so I stayed in the area just west over the road from the Burning Blade Ruins (69,71 is the middle of the small area I was doing this) while here I completed:\n\nClefthoof Mastery - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9789\nTalbuk Mastery - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9857\nI Must Have Them - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10109\nThe Tortured Earth - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9819\nA Head Full of Ivory - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9914 (although the Wild Elekk's dont come by often its easy enough with the kill list you have from the other quests)\n\n5 Quests in 1 small area meant some great XPph once all complete and hand ins done.",
            date = "2007-10-21T07:10:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=172562",
        },
    },
    [9790] = {
        {
            id = 21635,
            score = 38,
            author = "13105",
            text = "These drop off the stingers, needlers, and bleeders.",
            date = "2007-01-19T15:54:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9790#comments:id=21635",
        },
        {
            id = 70618,
            score = 24,
            author = "10415",
            text = "Do this quest along with http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9830 .",
            date = "2007-04-21T18:22:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9790#comments:id=70618",
        },
        {
            id = 25361,
            score = 17,
            author = "16485",
            text = "There are plenty south of Orebor Harborage and on the east end of Hewn Bog.\n\nI suggest doing the initial Angor'mosh and Daggerfen quests together with this one. They're good quests to grind in one general area.",
            date = "2007-01-26T21:50:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9790#comments:id=25361",
        },
        {
            id = 113757,
            score = 17,
            author = "44538",
            text = "Contrary to what Haalrun says, these wings also drop from Bogflare Needlers, Fenglow Stingers and Marshlight Bleeders (as indicated by the first post).\n\nIt may be advantageous for different classes to fight different bugs. For example, the Bogflare Needler gives Lambent Blood, which inreases Strength by 10%, and so could be used well by a warrior.",
            date = "2007-07-01T08:39:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9790#comments:id=113757",
        },
        {
            id = 27573,
