    [9801] = {
        {
            id = 21637,
            score = 62,
            author = "Detonite",
            text = "Dont waste time killing Young Spore Bats for an hour or so before you realise its the real Spor Bats you need to focus on. These you can find @ 53,66.\n\nOg and by the way, the Fen Striders have about <15% droprate on their Tentacles, so happy grinding!\n\n:D",
            date = "2007-01-19T15:57:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9801#comments:id=21637",
        },
        {
            id = 21748,
            score = 49,
            author = "MrGorun",
            text = "Spore bat Eye - 63,55 very good drop\nFen Strider in same place",
            date = "2007-01-19T19:26:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9801#comments:id=21748",
        },
        {
            id = 163561,
            score = 32,
            author = "91986",
            text = "Total completion time: 31 minutes.\n\nThe Unofficial Official Way to do This Quest Quickly™\n\n1. Obtain this quest\n2. Obtain quest \"Menacing Marshfangs\" ( http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9791 )\n3. Head to The Dead Mire\n4. Find Sporewing (Spawns at 76, 45 every time)\n\nNow, the quickest way to do this is to kill Sporewing, obviously, and then wait for him to respawn.  My luck with the Spore Bat Eyes killing *just* Sporewing over and over again was approximately 60%*.  It didn't take me long to figure out that this mob has a 150 second (2.5 minute) respawn.  Every time you kill him (Or any regular Spore Bat), you receive a buff called \"Energizing Spores\", which lasts 5 minutes.  As soon as you kill Sporewing, either find Fen Striders or Marshfang Rippers.  You will be able to kill approximately 1-2 of either of these mobs before Sporewing respawns, depending on what's around and how fast your mount is.  When your buff reads 3 minutes left, go back to his respawn, and he either should respawn shortly, or he just got there.  Either way, you're almost guaranteed the kill.  Rinse, lather, repeat.  You'll have both quests done within the hour*.\n\n5.  Chances are, you'll have the eyes finished before you have the tentacles, so finish up the Fen Striders, which drop chance isn't nearly as painful as regular Spore Bats.\n6.  Thank yourself for coming to this site and reading this stupid, bloated guide.\n7.  Send me gold ;)\n\n* Average mileage may vary.  Not available in all states.  For more information, see your local retailer.  WARNING: Doing this quest any other way may cause side effects, including depression, anger, and involuntary compulsion to jab out your own eyes.  In rare cases, the adventurer threw their computer in to a wall, quit WoW, and sought a life of self-actualization, but this occurred in less than 2% of all findings.",
            date = "2007-10-06T02:57:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9801#comments:id=163561",
        },
        {
            id = 28209,
            score = 10,
            author = "6225",
            text = "I did the quest , any my suggestion to you is to do it when you've got a reason to be happy. Because the low drop rates and the rarity of the mobs involved can turn you nuts.\n\nOR\n\ndo the first two parts fast so you can complete the quest while exploring the rest of the area and doing other quests.",
            date = "2007-01-31T10:15:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9801#comments:id=28209",
        },
        {
            id = 327241,
            score = 7,
            author = "39294",
            text = "Patch 2.4.3\n\"Young Sporebats and Greater Sporebats in Zangarmarsh now drop Sporebat Eyes for the quest Gathering the Reagents.\"",
            date = "2008-07-15T18:29:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9801#comments:id=327241",
        },
    },
    [9802] = {
        {
            id = 21074,
            score = 72,
            author = "Fugazi",
            text = "Available only until honored :(",
            date = "2007-01-17T15:16:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9802#comments:id=21074",
        },
        {
            id = 139194,
            score = 24,
            author = "bnetgamer77",
            text = "Shocking how no one mentions a fine area to farm these.\n\nIt's true most, if not all mobs have an average of 20-25% chance to drop these...but I found out that the most annoying of Zangarmarsh creatures hold the key to gaining many Unidentified plants.\n\nIf you've ever done an instance in Zangarmasrh, you know of the lake to swim through has a plentiful amount of Mudfin frenzys' that every so often shoot up at you.\n\nTurns out these buggers each have a 20-25% chance to drop an Unidentified Plant, and being they are all 1/4 of a regular mob, to AoE them down in a sense technically quadruples your chance of finding an Unidentified Plant.\n\nI farmed these guys in bear form with no hassle and hit some mobs of 4 with no drops, to tanking a mob of 8 getting 7 drops...the odds are in your favor if you're out for the Grinding of Unidentified Plants.\n\nBest of luck, and good fishing!",
            date = "2007-08-16T21:28:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9802#comments:id=139194",
        },
        {
            id = 128058,
            score = 13,
            author = "74113",
            text = "9000 rep from neutral (first contact) to Honored (when the quest stops being available).  This means 360 plant parts for non-humans, 330 for humans in order to go straight to Honored.  If you quest properly afterwards (All of CE's Zang quests, BEM quests, etc.) you can be Revered without even doing Steamvault.",
            date = "2007-07-28T01:53:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9802#comments:id=128058",
        },
        {
            id = 330138,
            score = 10,
            author = "175775",
            text = "As an herbalist, you have additional chances of gathering these, including:\n\n- any type of marsh herbs that you pick will give you chance of picking a plant part\n- you can \"gather herb\" off of dead mobs in dead mire -- same way a skinner skins a dead mob",
            date = "2008-07-19T11:02:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9802#comments:id=330138",
        },
        {
            id = 25781,
            score = 8,
            author = "16806",
            text = "Dropped off any creature in the entire Marsh, easly done with any other quest.",
            date = "2007-01-27T14:44:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9802#comments:id=25781",
        },
    },
    [9803] = {
        {
            id = 22495,
            score = 41,
            author = "13234",
            text = "Location is 45,66. The quest completes once you enter the hut in the far south of the ruins , and drink the potion you got from the quest giver , then just speak to him , thats all .\nVery easy quest , nice greenie armour , 12600xp for lvl 62-64",
            date = "2007-01-21T17:53:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9803#comments:id=22495",
        },
        {
            id = 58578,
            score = 15,
            author = "InfernoMan",
            text = "There are a set of steps that lead up to the ruins, with four guards, 2 about halfway and 2 at the top.  If you want to avoid a couple of fights you can use the potion on the very bottom step, walk by the guards and up to the boss to complete the quest.  The potion transforms you for 5 minutes, so more than enough time.",
            date = "2007-03-28T11:14:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9803#comments:id=58578",
        },
        {
            id = 248241,
            score = 10,
            author = "Kassimer",
            text = "A fun fact...if you're a 68+ druid doing this quest, you can shift to flight form after you've drunk the potion, and you'll fly while still an Arakkoa. It only works while in the Ruins though, so be careful to only try this after you've gotten the \"Complete\" message.",
            date = "2008-03-05T01:20:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9803#comments:id=248241",
        },
        {
            id = 1954789,
            score = 10,
            author = "Mondoblasto",
            text = "I find it interesting how Ahuurn is surprised that the Feralfen would say no to the offer.  They never wanted to leave in the first place, they were driven away by their own people.  Yes, they didn't know if the condition was contagious or not, but often times in Unbroken, the draenei didn't treat them as the sick to be pitied, but rather as pariahs that the Light punished, and thus deserving of contempt.\n\nI would think that all the draenei, including the Broken and Lost Ones, would still remember that we're all a part of the same people.\n\nAnd that's the thing in the end.  The Lost Ones that are still sane and the Broken still remember, and will always remember.  Not all the draenei agreed with sending them away, but as a whole, they were the ones that decided to forget.",
            date = "2014-03-30T08:03:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9803#comments:id=1954789",
        },
        {
            id = 278204,
            score = 6,
            author = "97917",
            text = "If you're a shaman, you are able to ghost wolf and still retain your arakkoa form as long as you're in the ruins. Not as cool as the druid thing, but it's still kinda funny watching an arakkoa sprint.",
            date = "2008-04-27T09:50:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9803#comments:id=278204",
        },
    },
    [9804] = {
