    [9897] = {
        {
            id = 28951,
            score = 77,
            author = "Sihmm",
            text = "Saving Kristen DeMeza from Ganky Rottenfist (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18297) causes her to offer this quest.  Anyone can take and complete it until she despawns, whether or not they really *did* save her.  Unfortunately, I've no idea what causes her to come running into the camp asking for help, yet!\n\nThe real Kristen DeMeza is an Assistant Game Designer at Blizzard, and is apparently part of the team in charge of world events.",
            date = "2007-02-01T13:21:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9897#comments:id=28951",
        },
        {
            id = 343064,
            score = 38,
            author = "StellHell",
            text = "Kristen has a 1.5h respawntime (1hour 30 minutes). When she spawns, she stayes at the camp for 5 minutes or until she is killed.\n\nI camped Nesingswary tonight, and logged some times.\n\n01:00: Kristen spawns and runs down to Nesingswary\n01:05: Kristen despawns from the spot\n02:35: Kristen spawns and runs down to Nesingswary\n02:40: Kristen despawns from the spot\n\nThese times are all serverside, checked with /time command.\n\nThis was on Blade's Edge-EU @ 08-08-03",
            date = "2008-08-02T19:47:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9897#comments:id=343064",
        },
        {
            id = 29824,
            score = 28,
            author = "11660",
            text = "Yep, I was just chilling in the camp, and this little gnome came walking up.  I have Heightened Senses, so I saw this UD Rogue named Gankly following her for a while.  Curious as to what was going on, I stuck around to watch.  She says something about a shipment of skins, and then the rogue attacked her.  Easy kill, she offers a quest to give the skins to the guy literally lying down right next to her ... the same guy she was talking to just a moment before.",
            date = "2007-02-03T02:57:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9897#comments:id=29824",
        },
        {
            id = 336369,
            score = 25,
            author = "OhTeeSee",
            text = "As of 2.4.3 (or possibly prior) Kristen DeMeza is now Kristen Dipswitch, the cause for this change is unknown.",
            date = "2008-07-25T22:04:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9897#comments:id=336369",
        },
        {
            id = 349632,
            score = 19,
            author = "177078",
            text = "Set and Setting:\n\nWaiting on Krsten Demeza.  I spent over two hours waiting for this event one night.\n\nActivitys:\n\nStarted grinding out Nes's first three master quests.\n\nKept a close eye on the camp while grinding almost continually in close range to the camp.\n\nFinished early. (completed all three quests in 25-30 minutes)\n\nContinued to grind on the saw few respawns.  There are plenty to keep my busy and let me stay close enough to the camp so I know what's happening.\n\nConclusions:\n\nEvent does not appear to be directly linked to any scripted sequence or event (ex. The Stag Event)\n\nEvent does not appear to be based on or tied to emotes.\n\nEvent does not appear to happenly on an hourly basis let alone on the hour.\n\nThoughts:\n  I can confirm that it is not linked to the stag event or any textual event involving the camp.  I saw most (probably all) of the different scripted events and emotes that can take place in Nesingwary's camp multiple times that night.  I even saw the emote: \"Harold Lane winces when he touches the tender area around his scratch\" and another similar version.  Though tangibly rarer than the other emotes, these emotes did not seem to trigger the event.  I witnessed most of the emotes multiples.  I have noticed that it does not seem to be hourly.  I was there for two complete hours.  I didn't notice it occur at all at that time.  When it did occur, the time was no where near a popular relative quanta and based on previous evidence did not appear to be hourly in anyway.\n\nFurther details of my attempt:\nAfter over two hours of waiting and grinding in the immediate area of the tent, I finally saw her ride up.\n\nIt's a little gnome that comes riding from the entrance into Zangarmarsh (in the Northeast of Nagrand).  She rides Soutwest along the path and pulls over into camp.  She dismounts and begins talking to the injured man (Harold, the man lying down in camp).  As she talks to him, Gankly Rottenfist sneaks up from behind Harold's tent around it's side and then moves into position behind her back (her back should be facing the tent from where Gankly is coming) and then after a short pause he attacks.  Krizten isn't super squishy.  She can take a few hits, but does go down fairly fast.  You have a matter of up to 7 seconds or so to respond to the even after she dismounts.  Gankly's attention is easily one.  I prepped a Searing Pain on my lock just in case, but he came off with no fuss.  After that it's just as simple as most other mobs.  Non elite.  He goes down without much effort.\n\nAdvice:\nGet the Nes's three beginning quests and grind in the immediate area.  I was able to grind out all three quests in 25 minutes without leaving the area.  At this point, after you have finised the quests, you should ready to leave this area.  You can justify staying by looking for a quest starting drop off an Air elemental in the area.  Outside of that.  I would recommend you move on.   The event is kinda cool, but not worth blowing time on it not happening.  If you do decide to stay, which I advise against, continually grind those mobs down in the area (great for skinners).\nGanklyGankly is easy to deal with.  Stand near Kristen and when Gankly comes close (if you have trouble seeing him spam tab till he comes up while facing his general direction) target him and spam a high aggro fast cast spell.  That should get him on you almost as soon as is attackable flag is set.  Burn him down.  He is an easy fight.  Get your sweet xp.  Some would call it free xp .. I would call it lucky in that case.  I had to point a lot of work in for it, but I did get a good bit of grinding done.\n\nIf you really want this quest, imagine it's a grinding-endurance test and start grinding till it happens.",
            date = "2008-08-11T00:22:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9897#comments:id=349632",
        },
    },
