            text = "The description gives you the impression he's in the water.  He infact spawns right in the middle of the island there and never moves.  co-ords confirmed 22,46",
            date = "2007-01-27T10:43:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9904#comments:id=25638",
        },
        {
            id = 22616,
            score = 15,
            author = "13907",
            text = "Spawn time is between 5-7 minutes.",
            date = "2007-01-21T23:43:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9904#comments:id=22616",
        },
        {
            id = 1199723,
            score = 9,
            author = "526525",
            text = "To all those that had trouble getting this quest; although the above comments are correct regarding Angling to Beat the Compotition (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9845) being a preQ, I did not see the Pursuing Terrorclaw (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=9904) immediately, only The Biggest of Them All (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=9903). After NerdRaging I simply walked away from Zurjaya for a few seconds, spoke to her again and voila! The quest appeared for me to take.",
            date = "2010-12-01T07:33:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9904#comments:id=1199723",
        },
    },
    [9905] = {
        {
            id = 17788,
            score = 53,
            author = "10162",
            text = "Mragesh - underwater (tloc 42,41)",
            date = "2006-12-22T03:18:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9905#comments:id=17788",
        },
        {
            id = 22990,
            score = 27,
            author = "Hyle",
            text = "Be sure to fight him on land, there are many frenzy fish in the area. Mragesh is a Black/Drk Brown hydra with an orange underbelly. Besides melee he has a frostbolt attack. I'm ot sure if it stacks but I know it slows you movement speed like a normal forstbolt. Not a very difficult mob to kill in my opinion.",
            date = "2007-01-22T22:11:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9905#comments:id=22990",
        },
        {
            id = 38717,
            score = 23,
            author = "23693",
            text = "Right at 42,41, beside a little island under the water.  While swimming you'll aggro about 4 - 6 of the frenzy's, all you gotta do is hop up outta the water and kill Mragresh standing on the island.  He is very easy non-elite lvl 64.\nIf you don't have coords, just look at your map, where it says Serpent Lake, you should be standing at the island where the L in lake is and that's where Mragresh is.  =D  easy quest",
            date = "2007-02-19T13:25:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9905#comments:id=38717",
        },
        {
            id = 384922,
            score = 9,
            author = "evilbyter",
            text = "An annoying spawn rate of 5 minutes if he has just died.",
            date = "2008-09-23T02:45:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9905#comments:id=384922",
        },
        {
            id = 413821,
            score = 2,
            author = "88677",
            text = "This mob is actually really easy to kill for most classes at lvl 65 or higher, as long as you don't have to deal with the stupid fish at the same time.\n\nNothing special to it, other than a frost bolt that slows you down a little.\n\nAfter patch 3.0.2, only affliction locks and shadow priests should have to struggle with the killing.",
            date = "2008-10-20T17:17:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9905#comments:id=413821",
        },
    },
    [9906] = {
        {
            id = 27371,
            score = 22,
            author = "15038",
            text = "All ogres found at 72, 69",
            date = "2007-01-29T20:11:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9906#comments:id=27371",
        },
        {
            id = 16623,
            score = 20,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Head to the Burning Blade Ruins and you'll find an abundant amount of these mobs.  Suggest pairing this quest with http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9910 .",
            date = "2006-12-17T17:34:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9906#comments:id=16623",
        },
        {
            id = 235047,
            score = 18,
            author = "SockPuppet",
            text = "Not really, or not necessarily, at any rate.  The phrase \"message in a bottle\" has a long history, and dates MUCH farther back than The Police.",
            date = "2008-02-13T08:50:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9906#comments:id=235047",
        },
        {
            id = 30076,
            score = 8,
            author = "Heathcliff",
            text = "Pair this with quests for Obsidian Warbeads (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=25433)",
            date = "2007-02-03T13:35:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9906#comments:id=30076",
        },
        {
            id = 348509,
            score = 3,
            author = "152011",
            text = "It is a reference to Message in a Bottle, but not The Police' song. The concept of a message in a bottle predates The Police by a loooooooooooooooong time.",
            date = "2008-08-09T14:26:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9906#comments:id=348509",
        },
    },
    [9907] = {
        {
            id = 16631,
            score = 31,
            author = "6934",
            text = "I prefer Southwind cleft for these, but either will do.  Head into the caves and make a loop or two if you need... there's a lot of kills required here.  Save yourself some time and pair this quest up with Bleeding Hollow Supply Crates(http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9916) if you can.",
            date = "2006-12-17T18:02:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9907#comments:id=16631",
        },
        {
            id = 24006,
            score = 18,
            author = "Zmoke",
            text = "You can find the Warriors and Mages in both of those caverns.\n\n(40,32)\n\n(50,56)",
            date = "2007-01-24T20:34:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9907#comments:id=24006",
        },
        {
            id = 62659,
            score = 12,
            author = "16379",
            text = "Whatever you do, no matter how tempting it may be, don't use fear in the cave ....",
            date = "2007-04-05T16:31:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9907#comments:id=62659",
        },
        {
            id = 32027,
            score = 7,
            author = "19061",
            text = "To confirm some of what has been said before. Be sure to have the Bleeding Hollow Supply Crates quest before you undertake this one.\n\nIf you need only the ogres, its safer outside the cave. If you need both, the cave is a good choice (the crates are very abundant in the caves), but can get rough in there if you're not a durable or particularly fast dps class. Very often you'll aggro a mage type behind the ogre you're fighting and you wont realize it until you notice you're very low on health. Also, running is very difficult in the caves as the warriors charge and will daze you constantly.",
            date = "2007-02-07T03:49:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9907#comments:id=32027",
        },
        {
            id = 25158,
            score = 6,
            author = "16346",
            text = "Watch for double spawns in the cave. 2 might be ok to fight at one time but 3 makes it tough if you are by yourself. Get the other quest as mentioned but get them quick and go outside. Much safer to fight outside the cave.",
            date = "2007-01-26T15:02:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9907#comments:id=25158",
        },
    },
    [9910] = {
        {
            id = 16622,
            score = 48,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Pair this up with Message in a Battle(http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9906) - both will take you to the Burning Blade Ruins. The first pyre is near the West enrance, for the second and third head up the paths that lead up the hill.  These pyres look just like big campfires ~ place the banners next to them to get credit.\n\nTlocs:\nPyre 1: 72, 69\nPyre 2: 74, 70\nPyre 3: 75, 68",
            date = "2006-12-17T17:23:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9910#comments:id=16622",
