    [9999] = {
        {
            id = 25454,
            score = 22,
            author = "13511",
            text = "Bit of information on these mobs. The tinkerers come in packs of 4 at a time. Seem to be leashed to one another. The engineers sometimes cast the magnetic pull spell which pulls someone to them, making them hard to kite. This only happened once of the 3 kites I did solo on them so I'm not sure if it was just a bug, or if its just something they do very rarely. Its definitely less common from them then it is on the next to quest encounters in the chain. The Legionnaires are just a straight melee type elite, hit fairly hard.. Not something to go toe to toe with unless you have a bit of backup.",
            date = "2007-01-27T02:11:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9999#comments:id=25454",
        },
        {
            id = 11634,
            score = 14,
            author = "8258",
            text = "Easily soloable as a demonology warlock. All demons here can be feared and banished and with the felguard it makes it a cake walk.",
            date = "2006-12-08T18:25:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9999#comments:id=11634",
        },
        {
            id = 28935,
            score = 6,
            author = "15533",
            text = "Solo'd this part of the quest as a 66 feral druid.  The tinkerers are easy in bear form.  Engineers are not totally hard but if you don't work it right, they might kill you.  The legionaires are prob the most difficult for a feral druid.  Charge them and kill their cannons first, then bash, shift out, entangle root them and heal.  Once healed, just let the root take it's corse so that bash can cool down.  Then go back in for more.  Tank, bash, root, heal...  takes some time but works like a charm.  Keep some health potions on hand to use incase bash is dodged, blocked, parried, etc.  You should be ok. ;-)",
            date = "2007-02-01T12:49:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9999#comments:id=28935",
        },
        {
            id = 491362,
            score = 6,
            author = "40967",
            text = "Soloed as 66 frost mage using some suggestions above (I used my pet for extra insurance).\n\nThere are two legionnaires on the northeast side of FC:F that can be pulled solo without cannons, and there's also a demon gate on the southwest side of the camp where there are two engineers who can also be pulled alone.\n\nBasically, I did what others did which is to kite them around in a tight circle near where they were spawned.  Legionnaires are hardest since they can do the most damage, but I had a few pots handy just in case, plus the mana ruby.\n\nIn the case of engineers, I died the first time since I wasn't aware of Magnetic Pull (which btw doesn't work on the elemental, so just keep as much distance as possible), but after that I didn't even take a hp of damage.  Using the pet to start off, slow the engy with FB / IL, used pet's nova and then mine when it broke.  By the time it was out of the second FN, it was pretty much dead.",
            date = "2008-12-05T10:24:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9999#comments:id=491362",
        },
        {
            id = 37722,
            score = 5,
            author = "17991",
            text = "Solo'd easily by a level 66 balance druid - mobs are not immune to roots.",
            date = "2007-02-17T19:13:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9999#comments:id=37722",
        },
    },
