    [10016] = {
        {
            id = 81377,
            score = 61,
            author = "26336",
            text = "Its amazing how few wolves in Terrokar have tails. You'd swear it looks like they all have one, but once the kill is done, lo and behold, no tail. Reminds me of those mutant humans in Hillsbrad that have no skulls....",
            date = "2007-05-11T11:48:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10016#comments:id=81377",
        },
        {
            id = 23497,
            score = 31,
            author = "14357",
            text = "No need to rush with this quest, the Worgs are all over Terrorkar, just kill them as you are taking care of more important quests.",
            date = "2007-01-24T04:34:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10016#comments:id=23497",
        },
        {
            id = 68647,
            score = 26,
            author = "40642",
            text = "Drop rate is somewhere between non-existant and ridiculous, leaning towards ridiculous, since every worg you find has a large fluffy tail which somehow seems to disappear at the moment you deal the killing blow. Very odd.",
            date = "2007-04-17T12:25:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10016#comments:id=68647",
        },
        {
            id = 31635,
            score = 20,
            author = "18685",
            text = "A lot of wolves are indeed located at the Bonechewer Ruins (not inside, but north of the zone). If you are here to kill the wolves, it would be smart to also pick up the quest \"Unruly Neighbors\" (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9998) for the Warped Peons there.",
            date = "2007-02-06T09:20:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10016#comments:id=31635",
        },
        {
            id = 330411,
            score = 15,
            author = "143590",
            text = "Y'know, I could understand the flaky drop rates if you were searching for something peculiar.. such as a certain type of wolf.. but a low drop rate for something that is intrinsic to the species as a whole..such as a tail... is ridiculous.  That's like saying \"Oh...you've killed the giant two-headed ogre...but you can't find his heads in order to decapitate them and return them for the quest...\"  HOW do you MISS something like that??  Whomever designs the quests and/or loot subroutines needs to be dragged out into the middle of the street and beat profusely about the head and shoulders with wolf tails..",
            date = "2008-07-19T16:48:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10016#comments:id=330411",
        },
    },
    [10017] = {
        {
            id = 22272,
            score = 71,
            author = "Thehermit",
            text = "This quest is only available to characters hostile to The Aldor. It is repeatable and used to switch over from The Scryers.",
            date = "2007-01-20T20:51:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10017#comments:id=22272",
        },
        {
            id = 1134600,
            score = 54,
            author = "Crucifisk",
            text = "Aight, so these things (http://www.wowhead.com/item=25802) drop off  Dreadfang Lurkers (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=18466) and Widows (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=18467) and with an estimated (quite correct) drop rate of 34%. You turn these in, 8 by 8 to get 250 reputation per turn-in with  the Aldor (http://www.wowhead.com/faction=932) if you chose the Scryers (http://www.wowhead.com/faction=934) by mistake, want to change for a pattern, going for the Feat of Strength achievement  Hero of Shattrath (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=1205) or whatever reason you want to come up with.\n\nStrained Supplies (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10017) is the way to turn in this things, although you don't need the quest to loot them! Correct, you can farm these without the quest which you might also want, because the achievement (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=1205) will require you (from 0/36000 Hated) to turn in, not one, not two, but 1344 of these beauties (Warning: This is a calculation based on the non-Human races, for a Human, that would be 1224). Oh yes, that many. It takes you to Neutral, making you able to do quests for the Aldor (http://www.wowhead.com/faction=932), as well as other (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10326) turn-in (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10654) quests (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10421).\n\nSo how am I gonna get 1344 before I die, you ask? Well, here's the answer, aswell as a good route (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=3519:555590520786549644541679533710527735554605541565532578531588533598545596541613549621542580528753532763532778529792516805505798510778520768515751541660536697527722) starting just outside the Alliance camp Allerian Stronghold (which is also a very good place to clear your bags in a way earning your money, unless you use addons like Loot Filter (http://wow.curse.com/downloads/wow-addons/details/loot-filter.aspx)). So running back and forth between Allerian Stronghold and Netherweb Ridge south of it at the edge of Outland might not be so fun you think, but with the right resolve and some good music you can earn above 100 per hour. I succeeded in getting exacly 100 per hour a couple of times, so with some complex maths it's about a 13-14 hour farm.\n\nI noticed that instead of pressing \"B\" every few seconds to see how many you've got left to gather, you can fix a macro. Because the game won't let you drag non-usable items out on the bars, you can always make something simple, such as;\n\n#showtooltip Dreadfang Venom Sac\n\nWorks really smooth. The icon shows how many you've got, and if you hold your mouse over it, it shows how much gold you're wasting not selling them to a vendor! (Combine this with an addon such as BankItems (http://wow.curse.com/downloads/wow-addons/details/bank-items.aspx) and you'll even see how many your account has, it you can't be arsed filling your farmer char's bags with them!)\n\nSo there you go, a small guide for farming the Feat of Strength achievement Hero of Shattrath (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=1205)!\n\nGood luck! Oh, and don't go insane while at it!",
            date = "2010-10-04T12:12:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10017#comments:id=1134600",
        },
        {
            id = 22521,
            score = 42,
            author = "11660",
            text = "Yes, it exists so that one can switch from Scryers to Aldor.  It is the same case for this quest, although this one is to switch from Aldor to Scryers:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10024",
            date = "2007-01-21T18:49:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10017#comments:id=22521",
        },
        {
            id = 1473592,
            score = 18,
            author = "mekikya",
            text = "In case you were confused as heck like me, you HAVE to have completed some prereq quests...and FYI, You wont be able to talk to Adal or Khadgar for the city of the light quest, you unless you get the quest from the veteran FIRST...learned that the hard way...\n\n[npc=19684 domain=www]\n[quest=10210 domain=www]\n[quest=10211 domain=www]\n\nand then choose a side\n\n[quest=10551 domain=www]\n[quest=10552 domain=www]\n\nif you pick the aldor, then a quest to switch sides to the scryers will appear\n\n[quest=10024 domain=www]\n[quest=10025 domain=www] (repeatable)\n\nif you pick scryer, then you will have this quest available and its repeatable counter part\n\n[quest=10019 domain=www]\n\nthose are only good for rep until neutral...then there are other turn ins to get your rep higher at the different factions rises...",
            date = "2011-07-18T19:02:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10017#comments:id=1473592",
        },
        {
            id = 217319,
            score = 15,
            author = "frago",
            text = "From wowwiki\n\nIt will take 1344 Dreadfang Venom Sacs to go from completely hated with Aldor to Neutral.",
            date = "2008-01-12T16:45:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10017#comments:id=217319",
        },
    },
