        {
            id = 21939,
            score = 31,
            author = "3101",
            text = "Shadowy Initiate 39,39\nShadowy Laborer 38,41\nShadowy Advisor 40,39",
            date = "2007-01-20T05:59:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10040#comments:id=21939",
        },
        {
            id = 21880,
            score = 25,
            author = "moptop",
            text = "If you get spotted by a hunter and lose your disguise, you can talk to Private Weeks again to get another one.",
            date = "2007-01-20T03:09:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10040#comments:id=21880",
        },
    },
    [10041] = {
        {
            id = 127289,
            score = 52,
            author = "68244",
            text = "You can accept this quest while mounted. However, you will not receive the disguise. Make sure to be unmounted to receive the disguise as intended.",
            date = "2007-07-26T16:36:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10041#comments:id=127289",
        },
        {
            id = 22882,
            score = 49,
            author = "Gokou",
            text = "All 3 guys are in Grangol'var Village.\n\nThe laborer = A Troll wandering around.\nThe initiate = In the middle of the area, on one of the docks surrounding the waters. A Human\nThe advisor = In the biggest building that you can find. A Gnome.",
            date = "2007-01-22T16:35:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10041#comments:id=22882",
        },
        {
            id = 61154,
            score = 26,
            author = "32282",
            text = "Laboror = 38, 39 (Patrols supposedly, found him standing there)\nInitiate = 39, 39\nAdvisor = 40, 39",
            date = "2007-04-02T15:36:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10041#comments:id=61154",
        },
        {
            id = 24956,
            score = 21,
            author = "16194",
            text = "You cannot mine minerals without losing your disguise",
            date = "2007-01-26T09:41:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10041#comments:id=24956",
        },
        {
            id = 228906,
            score = 19,
            author = "Cross88",
            text = "Be careful about talking to anyone else besides the three people. The other mobs talk about leather ball leagues and going into shat for drinks. I felt really bad about ruining their plans as I roasted them alive with fire balls...",
            date = "2008-02-03T14:22:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10041#comments:id=228906",
        },
    },
    [10042] = {
        {
            id = 23488,
            score = 15,
            author = "14357",
            text = "Private Weeks gives out one of the easiest chain quests here. The mobs can be pulled one by one and are easy to kill. However it would help to be in a party to make killing Grieve easier.\n\nGrieve is in the main hut at 40,39. You only have to worry about the Advisor when attacking Grieve, the summoner in the room won't aggro\n\n*Caution to rogues and druids... If you stealth past the guards to kill Grieve they will run in once he has been slain and begin to attack. So either have a vanish up, or get ready to dash outta there",
            date = "2007-01-24T04:08:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10042#comments:id=23488",
        },
        {
            id = 38133,
            score = 6,
            author = "24917",
            text = "If you have trouble getting into the Grieve's room like I did, you can die in the room and resurrect in the corner in front of the Grieve without aggroing him.  The Hunter patrol does patrol in the Grieve's room so be careful.",
            date = "2007-02-18T12:24:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10042#comments:id=38133",
        },
        {
            id = 842752,
            score = 6,
            author = "452994",
            text = "Or have a flying mount.\nThen you just fly in through the hole in the roof, land against the wall midway between Grieve and the Summoner. Then kill the summuner, rest, kill Grieve, then fly out through the hole.\n\nPicking off the others took more time.",
            date = "2009-09-17T21:42:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10042#comments:id=842752",
        },
        {
            id = 26271,
            score = 4,
            author = "Flexy",
            text = "He is easy to kill... You can pull the Advisoir without pulling the boss. Then just solo him :P",
            date = "2007-01-28T09:07:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10042#comments:id=26271",
        },
        {
            id = 341322,
            score = 4,
            author = "174981",
            text = "A couple of things:\n\nGrieve and his advisor have a respawn time of about one minute. I killed them, and the other mob in the room, and stopped to drink. Within one minute, both had respawned on top of me.\n\nMages can use Fire Ward very effectively against the summoners, because they only cast scorch. Fire ward is able to block 2-3 scorches easily.\n\nBe careful not to pull more than one summoner at a time. Four mobs is a lot to handle.\n\nIf the hunters spot you, they WILL bring at least one other mob with them. Try not to get seen by hunters.\nSummoners respawn after about 2 minutes, WITHOUT their pets. They summon the pets a few seconds after they respawn.",
            date = "2008-07-31T09:50:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10042#comments:id=341322",
        },
    },
    [10043] = {
        {
            id = 11341,
            score = 16,
            author = "6934",
            text = "This quest was a bit challenging compared to most. The close proximity of mobs, the constant patrols, and the somewhat quick respawn times here can cause you to become overwhelmed rather quickly. I had to corpse hop into the building that Shadowmaster Grieve was in due to the amount of mobs constantly in front of the entrance. Might be a good idea to bring a buddy along for this one.",
            date = "2006-12-08T15:35:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10043#comments:id=11341",
        },
        {
            id = 81453,
            score = 11,
            author = "48728",
            text = "Coords:  39, 40\n\nTough quest.  The area is dense with mobs, and there's a few packs of roamers.",
            date = "2007-05-11T14:50:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10043#comments:id=81453",
        },
        {
            id = 110519,
            score = 6,
            author = "65162",
            text = "Quest is a bit tricky, I soloed as a 63 Arms Warrior but I had to ghost walk behind Grieve. It was funny, I killed him and he respawned in less than a minute, litterally. I was just fighting the warlock near him and he just reapeared, so be careful and be hasty once hes dead.",
            date = "2007-06-24T18:38:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10043#comments:id=110519",
        },
        {
            id = 506499,
            score = 5,
            author = "256638",
            text = "As a death knight, this was easy. Death grip will be your best friend and keep you from pulling mobs. Most difficult part is Shadowmaster Grieve, you'll have to clear mobs in order to get in. He spawns quickly, so if someone gets in there before you just hang for a minute.",
            date = "2008-12-12T19:27:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10043#comments:id=506499",
        },
        {
            id = 1488016,
            score = 5,
            author = "Grukam",
            text = "Solo'd as a lvl 65 fury warrior. Reading earlier about dropping through the roof for the Grieve I decided to start there and work my way out. Flew in as close to him as possible and didn't aggro the summoners and their very naughty minions and was able to drop him then took out the summoners. Worked around the wall to the door and started picking them off. Summoners and Executioners are not that hard but still need to try to stay clear of the hunters of they will pull every mob nearby in on you. Almost lost it to that one. As you're looking out of the door of that building start working your way around to the left towards the back side, fewer mobs and easy to pull singles with plenty of both types needed for your tally. Keep working around the back and on towards the front over by the fence until you work around to the next building. By then you should have about all you need except possibly one summoner which is inside the building, kill him and his minion and fly on out.\n\nDo NOT loot the mobs as you go or they will respawn. I made that mistake with the Grieve and nearly regretted it. None of the others respawned after I killed them and he was the only one I looted out of habit.",
            date = "2011-08-05T14:09:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10043#comments:id=1488016",
        },
    },
    [10044] = {
        {
            id = 23680,
            score = 244,
            author = "12816",
            text = "OK, so i finally got this.\n\nthere are 3 confirmed quest lines you must finish before getting this Thrall questline to unlock\n\n1) blademaster chain http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10107\n\n2) altruis the demon hunter chain http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9983\n\n3) the murkblood quests (murkblood invaders http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9872 as well as the escort quest out of sunspring village)\n\nthanks to gurgthock from elitistjerks forums.",
            date = "2007-01-24T11:49:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10044#comments:id=23680",
        },
        {
            id = 502287,
            score = 182,
            author = "123744",
            text = "I originally posted this under the Rep page and under the final quest page but there was a request to repost it on this page so here it is.  Please rate me up, this took a long time to compile and code,  Thanks.\n\nThis Quest Chain starts in Hellfire with The Assassin.   This requires you are able to speak to Nazgrel (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3230) which means you will have to have done at least some of the level 58 outland Quests*.\n\n1. The Assassin (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9400)\n2. A Strange Weapon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9401)\n3. The Warchief's Mandate (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9405)\n4. A Spirit Guide (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9410)\n5. The Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9406)\n6. Messenger to Thrall (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9438)\n7. Envoy to the Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9441)\n\nAlso given at this point are the following, but may not be necessary to complete the Hero chain.  They are very nice rep rewards for each so you may want to do them since you’re there anyway.\n\0091. A Debilitating Sickness (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9442)\n2. Administering the Salve (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9447)\n\nThe next part leads you to Jorin Dead Eye  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18106) in Garadar, Nagrand.\n\n1. The Impotent Leader (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9888)\n2. Don't Kill the Fat One (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9889)\n3. Success! (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9890)\n4. Because Kilrath is a Coward (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9891)\n5. Message in a Battle (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9906)\n6. An Audacious Advance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9907)\n7. Diplomatic Measures (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10107)\n\nTakes you to Nagrand to Find Lantresor of the Blade  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18261) which gives you the Blademaster Chain\n\n1a. Armaments for Deception (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9928)\n1b. Ruthless Cunning (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9927)\n2a. Returning the Favor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9931)\n2b. Body Of Evidence (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9932)\n3.   Message to Garadar (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9934)\n\nYou will also need to complete The following Unrelated Quests.\n1. The Totem of Kar’dash  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9868)\n\nwhich is a simple escort quest beginning with the Mag'har Captive (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18210) in one of the buildings of Sunspring Post.\n\nThe second part involves Altruis the Sufferer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18417) who is right by the Mag’har captive so these are good quests to do together.\n\n1. Survey the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9991)\n2. Buying Time (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9999)\n3. The Master Planner (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10001)\n4. Patience and Understanding (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10004)\n5. Crackin' Some Skulls (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10009)\n6. It's Just That Easy? (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10010)\n7. Forge Camp: Annihilated (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10011)\n\nThis unlocks the final sequence which returns you to Garrosh  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18063).  He sends you finally to visit Greatmother Geyah  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18141).\n\n1. A Visit With the Greatmother (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10044)\n2. Material Components (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10045)\n3. To Meet Mother Kashur (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10081)\n4. The Agitated Ancestors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10082)\n5. A Visit With The Ancestors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10085)\n6. When Spirits Speak (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10101)\n7. A Secret Revealed (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10102)\n8. Auchindoun... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10167)\n9. What the Soul Sees (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10168)\n10. Return to the Greatmother (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10170)\n11. The Inconsolable Chieftain (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10171)\n12. There Is No Hope (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10172)\n13. Thrall, Son of Durotan (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10175)\n14. Hero of the Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10212)\n\nCongrats on you Uber new Gear and Exalted Rep.\n\nSmall disclaimer.  This is a compilation from a lot of peoples work using information from Allakazam (http://wow.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?source=live;wquest=10212), Wowhead  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10212), WoWWiki  (http://www.wowwiki.com/Geyah), and the Armory  (http://www.wowarmory.com/item-info.xml?i=28175).  This took many hours to complete since the info was so scattered so please rate me up if possible.\n\nRaimi, 70 Undead Warlock,\nTitianna 70 Belf Priest\nHeghbathl 70 Belf Tankadin\nSentinals\n*\n1. Through the Dark Portal  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9407)\n2. Arrival in Outland  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10120)\n3. Journey to Thrallmar  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10289)\n4. Report to Nazgrel  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10291)\n5. Eradicate the Burning Legion  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10121)\n6. Felspark Ravine  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10123)\n7. Forward Base: Reaver's Fall  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10124)\n8. Disrupt Their Reinforcements (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10208)\n9. Mission: Gateways Murketh and Shaadraz (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10129)\n10. Mission: The Abyssal Shelf  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10162)",
            date = "2008-12-10T16:17:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10044#comments:id=502287",
        },
        {
            id = 31681,
            score = 74,
            author = "ShihanLock",
            text = "Confirmed Prereqs:\n\nThe Blademaster Chain: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10044\nAltruis the Demon Hunter: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9983\nTotem of Kar'dash (escort): http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9868\n\nNote on the escort quest the horde npc will aggro the alliance npc if they see each other, so go ahead and take them out first.",
            date = "2007-02-06T11:07:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10044#comments:id=31681",
        },
        {
            id = 125845,
            score = 52,
            author = "7577",
            text = "I thought that I had done the escort quest.  I flew over the guy, saw the green NPC down below, and he didn't have a quest ! above his head.  So I assumed I had done it.\n\nBut I was wrong.\n\nTurns out you have to kill all of the mobs near him, and THEN he will give you the escort quest.  So if you've flown over and found the guy, and thought you'd already done it, try killing all of the mobs around him and see if he offers you the escort quest.\n\nBTW, it was reasonably easy to do as a solo 70 BM Hunter.  He heals himself, and my pet could tank most of the mobs.  Cakewalk.\n\nEdit: Fix spelling of a few words",
            date = "2007-07-24T04:03:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10044#comments:id=125845",
        },
        {
            id = 95926,
            score = 34,
            author = "58003",
            text = "The required chains you MUST complete before doing this are:\n\nThe Blademaster Chain:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9888\nThis starts in Nagrand, brings you to Terrokar forest and then back to Nagrand.  When you complete this chain with \"Diplomatic Measures\" the Burning Blade Chain will be unlocked.\n\nBurning Blade Chain (Lantresor of the Blade):\nStarts with:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9928\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9927\nOnce you complete these 2 quests at Kil'Sorrow fortress, you do another 2 up at the Laughing Skull ruins.  The last quest in this chain is \"Message to Garadar\" [http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9934]\n\nAltruis the Demon Hunter chain:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9983\nYou will need a group for most parts of this quest.  There are parts that are easily soloable.  Last quest in this chain to complete is Forge Camp: Annihilated\n\nMurkblood Invaders:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9872\nGet a note from Murkblood Invader who ride arround Nagrand to start the quest.  If you're under 70 you might want a partner.\n\nTotem of Kar'dash (Escort):\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9868\nEasily soloable.",
            date = "2007-06-02T11:07:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10044#comments:id=95926",
        },
    },
    [10045] = {
        {
            id = 24658,
            score = 440,
            author = "Wihl",
            text = "Small guide:\n\nTerokkar Forest:\nOlemba Root: 37.1 - 34.2\nExit through the south-east entrance of Shattrath. It's right outside.\n\nThen fly to Zabra'Jin, Zangarmarsh.\n\nZangarmarsh:\nMarshberries: 20.0 - 8.6\nExit Zabra'Jin and go north, and up to the small floating island, go over the 'mushroom-bridge' and turn right. Go up the slope and you'll see an orange thing on the ground. It looks kinda lika a stone when you first look at it.\n\nGo back to Zabra'Jin and fly up to Thunderlord Stronghold. If you don't have the flightpath, fly to Swamprat Post and go to 70.30 and go through the tunnel and continue north.\n\nBlade's Edge\nDragonspine: 48.6 - 67.1\nGo south from Thunderlord Stronghold to the bridge.\nIt's a small red plant.\n\nGet back to Thunderlord Stronghold and fly to Garadar, Nagrand.\n\nNagrand\nTelaari Frond: 62.3 - 55.7\nGet out of Garadar and go towards 'Ring of Trials'. Then when you get to the bridge go under it and you'll find the Telaari Frond. It's a lot bigger than the others but it can 'blend in' a bit. Looks like a medium-size bush.",
            date = "2007-01-25T20:25:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10045#comments:id=24658",
        },
        {
            id = 26163,
            score = 39,
            author = "17025",
            text = "if you are an herbalist all the materials for this quest will show up with track herbs",
            date = "2007-01-28T03:29:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10045#comments:id=26163",
        },
        {
            id = 48981,
            score = 28,
            author = "32191",
            text = "Olemba Root : 37,34 (Terokkar Forest)\nMarshberry : 20,9 (Zangarmarsh)\nDragonspine : 47,29 (Zangarmarsh)<---there was 5 plants in this area\nTelaari Frond : 62,55 (Nagrand)",
            date = "2007-03-10T03:05:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10045#comments:id=48981",
        },
        {
            id = 2361730,
            score = 15,
            author = "likwidd",
            text = "For tomtom/paste users:\n\nCredits to Wihl, thanks!\n\n/way Blade's Edge Mountains 48.6, 67.1\n/way Zangarmarsh 20, 8.6\n/way Terokkar Forest 37.1, 34.2\n/way Nagrand:Outland 62.3, 55.7",
            date = "2016-08-05T01:18:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10045#comments:id=2361730",
        },
        {
            id = 1574150,
            score = 11,
            author = "406368",
            text = "Quest Note:  It is SAFE to delete/trash the https://www.wowhead.com/item=25866 once the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10045 is completed.  It will sit in your bags until you do so, and cannot be sold.",
            date = "2011-11-17T07:12:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10045#comments:id=1574150",
        },
    },
    [10046] = {
    },
    [10047] = {
        {
            id = 17247,
            score = 61,
            author = "7344",
            text = "The Path of Glory runs from the Dark Portal to Helfire Citadel.\n\nThe far Northern part of the road has skull level mobs and no skeletons.\n\nThe Southern part of the road is covered with level 62 Orcs. However their are alot of skeletons on the road.\n\nThe easiest place to get the skeletons is between about (69, 49) and (62, 49). Although the skeletons are a lettle more spread out here compared to the southern part of the road, there are no mobs to deal with.\n\nWARNING: Fel Reavers cross the road at about 63, 49 (I found out the hard way)",
            date = "2006-12-19T08:45:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10047#comments:id=17247",
        },
        {
            id = 2035006,
            score = 39,
            author = "20136",
            text = "For those looking for the path of glory for https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=8940 it can be found at 66,10.",
            date = "2014-11-16T18:48:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10047#comments:id=2035006",
        },
        {
            id = 1536773,
            score = 15,
            author = "Magirock468",
            text = "You just have to wonder how many Draenei the Orcs had to kill in order to make this road out of bones... Chilling...",
            date = "2011-10-06T19:18:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10047#comments:id=1536773",
        },
        {
            id = 1839889,
            score = 10,
            author = "Myzvale",
            text = "They really need to remove the CD off the item. Makes it annoying to quest here",
            date = "2013-04-06T18:41:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10047#comments:id=1839889",
        },
        {
            id = 396910,
            score = 9,
            author = "MarsJenkar",
            text = "Apparently there's a prerequisite for this that isn't mentioned.  Probably the chain starting at the Dark Portal, Blasted Lands side.  But my L60 paladin can't get any quests from Warp-Scryer Kryv.  And I *know* I've not done this quest yet on this character.",
            date = "2008-10-04T23:22:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10047#comments:id=396910",
        },
    },
    [10048] = {
    },
    [10049] = {
        {
            id = 205953,
            score = 3,
            author = "58992",
            text = "This quest seems to have been removed from the beta.",
            date = "2007-12-23T09:15:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10049#comments:id=205953",
        },
        {
            id = 11686,
            score = 1,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Oye, if I had to choose one word to describe this quest it would be tedious.  The drop rate was about 2 out of 5 kills, and these guys aren't nicely clumped together.  They're in a triangle formed between Tuurem, Stonebreak Hold, and Firewing Point.  They're often surrounded by other aggressive creatures, making this a very time consuming quest.\n\nDon't forget to head over to Rokag after turning this in to pick up the next part of the series.",
            date = "2006-12-08T19:45:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10049#comments:id=11686",
        },
    },
    [10050] = {
        {
            id = 22985,
            score = 21,
            author = "Hyle",
            text = "Just a tip: Pick up the \"An Old Gift\" quest http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10050 along with this quest as you'll likely have to kill some of these undead there to get to that book.",
            date = "2007-01-22T21:58:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10050#comments:id=22985",
        },
        {
            id = 243666,
            score = 5,
            author = "75650",
            text = "55 75 and south for those of us with coords. Those without should head to Expedition Armory.\n\nThese guys are undead so bleed damage cannot be done to them =(\n\nFootman: all around the edge of the area, they can be pulled as singles but watch for patrolling knights!\nKnight: On horse patrols the entire area except the middle of the town. Knights have a charge like ability which CAN STUN!\nSorcerer: Found inside the town. Some patrol some are stationary!",
            date = "2008-02-26T04:43:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10050#comments:id=243666",
        },
        {
            id = 156991,
            score = 4,
            author = "Nerizor",
            text = "The Horde's quest: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10220 (Make them Listen)",
            date = "2007-09-23T05:32:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10050#comments:id=156991",
        },
        {
            id = 178354,
            score = 4,
            author = "24604",
            text = "There is some prereq, either a quest or reputation (according to allakhazam). He doesn't give me any quests and i'm level 61.\n\nEdit: after doing the quest chain that starts with Know your Enemy (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10160) and ends with Ill Omens (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10483), he now gives me the quest. I also completed \"Expedition Point\", but i think the aforementioned quest chain (3 quests) is what triggered it.",
            date = "2007-11-02T23:51:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10050#comments:id=178354",
        },
        {
            id = 398467,
            score = 3,
            author = "Dorean",
            text = "It should be noted that if you are ever ever fighting a knight and another mob at once KILL THE KNIGHT FIRST. They have a spell that heals the other mob for ~60% health which can get annoying.",
            date = "2008-10-06T16:10:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10050#comments:id=398467",
        },
    },
    [10051] = {
        {
            id = 193359,
            score = 50,
            author = "ninjasuperspy",
            text = "Why does she walk down the road?  Was shouting out her position to the nearby warlocks too blatant?  She could just duck between the buildings, go straight south and be out.  She's a druid to boot, its not like she didn't do the quest for cat form and couldn't just stealth right out of there!  If she wants to pay attention to the Blood Elf \"Stay off the Grass\" signs, and stay in caster form, would it kill her to throw a little Gift of the Wild my way?",
            date = "2007-11-29T11:35:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10051#comments:id=193359",
        },
        {
            id = 197236,
            score = 17,
            author = "90584",
            text = "Isla! My bandages will not save you when you chain pull 50 warlocks! Oh well, at least I can loot some signets after you die.",
            date = "2007-12-07T02:12:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10051#comments:id=197236",
        },
        {
            id = 171955,
            score = 12,
            author = "Sekai",
            text = "People are vastly underselling the relative difficulty of this quest. The NPC walks as slow as it's possible to walk and for that reason alone clearing the path for her isn't terribly effective. What you should make sure to do is clear the patrols at a bare minimum and clean up the pair of warlocks parked at the south end of the circular path at Firewing Point. Usually aggroing those forces her to soak a lot of needless damage.\n\nFurther, if she ever, ever gets tangled up by any of the warlock pairs in the very center of the camp and you don't have a partner to clean up the mess, just abandon the quest and run away. Unless you're level 66-67 as a melee or 65-66 as a caster you're going to set off a nasty chain reaction trying to save her that can bring up to 6 mobs down on your heads.",
            date = "2007-10-19T22:29:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10051#comments:id=171955",
        },
        {
            id = 232267,
            score = 9,
            author = "22087",
            text = "Fair Warning, this quest can be extremely difficult.\n\nWhile any one of the mobs in the surrounding area is a joke to take care of, you're rarely dealing with any one particular mob.  In general, you're dealing with an endless chain of warlock casters that will aggro as you attempt to dispatch one of the others.  As these casters can hit you, your pet or your party for 400+ damage a shot, they're not the type of mobs you ignore or wait for your questgiver to dispatch.\n\nRarely will you find such a huge long aggro chain in this game.\n\nAs a level 65 Hunter who knows the class well with 110 shadow resist on their tank pet Boar, it took me 4 attempts to 'safely' complete this.\n\nAside from the NPC (Isla) walking slow as molasses, she'll regularly draw the attention of the dual pairs of warlocks (the ones in the hot pink 10 yard auras).  If you're not extremely lucky or overly cautious, fighting off these 2 warlocks will aggro the 4 center warlocks (the ones channeling the mana bomb).  This in turn will aggro any of the other dual warlocks in the satellite pink auras.\n\nWhile Isla can put out a bit of damage, I didn't see her heal herself once.  Whether she's capable or not, I can't be certain.\n\nIf you do want to complete this quest, either bring a healer friend along, or be certain there are other players clearing the area for their own questchains.",
            date = "2008-02-09T15:59:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10051#comments:id=232267",
        },
        {
            id = 2563547,
            score = 7,
            author = "Shroominator",
            text = "If you accept the quest from her and she doesn't leave the cage, abandon and re-accept. This happened to me, just after someone else had done the quest.",
            date = "2018-04-19T21:22:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10051#comments:id=2563547",
        },
    },
    [10052] = {
        {
            id = 570496,
            score = 22,
            author = "gazhkull",
            text = "They have a dozen fraps of this NPC's pathetic escape attempts during this quest which are shown to new trainees in the Cenarion Academy for Druids in Moonglade as a warning:\n\n- You have easy escape abilities by shapeshifting into travel form or cat form (abilities every other druid on the planet has by that level). Not walking slowly through the valley of warlocks aggroing everybody with moonfire and daring them to test your leather armor's defense bonus.\n\n- You are children of the wild, masters of nature, but please learn to read a goddamn map to figure out that the quickest way out of that place is wading across the nearby  river in 20 seconds.\n\n- You can kill mobs at a distance with spells. You can (easily) kill mobs up close in bear or cat form.  But moonfiring a mob to annoy him (and all his nearby mates) and running up to it to beat on them with your fists in caster form is really, really stupid.\n\n- Walking away to moonfire aggro more mobs while your protector is still in combat at low health doing his damndest to save you is not really a good way to endear people to the Cenarion faction.",
            date = "2009-01-20T04:22:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10052#comments:id=570496",
        },
        {
            id = 235857,
            score = 13,
            author = "128069",
            text = "This is the stupidest NPC in TBC",
            date = "2008-02-14T08:10:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10052#comments:id=235857",
        },
        {
            id = 164156,
            score = 8,
            author = "vixis",
            text = "This has become even more difficult, for reasons other than Doyce stated above...\n\nPatch 2.2 came with the patch note \"Firewing Warlocks are now less likely to engage in melee combat.\" This causes a couple problems.\n\n1) You can no longer pull them seperately as a melee class, since they will cast instead of run to you. Instead, you have to run to them, and since they are 90% of the time in pairs, you will have to fight two of them.\n\n2) If Isla encounters a patrol, but only takes a couple hits from it, and she also happens to agro a Warlock at the same time, the Shadowbolt from the Warlock will cause her to agro on it, thus agroing that Warlocks teamate. Now she has 2 mobs on her, and if either of the Warlocks runs, you can easily have 3-4 mobs to fight at the same time.\n\nBasically I can only suggest you actually do this with one other person if possible.",
            date = "2007-10-07T09:00:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10052#comments:id=164156",
        },
        {
            id = 190616,
            score = 7,
            author = "mdfrancois",
            text = "After 2.3, this seems quite difficult to solo, as she pulls all the warlocks in the middle (or else I had very bad luck).  Bring a friend.",
            date = "2007-11-24T20:42:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10052#comments:id=190616",
        },
        {
            id = 494311,
            score = 7,
            author = "snuzzle",
            text = "I've solo'd this numerous times, but for some reason tonight she decided to be a true pain and aggro every single warlock in the center circle 2 by 2. She rooted the mobs so I couldn't AoE them, then just ran up to them and melee'd. It was like running the noobiest noob through WC. Just painful.",
            date = "2008-12-06T18:29:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10052#comments:id=494311",
        },
    },
