            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10109#comments:id=449122",
        },
        {
            id = 24725,
            score = 2,
            author = "javada",
            text = "Just be sure your at full health when you get rid of the slowfall buff because if you miss, it's a hard landing. I've seen pally's bubble themselves to do this. I died a couple of times trying. Eventually got it. The Matriach is a level 63 elite. Best bring a friend along to kill the bird.",
            date = "2007-01-25T22:59:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10109#comments:id=24725",
        },
    },
    [10110] = {
        {
            id = 91660,
            score = 29,
            author = "53461",
            text = "The Overlook is at 39,48.\nThe Stadium is at 35,50.\nBroken Hill is at 40,57.\n\nIt's only considered 'capturing' it if the bar was originally in the gray (neutral) area.",
            date = "2007-05-27T11:03:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10110#comments:id=91660",
        },
        {
            id = 103012,
            score = 23,
            author = "danter",
            text = "A friend of mine coldnt do this quest until he had done the quest:\n\nForward Base: Reaver's Fall (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10124)\n\nso I think it's maybe this quest you need to do in order to get this quest",
            date = "2007-06-12T10:21:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10110#comments:id=103012",
        },
        {
            id = 88829,
            score = 22,
            author = "Amoa",
            text = "This quest has changed in patch 2.1.\n\nIt is now a \"Daily PvP\", which means you can only complete is once a day.\n\nBut the rep you gain has increased. Now you gain 150 Rep each turn in, instead of 10.",
            date = "2007-05-23T20:09:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10110#comments:id=88829",
        },
        {
            id = 139537,
            score = 20,
            author = "yodadoe",
            text = "Since most servers seem to have more Ally's that Hordies, these things are almost always blue all of the time. Every time I have gone to capture them, Ally's come out of the woodwork. At first, I thought they were coming to kill me, but I quickly found that they just wanted to complete their version of this quest and were waiting for a Hordie to come turn the towers grey or red. I have yet to be attacked. It sure is spooky having a few 70's hovering over me waiting for me to leave, tho!",
            date = "2007-08-17T11:31:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10110#comments:id=139537",
        },
        {
            id = 931240,
            score = 18,
            author = "509205",
            text = "If you can't figure out how to capture them just sit next to a flag and wait til its captured. There is a bar on the right that tells you how far along the capturing has gotten. It takes a while lol so be patient. :)",
            date = "2009-12-29T02:32:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10110#comments:id=931240",
        },
    },
    [10111] = {
        {
            id = 21212,
            score = 211,
            author = "11862",
            text = "I got this done by getting the Jumpatron blowfall buff and jumping off the hill above the nest on an epic mount with spurs on my boots.  It dropped me right on the nest.",
            date = "2007-01-18T01:56:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10111#comments:id=21212",
        },
        {
            id = 19210,
            score = 81,
            author = "Lustral",
            text = "Use the Jump-a-tron 4000 next to Wazat to launch yourself into the air and land in the nest with the mysterious egg.  Using the Jump-a-tron gives you a 3 minute duration slow fall debuff, and the only practical way to land in the nest is to click it off once you're at the proper trajectory floating above it.\n\nOnce you interact with and take the egg, the matriarch will swoop down and is non-aggressive, ready to be killed.  I completed this quest with another warrior, and it was moderately difficult, though using taunt and bandaging properly made it reasonable to do.",
            date = "2007-01-03T14:39:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10111#comments:id=19210",
        },
        {
            id = 27135,
            score = 63,
            author = "Seregon",
            text = "People on my server had a hard time getting into the nest so here's a good trick:\n\nGet the slow-fall buff from the trampoline. Then mount up (epic mount only) and go up on the ridge a few yards south-east of the tree. If you time your jump good you should be able to float into the nest. It is doable without any speed spell on your mount, but it's piece of cake with stuff like \"Carrot on a stick\" or the \"Animal handler\" talent of the hunter.\n\nHere is a movie of me doing it:\nhttp://video.google.com/videoplay?docid=-4546574312878450602",
            date = "2007-01-29T12:51:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10111#comments:id=27135",
        },
        {
            id = 19430,
            score = 49,
            author = "3550",
            text = "You also want to make sure that you receive the message 'Mysterious Egg cracks open, filling the nest with yolk' before jumping out of the tree. While I received quest credit for attempting to steal the egg, the Matriarch did not spawn. I ended up having to jump back up and re-loot the egg two more times before she finally appeared.",
            date = "2007-01-05T04:50:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10111#comments:id=19430",
        },
        {
            id = 856953,
            score = 20,
            author = "463862",
            text = "Its possible to use a flying mount to land into the nest. Saves a LOT of trouble, especially since Blizz lowered the level requirements for flying training.",
            date = "2009-10-01T15:02:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10111#comments:id=856953",
        },
    },
