    [10132] = {
        {
            id = 6810,
            score = 37,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Get a group of 2-3 for this.  Colossals will spawn adds as their health depletes(up to 3 total).",
            date = "2006-12-05T22:49:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10132#comments:id=6810",
        },
        {
            id = 21965,
            score = 27,
            author = "12815",
            text = "Coords: (18.40) and surrounding area.\n\nSuggested group: 3 people although it can be done with 2. Perfect group: tank, healer, dps\n\nThese mobs summon non-elite adds (up to 3) as their health drops down. Once they are dead, they can be looted again with mining skill.\n\nTake care with agroing more mobs, move your target away from the area, since these elites wander around, and also Fel Reavers",
            date = "2007-01-20T07:47:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10132#comments:id=21965",
        },
        {
            id = 151094,
            score = 22,
            author = "Zellyn",
            text = "During this quest you will find a Crimson Crystal Shard (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=29476\") which is then turned in a few times and leads to Natural Remedies (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10351), but isn't technically a quest-chain because quests come from two different NPCs.",
            date = "2007-09-10T01:13:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10132#comments:id=151094",
        },
        {
            id = 297680,
            score = 21,
            author = "128231",
            text = "Well, I've been through HFP six times now on six different classes, so I figure I'll add my two cents in for those looking for information.  Seeing as how I like to come to WoWhead for information on quests like these to see if they are possible to solo with the class I am using, I figure I am not the only one, so hopefully this helps some people.\n\nRogue - When I came through on my Rogue at 61-62 it was during the release of TBC, so there were always people doing this quest.  I ended up doing it in a group for ease.  However, my Rogue was Combat Swords, so if he had to solo them, he probably could have if he waited for his cools between pulls.  Adrenaline Rush, Evasion and properly timed stuns make it possible to solo.\n\nMage - Couldn't solo this on my Mage, but that's because he was Fire spec.  The adds made it too much damage to live through.  Had he been Frost, I think there is a chance he could have done it by kiting them around and using the Water Elemental.\n\nShaman - My Shaman was able to solo this as Enhancement.  I used a Frost Shock and heal kiting method that worked to separate the mob from the adds as well as I Frost Shocked near the add spawn points and was far enough away that the adds did not aggro me.  If I got one, I dropped a Stoneclaw and continued.  Wasn't too bad.\n\nPaladin - Not too difficult as Protection.  Used a bit of Holy gear for mana and Consecrate and shield and I wasn't taking too much damage.  Mana is obviously the concern.\n\nWarlock - This quest is trivial as a Warlock, especially Affliction.  Neither the mob nor its adds are immune to fear.  Fear, DoT, kept a Voidwalker on it just in case fear broke at an add spawn point and the quest is done.  No problems.\n\nHunter - As a BM Hunter, this wasn't TOO bad.  Here's how I did it since I am not that big on my kiting skills.  I dropped a Freezing Trap, I sent my pet in, popped Beastial Wrath, Mend Pet and let her Growl twice.  I then popped my trinket (the one from the Overlord quest) and began using my Steady Shot/Auto Shot weave while keeping Mend Pet up.  The adds would aggro onto my pet at first, but heal aggro from Mend Pet would eventually pull to me.  One adds frozen, stepped away, dropped another and repeated.  Took a while, but they did do down.  Key is two things: Make good use of Feign Death to get the adds off you and ALWAYS keep Mend Pet ticking else the damage is too much to heal through.\n\nHere's how I spec'd my Cat for those interested:\n\nLevel 62, Loyalty Level 6 Cat\nGrowl Rank 7\nBite Rank 8\nClaw Rank 8\nDash Rank 3\nCobra Reflexes\nAvoidance Rank 2\nNatural Armor Rank 8\nGreat Stamina Rank 3\nRank 2 of all 5 Schools of Magic\n\nThat's it, hopefully this information helps some people!  Good luck, Have fun!",
            date = "2008-05-31T15:11:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10132#comments:id=297680",
        },
        {
            id = 24238,
            score = 16,
            author = "6833",
            text = "These can  be soloed as a feral dr00d. Just take care to kill the first two spawns as soon as they are there.\n\nMy strat:\n\nRoot the mob, cast moonfire, faerie fire. Regrowth/rejuv then bear charge into the mob and maul away.\n\nFirst add spawns at 70%, kill that straight away; 2k hp and should die fast.\n\nAfter that add was dead, carry on mauling/mangling away. If hp does run low - bash/root run away heal, hots whatever and go back in. Kill the 2nd add that spawns as fast as possible that should be around 45% hp.\n\nAfter that kill the mob till he's dead then kill the spawns after. One thing I did notice is when I CCed the last spawn with nature's grasp, and finished the mob off because my health was running low, was that the spawn despawned after maybe 10-15 seconds. It might be worth someone testing this to see if all spawns disappear after 10 seconds or so. :)\n\nIt's gonna be slow but they are soloable. Just be very careful where you pull, casting demo roar can pull a nearby mob to you and that is insta death for you. Move the mob to a clear area and you should have no problems at all.",
            date = "2007-01-25T07:25:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10132#comments:id=24238",
        },
    },
