            score = 226,
            author = "123744",
            text = "I originally posted this under Hero of the Mag'har, the former end of the chain.  Since this is the final quest I'll repost it here.  Please rate me up(original was up to +222)\n\nThis Quest Chain starts in Hellfire with The Assassin.   This requires you are able to speak to Nazgrel (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3230) which means you will have to have done at least some of the level 58 outland Quests*.\n\n1. The Assassin (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9400)\n2. A Strange Weapon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9401)\n3. The Warchief's Mandate (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9405)\n4. A Spirit Guide (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9410)\n5. The Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9406)\n6. Messenger to Thrall (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9438)\n7. Envoy to the Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9441)\n\nAlso given at this point are the following, but is not necessary to complete the Hero chain.  They are very nice rep rewards for each so you may want to do them since you’re there anyway.\n\n\0091. A Debilitating Sickness (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9442)\n2. Administering the Salve (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9447)\n\nThe next part leads you to Jorin Dead Eye  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18106) in Garadar, Nagrand.\n\n1. The Impotent Leader (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9888)\n2. Don't Kill the Fat One (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9889)\n3. Success! (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9890)\n4. Because Kilrath is a Coward (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9891)\n5. Message in a Battle (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9906)\n6. An Audacious Advance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9907)\n7. Diplomatic Measures (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10107)\n\nTakes you to Nagrand to Find Lantresor of the Blade  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18261) which gives you the Blademaster Chain\n\n1a. Armaments for Deception (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9928)\n1b. Ruthless Cunning (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9927)\n2a. Returning the Favor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9931)\n2b. Body Of Evidence (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9932)\n3.   Message to Garadar (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9934)\n\nYou will also need to complete The following Unrelated Quests.\n1. The Totem of Kar’dash  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9868)\n\nwhich is a simple escort quest beginning with the Mag'har Captive (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18210) in one of the buildings of Sunspring Post.\n\nThe second part involves Altruis the Sufferer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18417) who is right by the Mag’har captive so these are good quests to do together.\n\n1. Survey the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9991)\n2. Buying Time (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9999)\n3. The Master Planner (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10001)\n4. Patience and Understanding (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10004)\n5. Crackin' Some Skulls (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10009)\n6. It's Just That Easy? (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10010)\n7. Forge Camp: Annihilated (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10011)\n\nThis unlocks the final sequence which returns you to Garrosh  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18063).  He sends you finally to visit Greatmother Geyah  (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18141).\n\n1. A Visit With the Greatmother (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10044)\n2. Material Components (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10045)\n3. To Meet Mother Kashur (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10081)\n4. The Agitated Ancestors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10082)\n5. A Visit With The Ancestors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10085)\n6. When Spirits Speak (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10101)\n7. A Secret Revealed (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10102)\n8. Auchindoun... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10167)\n9. What the Soul Sees (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10168)\n10. Return to the Greatmother (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10170)\n11. The Inconsolable Chieftain (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10171)\n12. There Is No Hope (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10172)   (new ending)\n\n13. Thrall, Son of Durotan (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10175)\n14. Hero of the Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10212)\n\nCongrats on you Uber new Gear and Exalted Rep.\n\nSmall disclaimer.  This is a compilation from a lot of peoples work using information from Allakazam (http://wow.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?source=live;wquest=10212), Wowhead  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10212), WoWWiki  (http://www.wowwiki.com/Geyah), and the Armory  (http://www.wowarmory.com/item-info.xml?i=28175).  This took many hours to complete since the info was so scattered so please rate me up if possible.\n\nRaimi, 70 Undead Warlock,\nTitianna 70 Belf Priest\nHeghbathl 70 Belf Tankadin\nSentinals\n*\n1. Through the Dark Portal  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9407)\n2. Arrival in Outland  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10120)\n3. Journey to Thrallmar  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10289)\n4. Report to Nazgrel  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10291)\n5. Eradicate the Burning Legion  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10121)\n6. Felspark Ravine  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10123)\n7. Forward Base: Reaver's Fall  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10124)\n8. Disrupt Their Reinforcements (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10208)\n9. Mission: Gateways Murketh and Shaadraz (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10129)\n10. Mission: The Abyssal Shelf  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10162)",
            date = "2010-12-29T13:36:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10172#comments:id=1266060",
        },
        {
            id = 1164121,
            score = 118,
            author = "336987",
            text = "*War drums echo in the distance.\nThrall yells: At long last, I am home...\n\n(About 6 minutes later)\n\nThrall says: Greatmother...\n\nGreatmother Geyah says: I have been expecting you, young one. Come closer - my eyes are not as sharp as they once were.\nGreatmother Geyah says: Yes, you move like my son. You have his broad shoulders - ahh, and your mother's fierce eyes.\n\nThrall says: Greatmother...Am I...\n\nGreatmother Geyah says: There is no doubt - you are the heir of Durotan... my grandson. Draka told me she was with child before she and your father left our world, but I never dared dream that they would survive...\n\nThrall says: They... did not, Greatmother. They were killed shortly after I was born. I never knew them. I was raised as a slave. To this day, I carry the name of Thrall.\n\nGreatmother Geyah says: Thrall? You've been a slave only to the past, grandson! But no more! When last I saw him, Durotan told me the name he would give his unborn son... He was... so proud...\n*Greatmother Geyah wipes a tear away.\nGreatmother Geyah says: Go'el. You are Go'el, son of Durotan - rightful chieftain of the Frostwolves. This day, grandson - you are the great joy of my heart.\n\nThrall says: I have dreamed of this moment all my life, Greatmother. 'Till now, all I've had were Orgrim's stories about my parents and their adventures on Draenor. He was my greatest teacher and dearest friend. He died a hero... They all died as heroes - and for all of them, a song of honor remains.\n\nGreatmother Geyah says: I see that you hold the Doomhammer. Have all of our greatest heroes fallen, grandson?\n\nThrall says: They died honorably, Greatmother.\nGreatmother Geyah says: What of Grommash? What of Hellscream?\n\nThrall says: He died our greatest hero. It was Grom who freed us all... I was by his side when he struck down Mannoroth and ended the curse forever.\n\nGreatmother Geyah says: Blessed spirits! For twenty years, all we knew was that Grom was the first to drink from the cursed chalice and bring damnation down upon our people... It is the only truth his son, Garrosh has ever known.\n\nGreatmother Geyah says: Grandson, will you... Will you tell Garrosh what you have told me about his father?\n\nThrall says: Tell him? Greatmother, that boy's father died so that all of us could live free of the blood curse. I will tell him nothing. I will show him! Show him and any that would doubt Hellscream's resolve exactly what Grom Hellscream did for all orcs!\nThrall says: Please excuse me, Greatmother. I will return soon.\n\n(Thrall walks down to Garrosh, then leads him to the spirit circle)\n\nThrall yells: Spirits give me strength! Take from my soul these old wounds and expose them for all to see! Let this child know his father! Let these people know their savior!\n\n(Thrall summons a sort of miniature version of the fight with Mannoroth in the spirit circle)\n\n*Mannoroth laughs.\nMannoroth says: So predictable. I knew you would come. And I see you've brought the mighty Hellscream.\nMannoroth says: His blood is mine, as is your whole misbegotten race.\nThrall roars in defiance.\n\n(Mannoroth strikes down Thrall)\n\nMannoroth says: A worthy effort, but futile.\n*Mannoroth laughs.\nMannoroth says: The boy believed you could be saved, but he didn't know what burns within your soul when in your heart, you know we are the same.\n\nGrom Hellscream says: NOOOO!\n\n(Hellscream and Mannoroth strike each other down, Thrall gets back up)\n\nGrom Hellscream says: Thrall... The blood haze has lifted.\n*Grom's eyes go dim as the blood curse is lifted.\nGrom Hellscream says: The demon's fire has burnt out in my veins. I have... freed myself.\n\nThrall says: No, old friend. You've freed us all...\n\nGarrosh collapses.\nGarrosh says: For my entire life I have thought my bloodline cursed. I have lived beneath the shadow of my father's greatest failure.\nGarrosh says: I hated him for what he had done. I hated him for the burden he left me. But now...\nGarrosh says: You have shown me truths that I would have never known. You and your allies have gifted me with something that cannot bear a price: Redemption. Thrall, redeemer of the Mag'har, you honor me as none ever have...\nGarrosh says: On this day, a great burden has been lifted from my chest. My heart swells with pride. And for the first time, I can proudly proclaim who I am. I can finally unleash the fury in my heart.\nGarrosh yells: I am Garrosh Hellscream, son of Grom, chieftain of the Mag'har! Let the battle call of Hellscream give you courage and strength! Be lifted by my rallying cry.\n\n(Everyone gets Hellscream's Warsong buff)\n\nGarrosh says: Thank you, son of Durotan.\n\nThrall places a hand on Garrosh's shoulder.\nThrall says: You need not thank me, Garrosh. Your father was a brother to me. I would do anything for you and the Mag'har. I must now return to the Greatmother.\n\n(Thrall walks back to the Greatmother)\n\nThrall says: I have returned, Greatmother. Garrosh has found his heart and his fury.",
            date = "2010-11-07T01:43:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10172#comments:id=1164121",
        },
        {
            id = 1911154,
            score = 80,
            author = "Bonelich",
            text = "\"I cannot become the second Hellscream to damn the orcs.\"\n\nYeah, sure.",
            date = "2013-10-22T14:44:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10172#comments:id=1911154",
        },
        {
            id = 764094,
            score = 44,
            author = "entropicdragon",
            text = "Speaking to Greatmother Geyah (spoiler alert!)\n\nWhat did Garrosh tell you, ?\n\nGarrosh is beyond redemption, Greatmother. I fear that in helping the Mag'har, I have convinced Garrosh that he is unfit to lead.\n\nI can no longer fight the spirits, . My time has long since passed. Once again, I must thank you for all that you have done. While Garrosh may be unmovable, many of my people have been lifted by your accomplishments. They are now willing to fight for our rights as a united clan.\n\nI have done all that I could, Greatmother. I thank you for your kind words.\n\nYou remind me of my son, .\n\nHe was an immovable mountain: A pillar of strength and honor.\n\nHe sacrificed himself so that we could survive. So that generations of orcs after him could be born into a world without the blood curse... Without Gul'dan and his dark Horde...\n\nOh Durotan, how I wish that you could be here. Your people so desperately need you...\n\nGreatmother, you are the mother of Durotan?\n\nDid you know my son?\n\nGreatmother, I never had the honor. Durotan died long before my time, but his heroics are known to all on my world. The orcs of Azeroth reside in a place known as Durotar, named after your son. And...\n\nYes...\n\nIt is my warchief, Greatmother. The leader of my people. From my world. He... He is the son of Durotan. He is your grandchild.\n\nI... I... Durotan survived to have a child? The child Draka told me of before they left... It was their greatest fear... To raise a child in this world. On the other side of that gate was their only hope. I dared not tell Durotan, but secretly, I begged the spirits to watch over them - to protect their child and to give them strength.\n\nI... I must see my grandchild. I must see him. Please, I am too weak. You must tell him. Before I leave this world...\n\nI will return to Azeroth at once, Greatmother.",
            date = "2009-07-01T01:28:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10172#comments:id=764094",
        },
        {
            id = 1144862,
            score = 23,
            author = "Shadowajohn",
            text = "As of the current patch, the quest line seems to end here.\nThe rewards seem to be the same as The Hero of Mag'har (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10212), with the difference of 2000 Mag'har rep.",
            date = "2010-10-17T00:12:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10172#comments:id=1144862",
        },
