            score = 124,
            author = "InfinityX",
            text = "This has to be one of the most interesting solo quests in the Burning Crusade.\n\nWhen you start the quest, Doctor Vomisa gives you the Scrap Reaver Controller. When used, you'll gain the Scrap Reaver X6000 under your control, just like a hunter or warlock pet (not direct control, like Mind Control). The Scrap Reaver has three abilities at your disposal. All three abilities are on a linked 10 second cooldown. One ability is a two second stun, which isn't nearly as useful as the other 2 abilities in almost all situations. The second ability is called \"Smash\" (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=34618). It deals a large amount of instant damage, and causes a very large amount of threat, as the tooltip describes. You should use this as soon as the fight starts to be sure you or any allies you have helping you do not get aggro from Negatron. He hits extremely hard and should only be tanked by the Scrap Reaver. The Reaver's last ability is a self-heal, named \"Repair\" (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=34619). It heals 10,000 damage over 10 seconds (1000 per second), regardless of the odd/buggy tooltip. This ability should be used early, and not as a last resort after your Reaver is low on health. Be aware that Negatron has a 75% healing effect reduction ability called \"Demolish.\" Try to time your repairs when your Reaver is not afflicted by Demolish.\n\nThis quest will take a few tries, so don't get frustrated if you aren't able to complete it at first. It's a decent challenge, but just be patient and get a feel for when to use your Reaver's abilities. Be sure not to walk too far away from Vomisa's console, or you'll lose control of the Scrap Reaver and Negatron will make a beeline to you, and he is much faster than players on foot.",
            date = "2006-12-03T20:49:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10248#comments:id=5468",
        },
        {
            id = 2252076,
            score = 121,
            author = "wowhead100",
            text = "The proving grounds are at 37, 63.  The quest isn't marked correctly on the mini map.",
            date = "2015-09-13T20:18:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10248#comments:id=2252076",
        },
        {
            id = 27561,
            score = 40,
            author = "18085",
            text = "Very easy if you have Improved Leader of the Pack, since the pet gets it as well.  I only looked once near the end but I think ILotP heals it for 2400 or so everytime it crits.",
            date = "2007-01-30T03:40:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10248#comments:id=27561",
        },
        {
            id = 32935,
            score = 35,
            author = "21871",
            text = "sadly for hunters we cant use our normal pet! also DO NOT FEIGN DEATH!! the robot well despawn and you'll have to start over again. i love this quest great fun!!:)",
            date = "2007-02-09T02:26:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10248#comments:id=32935",
        },
    },
    [10249] = {
        {
            id = 2336769,
            score = 63,
            author = "albinoette",
            text = "Mini-Guide for https://www.wowhead.com/item=134021 (Legion toy), previously https://www.wowhead.com/item=30847 (head armor).\n\nRewarded from https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249, the final quest in a 7-part quest chain, all taking place in Netherstorm, Outland.\n\nIf you have destroyed your helmet:\nAs of 6.2.3, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19570 has the dialog option: \"Chief, I've somehow misplaced my X-52 Rocket Helmet!\" to which he replies \"Well, alright then, there you go, First Officer . Just try to be more careful with your helmet in the future. Those things don't grow on trees, you know!\" and gives you a new helmet.\n[hr]\nIf you cannot get the initial quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10333 from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19645, you need to complete these pre-quests:\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10265 from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19880 which, once complete, will let you pick up  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10206 from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19645.\n[hr]\nAnd now you can...\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10333 - Fly to Eco-Dome Midrealm and talk to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19728 at 46.63 56.53. (map (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19728/mama-wheeler#map))\nShe will offer https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10234.\n - Collect https://www.wowhead.com/object=183935 at The Scrap Fields, just southeast of Mama at/around 49.27 59.77. (map (http://www.wowhead.com/object=183935/fel-reaver-part#map)) Be warned if you are doing this quest at level: the surrounding mobs have a dynamite attack at low health.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10235\n - Obtain https://www.wowhead.com/item=28563 from killing/looting https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19738 to the east at 50.69 57.19. (map (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19738/doomclaw#map))\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10237 - Return to Area 52 and speak to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19570 under the rocket at 32.72 64.97. (map (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19570/rocket-chief-fuselage#map))\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10247 - Speak with https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19832 at 37.27 63.69. (map (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19832/doctor-vomisa-ph-t#map))\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10248 (At level: Suggested Players [3].)\n - It appears you cannot do this quest if someone outside your party is already on it, as I was given the error \"Requires Uncontrolled Scrap Reaver X6000\" while someone else was controlling one.\n- Soon after using the provided https://www.wowhead.com/item=28634, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19851 (69 elite) will start running at you from the location marked on your minimap (near the bridge around 40.48 62.61). He stops just outside Doctor Vomisha's camp at 37.72 63.46. Watch for him to come running.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249 - Return to Area 52 and speak to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19570 who has moved slightly north of the rocket at 32.69 64.42. (map (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19570/rocket-chief-fuselage#map))\n\n[hr]\nCongratulations on your new X-52 Rocket Helmet!\n[hr]\nRazerWolf came up with a great macro here (http://www.wowhead.com/item=30847/x-52-rocket-helmet#comments:id=223483) (will need to be tested once this item is a toy instead of a helm), that simulates a problem with your mount (/panic /emote slams the ejector button!) and ejects you (/dismount /use X-52 Rocket Helmet). He/She also notes that \"the Parachute effect only works to the height you blasted off from, so if you're too high up you might still kill yourself.\"\n[hr]",
            date = "2016-06-03T17:31:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249#comments:id=2336769",
        },
        {
            id = 194816,
            score = 58,
            author = "8244",
            text = "An awesome quest line, ultimately ending in a \"cool\" rocket helm. :)\n\nThe rocket helm won't save you from things really, but it is alot of fun to go to Shatt with some friends that have the helms, & get in a big group & all take off at the same time. :)\n\nProps to Blizz for a worthwhile toy item & a decent story driven quest series.\n\nOh yea, first! :P",
            date = "2007-12-02T10:04:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249#comments:id=194816",
        },
        {
            id = 1072231,
            score = 13,
            author = "Little",
            text = "Heh. \"I could just kiss you... but I won't.\" Goblins ^^",
            date = "2010-07-03T16:43:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249#comments:id=1072231",
        },
        {
            id = 1596137,
            score = 4,
            author = "250843",
            text = "For those looking to transmog the X-52 Rocket Helmet it won't let you. :(\nThe may change this is a future patch but a doubt it.",
            date = "2011-12-14T15:56:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249#comments:id=1596137",
        },
        {
            id = 2298624,
            score = -1,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YgRdVsbsnfw\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10249, from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19832 at coords 37.2, 63.8.\n•\009Travel west, to Area 52, to coords 32.6, 64.4.\n•\009Turn in the quest to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19570.",
            date = "2016-01-15T16:26:39-06:00",
