    [10277] = {
        {
            id = 110220,
            score = 176,
            author = "6918",
            text = "Confirmed, AFK at the quest-giver for 9min and you'll get credit when your tour guide finishes the circle.",
            date = "2007-06-24T06:11:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10277#comments:id=110220",
        },
        {
            id = 198472,
            score = 91,
            author = "26532",
            text = "Here's a transcript of what the Custodian of Time (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=19950) whispers to you as you take your tour:\n\nGreetings, .  I will guide you through the cavern. Please try and keep up.\n\nWe do not know if the Caverns of Time have always been accessible to mortals.  Truly, it is impossible to tell as the Timeless One is in perpetual motion, changing our timeways as he sees fit.  What you see now may very well not exist tomorrow.  You may wake up and have no memory of this place.\n\nIt is strange, I know... Most mortals cannot actually comprehend what they see here, as often, what they see is not anchored within their own perception of reality.\n\nFollow me, please.\n\nThere are only two truths to be found here: First, that time is chaotic, always in flux, and completely malleable and second, perception does not dictate reality.\n\nAs custodians of time, we watch over and care for Nozdormu's (http://www.wowwiki.com/Nozdormu) realm.  The master is away at the moment, which means that attempts are being made to dramatically alter time.  The master never meddles in the affairs of mortals but instead corrects the alterations made to time by others.  He is reactionary in this regard.\n\nFor normal maintenance of time, the Keepers of Time (http://www.wowhead.com/?faction=989) are sufficient caretakers.  We are able to deal with most ordinary disturbances.  I speak of little things, such as rogue mages changing something in the past to elevate their status or wealth in the present.\n\nThese tunnels that you see are called timeways.  They are infinite in number.  The ones that currently exist in your reality are what the master has deemed as 'trouble spots.' These trouble spots may differ completely in theme but they always share a cause.  That is, their existence is a result of the same temporal disturbance.  Remember that should you venture inside one...\n\nThis timeway is in great disarray!  We have agents inside right now attempting to restore order.  What information I have indicates that Thrall's (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=17876) freedom is in jeopardy.  A malevolent organization known as the Infinite Dragonflight (http://www.wowwiki.com/Infinite_Dragonflight) is trying to prevent his escape.  I fear without outside assistance, all will be lost.\n\nFollow me, please.\n\nWe have very little information on this timeway.  Sa'at (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=20201) has been dispatched and is currently inside.  The data we have gathered from his correspondence is that the Infinite Dragonflight are once again attempting to alter time.  Could it be that the opening of the Dark Portal (http://www.wowwiki.com/Dark_Portal) is being targeted for sabotage?  Let us hope not...\n\nFollow me, please.\n\nThis timeway is currently collapsing.  What that may hold for the past, present and future is currently unknown...\n\nThe timeways are currently ranked in order from least catastrophic to most catastrophic.  Note that they are all classified as catastrophic, meaning that any single one of these timeways collapsing would mean that your world would end.  We only classify them in such a way so that the heroes and adventurers that are sent here know which timeway best suits their abilities.\n\nFollow me, please.\n\nAll we know of this timeway is that it leads to Mount Hyjal.  The Infinite Dragonflight have gone to great lengths to prevent our involvement.  We know next to nothing, mortal.  Soridormi (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=19935) is currently attempting to break through the timeway's defenses but has thus far been unsuccessful.  You might be our only hope of breaking through and resolving the conflict.\n\nFollow me, please.\n\nOur time is at an end .  I would wish you luck, if such a thing existed.",
            date = "2007-12-09T10:57:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10277#comments:id=198472",
        },
        {
            id = 14370,
            score = 52,
            author = "9110",
            text = "The Caverns Of Time is protected by the Bronze Dragonflight which cannot let mortals interrupt the timeline so thats why the doors were closed, but a new race of dragon flight named the Infinite Dragonflight has been interrupting the time flow in the caverns. The Bronze Dragonflight is recruiting adventurers to make sure all past events occur the way they should.\n\nAs of what I have heard, the instances will be as followed:\n\nOld Hillsbrad - help Thrall escape from Durnholde keep.\nBlack Morass - protect Medivh as he opens the Dark Portal.\nOld Hyjal - Fight Archimonde atop Mount Hyjal.",
            date = "2006-12-12T18:35:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10277#comments:id=14370",
        },
        {
            id = 487058,
            score = 48,
            author = "estroBiologist",
            text = "\"Don't do anything that affects anything. Unless it turns out you were supposed to do it, in which case for the love of God. Don't not do it!\"\n-Professor Hubert Farnsworth, regarding Time Travel",
            date = "2008-12-03T10:56:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10277#comments:id=487058",
        },
        {
            id = 647475,
            score = 46,
            author = "Heliotrope",
            text = "There should be a meta-achievement for finishing all of the instances here that rewards a DeLorean mount.",
            date = "2009-03-19T01:17:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10277#comments:id=647475",
        },
    },
    [10278] = {
        {
            id = 24103,
            score = 49,
            author = "15480",
            text = "The location is correct. However, what to do once you get there is a bit foggy....\n\n\"Use my unstable warp rift generator in the Warp Fields to create a warp rift\"\n\nHowever, you have to rightclick on the generator, and then on the GROUND below the warp fields, not ON them. Hover your mouse on the ground under one of the rifts, and you will get a targeting cursor that turns green when you are in range, and is red if you are not. Click when you are in range, and some more voidwalkers will spawn.\n\nThe ones that spawn as a result of clicking on the ground will contains the quest item, with a seemingly 100% drop rate.",
            date = "2007-01-25T00:08:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10278#comments:id=24103",
        },
        {
            id = 21013,
            score = 23,
            author = "3182",
            text = "I found it 52, 84",
            date = "2007-01-17T10:04:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10278#comments:id=21013",
        },
        {
            id = 97852,
            score = 7,
            author = "58687",
            text = "You get an item (Unstable Warp Rift Generator) in your backpack when you accept the quest. Use this item aroud loc:45,80 and kill the 'Unstable Voidwalker' it will make spawn.\n\nloc: 45,80 on the map is approx 1 inch west of expedition Armory in Hellfire Peninsula.",
            date = "2007-06-04T06:53:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10278#comments:id=97852",
        },
        {
            id = 187405,
            score = 5,
            author = "4139",
            text = "Im a pack rack so about 90% of the time my bags are full. Anyways, just a warning you can not complete the quest if you destroy the generator, i figured since I had the 3 i would delete it when I was doing the other voidwalker quest and saw my inventory was full for that item. When I collected the 10 items and went back to complete, yeah you need the gen, now im omw back to do this quest again :)",
            date = "2007-11-19T03:14:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10278#comments:id=187405",
        },
        {
            id = 278167,
            score = 3,
            author = "15813",
            text = "Combine this quest with http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9351 as you can do both in the same area",
            date = "2008-04-27T07:32:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10278#comments:id=278167",
        },
    },
    [10279] = {
        {
            id = 30146,
            score = 59,
            author = "5027",
            text = "When you accept the quest, make sure you are not mounted. I was, got a dumb error message and have had a pain trying to do it now because of the problems this caused.\n\nNot mounted!",
            date = "2007-02-03T16:20:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10279#comments:id=30146",
        },
        {
            id = 6277,
            score = 21,
            author = "Toloran",
            text = "This quest chain is required to be able to do the caverns of time instance/events. You can't do the first one (Thralls Escape) without doing this quest. The second one, The Opening of the Dark Portal, cannot be done without doing the Thrall event. So in other words, you have to do this chain to even visit the CoT instances. :(\n\nAt level 60, you can't even see the greyed out exclemation point above the quest-giver.",
            date = "2006-12-05T14:05:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10279#comments:id=6277",
        },
        {
            id = 41126,
            score = 9,
            author = "fletch",
            text = "I was confused.. here is a more clear picture what to do.\n\nFollow me, please.\n\nFly/summon to Tanaris or COT. Go in front, you'll see a 'friendly' dragon inside the tunnel. Talk to it, get a quest.\n\nThen run/ride all way down to bottom, you'll see a glowing circle with 2 kids there. That's the boy you need to speak to.",
            date = "2007-02-23T13:34:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10279#comments:id=41126",
        },
        {
            id = 871569,
            score = 9,
            author = "407514",
            text = "Once you complete this quest can you still get a ride to the bottom?",
            date = "2009-10-20T13:28:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10279#comments:id=871569",
        },
        {
            id = 1007834,
            score = 8,
            author = "Missigno",
            text = "Even with the Dungeon Finder; you still need to do this quest.\n\nSo \"Escape from Durnholde Keep\" will be locked at least until lvl 66.",
            date = "2010-03-29T11:16:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10279#comments:id=1007834",
        },
    },
    [10280] = {
        {
            id = 34024,
            score = 174,
            author = "3316",
            text = "Big big big quest line!\n\n1. Assisting the Consortium [Level 68] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10264, a 'go talk to' quest\n2. Consortium Crystal Collection [Level 69] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10265, kill a dreadlord called Pentatharon and get a crystal from him\n3. A Heap of Ethereals [Level 68] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10262 , repeatable quest also for Consortium reputation.\n4. Warp-Raider Nesaad [Level 69] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10205, a go-kill-him quest.\n5. Request for Assistance [Level 69] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10266 , find Gahruj at 47,57\n6. Rightful Repossession [Level 69] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10267 , get 10 boxes from around Mana Forge: Duro\n7. An Audience with the Prince [Level 69] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10268 , Nexus-Prince Haramad at 44,35 or so in the Stormspire.\n8. Triangulation Point One [Level 69] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10269 , use the Triangulation Device at 66, 33\n9. Triangulation Point Two [Level 70] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10275 , same thing at 28,41\n10. Full Triangle [Level 70] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10276 , Find Culuthas at 53, 21, 70 Elite demon.\n11. Special Delivery to Shattrath [Level 70] : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10280 , pretty obvious.\n\nFollow-up for key to Arcatraz",
            date = "2007-02-11T10:06:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10280#comments:id=34024",
        },
        {
            id = 2009091,
            score = 131,
            author = "Gershuun",
            text = "If you accidentally one shot all of the blood elf party, Image of Nexus-Prince Haramad will respawn with the next part of the quest chain in about 8 minutes.",
            date = "2014-10-01T22:32:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10280#comments:id=2009091",
        },
        {
            id = 120373,
            score = 46,
            author = "51610",
            text = "Rogue does the quest, but does not turn it in with A'dal. Rogue gets permanent port to shatt from stormspire. Rogue hearths in Stormspire and is always first to the summon stone plus has easy access to socrethar's place for mining and herb farming.\n\nRogue is happy.",
            date = "2007-07-14T03:44:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10280#comments:id=120373",
        },
        {
            id = 28435,
            score = 21,
            author = "2349",
            text = "Prereq: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10276",
            date = "2007-01-31T17:14:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10280#comments:id=28435",
        },
        {
            id = 151051,
            score = 17,
            author = "73207",
            text = "When you complete this quest you are given the buff Blessing of A'dal (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=35076) which is one of the best buffs I've ever seen.\nToo bad you can only get it once. (lasts for 2h)",
            date = "2007-09-09T22:18:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10280#comments:id=151051",
        },
    },
    [10281] = {
        {
            id = 23026,
            score = 12,
            author = "14145",
            text = "Coords: 71,35\nLeads to \"Troublesome Distractions\"\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10273",
            date = "2007-01-23T00:00:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10281#comments:id=23026",
        },
        {
            id = 162975,
            score = 12,
            author = "91707",
            text = "\"Tyri\" is actually a blue dragonkin by the name of Tyrygosa, depicted in the Sunwell Trilogy by Richard A. Knaak.\n\nShe is a fond of her good looks, and wanted to be a Night Elf female when transformed, because \"elves are at least aesthetically attractive\", as she so approriately put it.\n\nShe is the fiancee of Kalegcos, a young blue dragonkin who is trapped in human form due to a magical neck chain made by Dar'Khan, a deceptive blood elf. Kalegcos possesses tremendous amounts of magic, and although his human form refrains him from practicing most of it, he can still do some cool stuff, e.g. make a sword out of thin air.",
            date = "2007-10-04T18:22:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10281#comments:id=162975",
        },
        {
            id = 46876,
            score = 6,
            author = "1822",
            text = "Confirming coordinates with slightly more accurate ones.\n\n71.2, 35.1",
            date = "2007-03-06T02:29:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10281#comments:id=46876",
        },
        {
            id = 282253,
            score = 5,
            author = "143861",
            text = "For those of us without a coordinate mod, don't take the path back north, just turn directly north of her image and she is just a short run away.",
            date = "2008-05-04T13:27:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10281#comments:id=282253",
        },
        {
            id = 2298442,
            score = 1,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dtaAbN-L-kc\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10281\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10281, from the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20154 at coords 70.8, 38.8 (Celestial Ridge).\n•\009Travel north to coords 71.2, 35.2.\n•\009Turn in the quest to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20110.",
            date = "2016-01-15T14:41:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10281#comments:id=2298442",
        },
    },
    [10282] = {
        {
            id = 42806,
            score = 78,
            author = "6460",
            text = "In Old Hillsbrad despite it is only 7 years ago you see Whitemane and several other bosses from SM as young children.   Apparently we've been fighting kids in SM this whole time.  Even adding 7 years to what they look like in Old Hillsbrad none of the bosses in SM should even be legally able to drink in the U.S.\n\nI can't believe a 14-year old wiped my whole party.   :-(",
            date = "2007-02-26T14:08:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10282#comments:id=42806",
        },
        {
            id = 14469,
            score = 42,
            author = "9110",
            text = "Old Hillsbrad is the first instance you are allowed to enter in the caverns and is very insightful as to warcraft lore. If you go to the southshore inn you will hear a story of the origins of Ashbringer. But mainly, Old Hillsbrad is for rescueing Thrall from the orc internment camp known as Durnholde Keep. If you do not rescue him, the world will cease to exist.",
            date = "2006-12-12T21:52:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10282#comments:id=14469",
        },
        {
            id = 24395,
            score = 42,
            author = "3500",
            text = "Prereq:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10277\n\nFollowup:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10283",
            date = "2007-01-25T12:44:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10282#comments:id=24395",
        },
        {
            id = 95887,
            score = 41,
            author = "57972",
            text = "If you are looking to get out of the instance, for whatever reason, you need to go where the Yeti caves are. It is directly north from southshore and west of tarren mills.",
            date = "2007-06-02T09:50:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10282#comments:id=95887",
        },
        {
            id = 1059352,
            score = 23,
            author = "423524",
            text = "OK, I read through several of the notes and still could not figure out what I needed to do to run this instance. I pretty much had to figure it out on my own and since I did, I figured why not let everyone else know in a simple and easy way how to do this. How thoughtful of me :)\n\nA quick note before getting started with this instance, I've been doing Loremaster for awhile now so I'm not sure if there are any prerequsite quests for [Nice Hat...] but if there isn't you wanna grab this before doing this instance. Pretty easy fight just tank and spank Don Carlos and he drops dead leaving you his hat. You get the quest in Gadgetzan from none other than Don Carlos and also turn it in to him, how clever.\n\n#1 Get the quests needed to do the instance. [Old Hillsbrad] starts the chain of quests for the instance. \"Andormu\" gives the quest she/he is just outside of the entrance to the instance.\n\n#2 OK this part was very confusing to me because no one explained it in a straight forward manner in all the notes I could find for the 2nd quest. As soon as you enter the instance you'll meet up with \"Erozion.\" You hand in the 1st quest to him [Old Hillsbrad] and then accept the 2nd one [Taretha's Diversion]. If you read what \"Erozion\" says then this part really isn't too hard to understand but when you're workin towards Loremaster you usually don't take too much time for that.\n\n#3 OK, so you accepted [Taretha's Diversion] now talk to \"Erozion\" again and tell him you're ready then he tells you to ride \"Brazen\" to Durnehold Keep. Now talk to \"Brazen\" to ride him/her to Durnehold Keep. Gratz! You've dicovered what took me an hour to do.\n\n#4 Now there are some tough mobs, lvl 63 elites all through out this place so be prepared. You'll want pots, good heals and a decent tank, or just be an epic geared 80 DK, this works too.\n\n#5 \"Erozion\" gives you some neat little bomb thingys to place inside of some barrels in the prison holding cells [Internment Lodges]. The barrels that you are supposed to place the bombs in will stick out and be a bit richer in color than the other barrels in the area. It has been noted that if there are people in your group that have completed this quest before that they can not place the bombs in them selves because it will glitch and not work properly. I don't know if the problem still exists as I soloed this, so to be on the safe side have only those who have not completed the quest do this errand.\n\n#6 AFTER all 5 Bombs are placed then go into the basement of Durnehold Keep and speak with \"Thrall\" turn in the quest [Taretha's Diversion] to him. Then accept the quest [Escape From Durnehold] from him.\n\n#7 [Escape From Durnehold] is an Escort quest, if this was not previously known now it is. Thrall doesn't waste any time getting his Orc booty outta Durnehold Keep, if ya know what I mean. So you definitely need a group if you're only lvls 63-72 or so. Bring pots because if healers run outta mana it's going to be a wipe.\n\n#8 Basically you'll have a one boss on the way to Tarren Mill, just be ready. It's pretty much tank and spank with these bosses. The action gets pretty thick once you get back to Tarren Mill and the attacks start up again. So save pot cd's for those last battles. There's a little time for cd renewal from Durnehold Keep to Tarren Mill so you can pot on the 1st main boss. The last boss is a fairly decent fight still tank and spank style combat but the dragon thing has alot of hp around 100k, so be ready.\n\n#9 Hand in the quest [Escape From Durnehold] to the old Wizard guy (Erozion) after he mourns about Taretha having to be teleported to some other dimension or something like that. He then gives you the last quest [Return To Andormu] which is simple enough to do as the title explains it all. Just exit the instance by goin to the old Yeti caves and continuing until you leave the instance. Upon exiting you will see Andormu waiting to give you your well earned reward.",
            date = "2010-06-16T20:01:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10282#comments:id=1059352",
        },
    },
    [10286] = {
        {
            id = 23269,
            score = 72,
            author = "12690",
            text = "I found this guy immediately outside of Falcon Watch. Guess I got lucky. You can see a map of his path here:\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?npc=20159\n\nHe didn't attack me, he just gave the quest straight to me.",
            date = "2007-01-23T13:03:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10286#comments:id=23269",
        },
        {
            id = 39300,
            score = 42,
            author = "Bunneh",
            text = "Be aware that attacking this guy for this quest will flag you for PvP on PvE servers.",
            date = "2007-02-20T11:49:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10286#comments:id=39300",
        },
        {
            id = 23957,
            score = 30,
            author = "15289",
            text = "I found him right outside Falcon Watch.\n\nWARNING: He doesn't have a ? over his head, so you have to look at his name. Go up to him and talk to him, and after you talk he'll dismount and attack you.\n\nOnce you get him to 20% (it's an easy fight), he'll give you the next quest in the chain.",
            date = "2007-01-24T19:01:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10286#comments:id=23957",
        },
        {
            id = 929447,
            score = 18,
            author = "468228",
            text = "if you have quest helper don't pay any attention to the question mark on Falcon Watch just follow the road to Zangarmarsh he will be on there somewhere.",
            date = "2009-12-26T23:59:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10286#comments:id=929447",
        },
        {
            id = 2506264,
            score = 11,
            author = "Aerynsun8449",
            text = "Not that I have any confidence Blizzard will do anything about this, however. Why DOES this quest flag us pvp? There is no action being taken against the alliance. It's a Horde NPC that attacks us. It's not even a player versus a player, it's a player versus a computer generated NPC (hence the NPC). This isn't the only time this has happened either. I believe a quest in Stonetalon Mountains does the same thing, NPC attacks us and we're flagged pvp. Why? There isn't a player versus a player involved.",
            date = "2017-07-05T20:47:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10286#comments:id=2506264",
        },
    },
    [10287] = {
        {
            id = 60992,
            score = 28,
            author = "danyjr",
            text = "First go buy the alcoholic beverage is in Zangarmarsh, Cenarion Refuge at the inkeeper Coryth Stoktron http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18907, the item is called Cenarion Spirits http://www.wowhead.com/?item=29112. The NPC to turn it into is right in the middle of the lower part of Falcon Watch (called: Viera Sunwhisper http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=17226). Give the beverage to her, walk down the path and use the scroll on her (she will turn into a rat!)\n\nNote: If the NPC is not there, it's because somebody else is doing the quest currently",
            date = "2007-04-02T10:38:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10287#comments:id=60992",
        },
        {
            id = 292433,
            score = 13,
            author = "124958",
            text = "If you happen to be on a PvE Realm when you talk to Aledis, make sure you are close to Falcon Watch [Or no high levels are around]. It immediately puts you into PvP leading to a possible attack if opposite faction is nearby.",
            date = "2008-05-22T04:26:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10287#comments:id=292433",
        },
        {
            id = 5600838,
            score = 3,
            author = "Warlordmom",
            text = "If you are doing this on live now leveling a new toon or going back and doing old content you will need to spam your target interact hotkey to bypass the scroll. If you try to do the standard right/left click to turn in the Cenarian Spirits it will try to use the scroll repeatedly. I was only able to bypass this by making sure I had set up my interact with target to a keybind setting (H is what I used) and then made sure to press it a few times quickly to get the Cenarian Spirits to turn in.",
            date = "2023-05-04T14:56:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10287#comments:id=5600838",
        },
        {
            id = 51442,
            score = -1,
            author = "Ambushed",
            text = "\"6 reputation with Horde\" means all Horde factions - Meaning Dearskpear, Org, Silvermoon, TB, UC",
            date = "2007-03-15T04:46:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10287#comments:id=51442",
        },
        {
            id = 644639,
