    [10320] = {
        {
            id = 34560,
            score = 159,
            author = "15699",
            text = "I was able to solo this with very minimal support, as a 70 shadow priest. There was a friendly tauren druid who would cast moonfire or starfire on Naberius, but that was towards the end of the fight.\n\nHere is a synopsis of the strategy I used:\n\nNaberius: \"Grr, I'm going to cast frostbolt on you\"\nPlayer: \"I'm going to duck around the corner.\"\nNaberius: \"Gosh I can't see you anymore. Let me run after you.\"\nPlayer: \"I came back out from the corner!\"\nNaberius: \"Grr, let me cast frostbolt on you again.\"\n\nHere is the strategy I used in more detail:\n\nClear the area surrounding the church of any ghosts. Then clear the inside of the chapel of the two stationary ghosts. Like people have mentioned in previous comments, Naberius will use frostbot as a primary attack. He needs a few seconds to cast this, of course. So what you do, is mindflay or renew any dots you want to use while he is casting, then quickly move out of line of sight from the frostbolt. This will cause him to stop casting, and move after you. Once he does this, move back out into his line of sight. He will again try to frostbolt you. Mindflay, or wand, whichever you prefer. Then before he finishes casting, move out again.\n\nI used the chapel as a means to escape line of sight from Naberius by moving around corners just as he was finishing frostbolt.\n\nOh, and if you see the red diagram under your feet, move out of the way.\n\nYou could probably solo this as a lower level shadow priest. The strength is in the strategy and execution.",
            date = "2007-02-12T08:18:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10320#comments:id=34560",
        },
        {
            id = 22491,
            score = 50,
            author = "13088",
            text = "You can find him in a church at (63,79). This quest is actually very soloable. Inside his room are two Tortued Spirits which can be pulled independently from Naberius. Naberius casts Frostbolt so it's very easy to LoS him. Don't get too close to the edge because he does a knockback. Lastly, stay out of the red portals he summons.",
            date = "2007-01-21T17:36:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10320#comments:id=22491",
        },
        {
            id = 26518,
            score = 18,
            author = "Fugazi",
            text = "Only dangerous things he does are red portals. Its small aoe 1000 damage per tick. Avoid that and nuke him down before he nuke you with his frostbolts :p",
            date = "2007-01-28T16:49:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10320#comments:id=26518",
        },
        {
            id = 40698,
            score = 18,
            author = "zhek",
            text = "If you choose not to solo, be warned he can mind control one player. The debuff isn't typed, so not dispellable.",
            date = "2007-02-22T17:52:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10320#comments:id=40698",
        },
        {
            id = 29653,
            score = 16,
            author = "annick",
            text = "Immune to gouge, kidney shot, blind, cheap shot, rupture, garrote.\n\nPlaces the red circles on the ground under you that instantly hit you for 1000 damage then tick for more if you stay in them. Doable as a 69 combat sword rogue, but based on luck. If you get bad crit streak you'll die.",
            date = "2007-02-02T19:36:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10320#comments:id=29653",
        },
    },
    [10321] = {
        {
            id = 27167,
            score = 15,
            author = "12554",
            text = "Located at 48,81",
            date = "2007-01-29T13:22:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10321#comments:id=27167",
        },
        {
            id = 38455,
            score = 9,
            author = "16445",
            text = "Enter the manaforge from the west: there's an elite guarding the east door, and the overseer's on the west side anyway. Techs spawned two at a time, but still easy. Elite wanders a bit, but will not path around to the west side.",
            date = "2007-02-19T01:14:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10321#comments:id=38455",
        },
        {
            id = 39463,
            score = 9,
            author = "Alarius",
            text = "Do this along with Attack on Manaforge Coruu (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10246).",
            date = "2007-02-20T16:51:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10321#comments:id=39463",
        },
        {
            id = 133299,
            score = 3,
            author = "4324",
            text = "Speed is the key.  Either watch your back constantly or spin a lot.  Just when you think you can take a breath a couple of them will appear out of nowhere.  If you have a ranged attack, hit them with the ranged attack when they try to channel on the mana forge.  That will break their attempt to abort the shutdown, and agro them.  They're MUCH less to worry about one you have them agro'ed.",
            date = "2007-08-06T15:23:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10321#comments:id=133299",
        },
        {
            id = 810799,
            score = 2,
            author = "390657",
            text = "The respawn for the overseer is two minutes, give or take about 3 seconds.  She spawned on me just after I activated the shutdown, and just as the cutdown completed.  Becareful also where you choose to stand guard while ensuring the techs don't abort the countdown as she spawned right in the spot where I was standing and gave me a couple \"Target must be in front of you\" before I was able to BBQ her back to oblivion.",
            date = "2009-08-13T21:23:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10321#comments:id=810799",
        },
    },
    [10322] = {
        {
            id = 30320,
            score = 25,
            author = "kingdave27",
            text = "Loc 59, 67\n\nThe Duro Access Crystal drops from Overseer Athanel.",
            date = "2007-02-04T00:51:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10322#comments:id=30320",
        },
        {
            id = 39349,
            score = 14,
            author = "25150",
            text = "I suggest completing these other quests at the same time as this one:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10267\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10328",
            date = "2007-02-20T12:54:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10322#comments:id=39349",
        },
        {
            id = 46841,
            score = 11,
            author = "28929",
            text = "Overseer is at 60.0, 68.4.",
            date = "2007-03-05T23:57:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10322#comments:id=46841",
        },
        {
            id = 23279,
            score = 8,
            author = "12909",
            text = "Completed it just now without problems. Grab the Access Crystal in the small room inside the Manaforge and defend the console for 2 minutes.",
            date = "2007-01-23T13:15:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10322#comments:id=23279",
        },
        {
            id = 253724,
            score = 6,
            author = "104399",
            text = "The entrance on the northeast side (61,65) is much easier than the one on the northwest side.\n\nThe northwest entrance has  six archers all packed together, armed with immolation shot. They'll throw nets and run, sometimes towards the others, aggro'ing them and the problems spirals outward from there, as they can grab the Sunfury Conjurers to join against you.\n\nThe northeast entrance had a single Sunfury Centurion  fighting one of the Nether Anomolies.\n\nTIP: Inside the manaforge center, if you ignore the Anomalies and focus on killing the Sunfuries first (and refrain from doing any damage to the Anomalies), the Anomalies will gang up on the Sunfuries and even  assist you in killing them. As soon as the Sunfury you're fighting dies, the Anomaly will hunt down another Sunfury instead of fighting you. (You'll have to face the Anomalies eventually, but you might as well take their help while you can and then stomp them flat after the Sunfuries are dead.)",
            date = "2008-03-15T10:28:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10322#comments:id=253724",
        },
    },
    [10323] = {
        {
            id = 215422,
            score = 27,
            author = "8792",
            text = "It's possible to walljump up the interior side of the Manaforge after triggering the shutdown, from there all the mobs will evade, all you have to do is keep them in combat for two minutes, no fighting necessary.",
            date = "2008-01-09T05:19:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10323#comments:id=215422",
        },
        {
            id = 26692,
            score = 17,
            author = "5288",
            text = "About three times more mobs spawn to try and stop you, so it's harder than the other manaforges but still pretty easy so long as you have the suggested 3 people. Elite spawns at the end, he's also straightforward and easy to kill.",
            date = "2007-01-28T21:41:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10323#comments:id=26692",
        },
        {
            id = 93308,
            score = 11,
            author = "8601",
            text = "The conrtols are at, 25, 38\n\nand entrance is at 25,41\n\nIts a good idea to clear room before doing it, 2 Elites spawn. Any extra mobs would suck. AoE classes would be the best for this.",
            date = "2007-05-29T23:32:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10323#comments:id=93308",
        },
        {
            id = 44455,
            score = 6,
            author = "18571",
            text = "Possible to solo for - I did it as 70 lvl feral druid with equipped tanking gear.\nMobs are spawning fast and I was able to kill only few of them, but they are not hitting too hard, so just attack those trying to stop countdown (channeling beam toward console) and survive two minutes. I've died 5 seconds before shutdown but still completed the quest.",
            date = "2007-03-01T08:37:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10323#comments:id=44455",
        },
        {
            id = 352692,
            score = 4,
            author = "131009",
            text = "This is a bit of a stretch to do, but if you're wanting to solo it with your big shouldered, tauren male self, there is a way to do this (it takes two exploits of the area, though).\n\nFirst, head into the forge and clear the four nethermancers that are positioned around the center of the forge.  Grab the activation crystal, and head out of the South-East entrance.\n\nOnce you're outside, get on your mount, back a way a bit from the entrance, and fly in fairly high through the doorway.  It's pretty random when it happens, but normally you can fly through the entrance and stay mounted in the forge (if it doesn't work a few times, just keep flying in straight without pausing;  it shouldn't take more than a minute of attempts).  Fly to the normal spot in the forge for using the evade bug trick, and make sure you're properly positioned before you touch down;  you'll probably dismount the moment you touch anything  (As to why you kill the nethermancers when doing this, they can aggro as you fly in, and there isn't a high enough ceiling to drop aggro from them).\n\nAfter all that, you can just do the evade bug trick as normal where you hit mobs as they come in.  One thing I've noticed about the evade bug is that sometimes the big guys will still channel a shutdown once they start, so try to tag them before they get a chance to cause a problem.",
            date = "2008-08-14T11:49:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10323#comments:id=352692",
        },
    },
    [10325] = {
        {
            id = 51968,
            score = 52,
            author = "22023",
            text = "To get this quest do the following preqs:\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10210\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10211\n\n10 Marks of Kil'jaeden hand ins @ Friendly will give you:\n\n250 rep with The Aldor\n125 rep with The Sha'tar\n-275 rep with The Scryers\n\nTo max your rep with these hand ins do the following:\n\nSince the rep increase stops when hitting honored, you want to get as close as you can\nto the end of Friendly before doing the last hand in. You will want to push your rep as far as possible into Honored\nwhen handing in the last one.\nSo when you're starting to get to the end of Friendly, change to the other hand in quest, \"Single marks of Kil'jaeden\" (its a quest from the same guy, difference is you only hand in 1 Mark of Kil'jaeden instead of 10).\nUsing them get to 5975/6000 Friendly. Then once again hand in 10 Marks of Kil'jaeden which will bring you to 225/12000 Honored.",
            date = "2007-03-16T05:17:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10325#comments:id=51968",
        },
        {
            id = 2418297,
            score = 17,
            author = "gbalkam",
            text = "NPC wont talk to you?  Haven't selected a faction?  You didn't talk to A'dal yet and he won't speak to you?  Are you feeling snubbed?  No worries.\nJust find the Haggard War Veteran just outside the entry to the center of the city where A'dal is.  He'll get you started on  your way!\n\nUnfortunately since I am level 85 the low level quest did not appear on the map, so I had to do the old mouse and click trick. LOL.",
            date = "2016-09-30T12:56:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10325#comments:id=2418297",
        },
        {
            id = 5233913,
            score = 13,
            author = "Dervacus",
            text = "Mark of Kil'jaeden (https://www.wowhead.com/item=29425/mark-of-kiljaeden) is most definitely level-locked, meaning it will no longer drop after a certain level. I was not able to get it to drop on my level 60 or level 50 characters, but could get it with a fairly high drop rate on my level 36 character (which was not attuned to the Burning Crusade timeline). Once I can confirm what the cutoff level is, I will update",
            date = "2021-08-08T15:59:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10325#comments:id=5233913",
        },
        {
            id = 24195,
