            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10341#comments:id=94906",
        },
        {
            id = 810825,
            score = 4,
            author = "390657",
            text = "I had a very weird experience doing this quest.  Of the 3 or so bowmen on the upper ridge, I had just killed the last one at having pulled him towards me 55.99, 63.67.  Just after he died I couldn't figure out while I was still \"in combat\".  I then saw a centurion come over the little fence, down and through the bowmen below the ridge (without adding them), so he could attack me.  He couldn't have been an add or he would have already been attacking me while I was still fighting the bowman - not a few seconds after I was done.  Also not sure why none of bowmen he ran through didn't join him.\n\nI can only assume he got hung up on some sort of pathing glitch, so keep an eye out when pulling.  Another note also: Although they have no mana bars, the bowmen may cast Immolate  (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=11667)at least once before closing to melee.\n\nEdited to correct myself: It's not a spell.  Their arrows proc the immolate effect.",
            date = "2009-08-13T22:10:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10341#comments:id=810825",
        },
    },
