    [10405] = {
        {
            id = 26451,
            score = 109,
            author = "10938",
            text = "The quest item drops of \"Ethereum Archon\" and Ethereum Overlord\" (southern part of the camp).",
            date = "2007-01-28T14:34:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10405#comments:id=26451",
        },
        {
            id = 49716,
            score = 96,
            author = "Tochiazuma",
            text = "Random drop, had nothing to do with where they were standing or anything. Took about 25 kills.\n\nLike every low drop rate quest, of course, there are lots of posts about 'tricks' to use how to get the item. Just kill, kill, kill. ;)",
            date = "2007-03-11T19:11:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10405#comments:id=49716",
        },
        {
            id = 26484,
            score = 32,
            author = "17317",
            text = "Pretty bad drop rate, it took around 30 kills to get mine.\n\nThe Archon's and Overlord's are around 56,46.",
            date = "2007-01-28T15:43:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10405#comments:id=26484",
        },
        {
            id = 2298435,
            score = 11,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R3VgIT3l-tM\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10405\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10405, from the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20482 (summon him first by clicking on the Ethereum Transponder Zeta) at coords 56.8, 38.6 (Ethereum Staging Grounds).\n•\009Travel southwest, further into the Ethereum Staging Grounds, and kill Ethereals located there until you loot the https://www.wowhead.com/item=29591.\n•\009Travel back to coords 56.8, 38.6.\n•\009Turn in the quest to the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20482.",
            date = "2016-01-15T14:36:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10405#comments:id=2298435",
        },
        {
            id = 347986,
            score = 8,
            author = "Zeluha",
            text = "\"I need a wrapping from an archon or overlord that might be transforming soon in order to calibrate the device.\"\n\nIt does say this in the quest, however, it's still not 100%... it, however, is a much higher droprate off them. That or I just got really lucky. I killed over 20 of them not watching what they were doing - both the archons and the overlords, but the second one I killed that was \"transforming\" i got the item...\n\nDunno... Just my two cents ;P",
            date = "2008-08-08T21:58:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10405#comments:id=347986",
        },
    },
    [10406] = {
        {
            id = 62423,
            score = 50,
            author = "ghostdrive",
            text = "worst quest ever.\n\nfirst the bug,\n\nmake sure you are standing on the platform that summons the quest giver or else the escort NPC will not show.  Tested this numerous times, it only showed up for me while standing on the platform.\n\nSecond, the design of the area.\n\nMobs are tightly packed, here so be careful.  the problem with this quest is that there is way too much shit lying on the ground making it confusing to complete. I didn't know which way the npc would turn towards, he would turn right, and then left, making you aggro the mob to the right, not knowing that you don't have to kill it.\n\nNot to mention the distance from the quest area from the nearest rez point, way to go blizz on keeping me logged in for an extra 12 minutes to run to my corpse.\n\nThird, GG Bliz.\n\ntrying to add lore to this quest makes it really stupid.  Not only to i have to deal with summoning the quest giver in a dangerous area, but the summoned NPC escort is just as stupid, i mean there are maybe 4 types of soloable quests in this game, why would you have to make this one any different by adding a summonable NPC in an aggroable area ?\n\nI give you 1/10 for effort, worst quest ever.\n\nBy the way if your a mage, use mage armor its hella easier",
            date = "2007-04-05T08:06:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10406#comments:id=62423",
        },
        {
            id = 42985,
            score = 34,
            author = "18798",
            text = "if you fail the quest by letting the guy die, you have to wait about 10 min before he respawns. pretty annoying, i thought it became broken after the demolitionist was killed.",
            date = "2007-02-26T19:00:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10406#comments:id=42985",
        },
        {
            id = 67194,
            score = 28,
            author = "23252",
            text = "As others have said, make sure you've got the area to the south cleared before you accept this quest, because he WILL chain-pull the entire thing.  By the time I killed the first two, he'd aggroed three more and I was at half-health.\n\nAnd yes, after accepting the quest you get a 10-min debuff before you can try again.\n\nOnly thing worse than an escort quest, is an escort quest with a NPC that doesn't even bother to pause on his route and had a 10-minute cooldown.\n\nWorst quest in netherstorm, IMO.",
            date = "2007-04-14T15:18:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10406#comments:id=67194",
        },
        {
            id = 99982,
            score = 19,
            author = "1826",
            text = "Ice Block removes the \"you can only summon a demotionalist every 10 minutes\" debuff",
            date = "2007-06-07T07:07:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10406#comments:id=99982",
        },
        {
            id = 2298432,
            score = 11,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8cUZ_Hguptk\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10406\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10406, from the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20482 (summon him first by clicking on the Ethereum Transponder Zeta) at coords 56.8, 38.6 (Ethereum Staging Grounds).\n•\009A https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20802 will appear.  You must protect the Demolitionist while the NPC continues through the Ethereum Staging Grounds.\n•\009After you receive notification that the quest is complete, travel north to coords 56.8, 38.6.\n•\009Turn in the quest to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20482.",
            date = "2016-01-15T14:34:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10406#comments:id=2298432",
        },
    },
    [10407] = {
        {
            id = 2174040,
            score = 61,
            author = "430429",
            text = "Perhaps you are wondering how you can get this quest... You need to have completed Allegiance to the Aldor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10551/allegiance-to-the-aldor) (to do this quest you first need to do A'dal  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10210) and City of Light (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10211)).\n\nAfter you're affiliated with The Aldor, you need to talk with Exarch Orelis (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19466/exarch-orelis) in Netherstorm, Area 52 Inn. You will then need to complete all of the Anchorite Karja (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19467/anchorite-karja) and Exarch Orelis (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19466/exarch-orelis) quests.",
            date = "2015-04-29T09:55:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10407#comments:id=2174040",
        },
        {
            id = 35675,
            score = 31,
            author = "17490_",
            text = "Soloable by a 70 rogue. Premed / Cb hemo spec, With Drakefist, 1400ap , 8k hp.\n\nMorug:\n\nHas a \"Poison Splash\" Aoe that hits for 900ish with a 200+ dot over 10 seconds. The range seems to be about 15 yards. Casts about once every 30 seconds.\n\nHas a throw ability where he hurls his saw blade at you. Around a 30 yard range and hits for 900-1100 on 20% damage reduction.\n\nAverage melee from 500-800.\n\nDefinitely the harder of the two for this quest, but it can be soloed with proper use of cooldowns and some patience. Has about 29k hp ( according to mobhp )\n\nMake sure to clear a suitable area to fight just before you pull. Respawns will wipe you.\n\nYou will want to keep crippling poison up for this fight.\n\nStart off with a CS > Shiv > Rupture then run  towards your cleared kill zone. Make sure to keep him in combat with deadly throw / ranged weapons. You will probably be hit with his saw blade attack, don't worry.\n\nAs soon as he reachs your kill spot, Immediately hit evasion and reach 5 combo points. Keep doing white dps while saving your cp until evasion wears. Gouge into a kidney shot ( gouge is to prevent an unlucky parry / dodge / block ) Dps him during the ks and move backwards just before it wears off, hopefully he will be slowed and you can stay safely out of his melee range until your gouge cooldown comes back up.\n\nUse your blind early, and CoS out of his poison dot every time it is up.\n\nThe fight should consist of brief periods of melee to gain combo points, followed by a gouge > kite > gouge > ks > melee > gouge repeat.\n\nYou do NOT want to stay at range for a long period of time, long enough for you gouge cooldown to finish. Staying at range for too long will result in not having enough hp to finish the fight. Do not give him an extended window in which to poison you / saw attack. You should have a max of 6 seconds of kiting to preform before you run in to gouge unless a special misses.\n\nUse all your cooldowns early. This includes bandages and potions. They will probably refresh before you kill him.\n\nIf your gouge / ks don't connect for some reason, just shiv him with cripple and kite some more. You have about 5-6 minutes to play with him before respawns of the spot you cleared return, so don't feel you have to rush the fight.\n\nSilroth:\n\nHas a \"chemical flames\" attack. Not as issue at all, just run out of it.\n\nHas another flame based attack, I didn't catch the name because it was so easy to interrupt. Takes about 3 seconds to cast. Just kick / gouge / whatever to get him to stop.\n\nAverage melee on leather for 400-700\n\nIf you soloed Morug first, this guy is a cakewalk.\n\nSimilar strat to Morug . Clear an area to work in. This is the only part harder than Morug in some respects. There are many many more patrols by Silroth. I cleared a path west up upon a hill to where I could see the ecodome and fought him there.\n\nI used mind numbing poison main hand and cripple off hand for this fight.\n\nCS > Shiv > Rupture > Run to cleared area.\n\nEvasion tank it up till 5 CP then Gouge > Ks > Melee > Gouge etc.\n\nI could tank his damage much more easily than Morug's. With a liberal use of kick and a blind / bandage thrown in I didn't have to kite him much at all.\n\nHe has about 10k hp less than Morug ( According to mobhp ) and seems to have less damage reduction.\n\nIt may take you a few tries to get the hang of it, but this quest is definitely soloable by a decently geared rogue who knows how to handle the fight.",
            date = "2007-02-14T04:07:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10407#comments:id=35675",
        },
        {
            id = 23956,
            score = 28,
            author = "Prozen",
            text = "Found Forgemaster Morug at 37,27 (68 elite)\nSilroth at 41,19 (68 elite)",
            date = "2007-01-24T19:00:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10407#comments:id=23956",
        },
