    [10408] = {
        {
            id = 62307,
            score = 82,
            author = "2542",
            text = "Warning to warriors: Salhadaar's Stasis ability clears all buffs and auras, including your stance.  You are put into \"no stance\", and your toolbar switches to the \"no stance\" toolbar.  You probably have never seen this toolbar, so it's probably going to be blank.  So you're tanking along, when suddenly your ENTIRE TOOLBAR VANISHES.  Fun, eh?  Just hit one of your stance buttons and all will be well.",
            date = "2007-04-05T01:24:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10408#comments:id=62307",
        },
        {
            id = 27399,
            score = 47,
            author = "14235",
            text = "After killing all the adds around the pillars..start the event by cutting off his energy shield supplies using the quest item.\n\nWhoever does the last gets the initial aggro.\n\nKite him down into the canyon just to the southeast of the platue he starts on. Ensure you keep your backs towards the inside of the continent cause his knockback ( which is un-interruptable) could potentially knock you off the island. When he gets to 50-60% he spawns several adds. Allow the main tank to maintain the aggro on the boss and kill of the adds. Adds down..kill the boss. Besides the knockback he also does stasis on a  . Only lasts a few seconds.",
            date = "2007-01-29T21:27:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10408#comments:id=27399",
        },
        {
            id = 285359,
            score = 20,
            author = "133296",
            text = "well, another bug to add to this crappy quest. if the person who activates it dies, then the guy becomes untargetable and the rest of the party can't finish him off. what a terribly buggy piece of !@#$.\nIt finally worked with 1 person using their disruptor at all spots, and people focusing on the add when it came out, not just the boss. I also (tank) moved out of the way of his explosion so I wasn't thrown in the air. Honestly don't know if any of those 3 things helped, but he didn't bug out when we did the combination of these things.\nIt appears that he's still bugged if more than one person destroys his pylons. Just have one person do it.\nAfter killing all the adds around the pillars..start the event by cutting off his energy shield supplies using the quest item. Whoever does the last gets the initial aggro.\nthis quest is still bugged, but what ended up working was having the rogue take on the copy while i tank the other. when the copy vanished, the real one was still targetable and could take damage.\nAh yes. As has been mentioned earlier, this happens when not all the disruptors are set by the same person. Have one person set ALL the disruptors, or this may happen.\nBe careful not to get too far away from the place he is captured. After he turned back into himself after splitting into his clones, we couldn't target him anymore, because the tank had pulled him very far away from his original \"spawn\" location. This may be a bug, but it happened twice for us before we could finally kill him.\n\nSeems that if you follow all these rules, you'll be in good shape to kill this boss. I mean, alot of these are repeats, and only quotes from this \"Thread\", but I just decided to condense it into one easy to read list. Just do what this says, and you SHOULD be fine. If doing ALL OF THE ABOVE doesnt work, then nothing is a solution except pure luck. Good luck, and I hope you complete it, the reward is nice, especially as a 70. lulz.",
            date = "2008-05-09T21:59:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10408#comments:id=285359",
        },
        {
            id = 2562945,
            score = 17,
            author = "Beace",
            text = "Unless you're a tank with strong self-heals, or possibly a hunter/warlock, you're not gonna solo this fight with the new level scaling in place.",
            date = "2018-04-15T07:34:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10408#comments:id=2562945",
        },
        {
            id = 25568,
            score = 16,
            author = "5121",
            text = "He's hard, but doable. Our first try, he bugged.\n\n2nd try we - made 1 guy (MT) use the disruptor on all three (and only him), and he was attackable. Gives some bonus threat too, i think.\n\nWe wiped at adds though (un- rootable/kiteable and 10-15k hp), and two people had to leave.\nSo, my proposition is just PEW PEW PEW boss after add spawns",
            date = "2007-01-27T08:24:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10408#comments:id=25568",
        },
    },
    [10409] = {
        {
            id = 35157,
            score = 54,
            author = "23179",
            text = "Scryer version of this quest:\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10507",
            date = "2007-02-13T08:55:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10409#comments:id=35157",
        },
        {
            id = 26831,
            score = 39,
            author = "17512",
            text = "Place to use item is in the gateway located at 36, 18.\n\nThat ports you to 31, 18 which after a few nonelites, you fight Socrethar and Kaylaan.",
            date = "2007-01-29T02:00:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10409#comments:id=26831",
        },
        {
            id = 40154,
            score = 25,
            author = "19313",
            text = "The teleportation stone still remains in my inventory after i completed the quest, i did 99% of all quests and have not found any other use for it, so unless you want it for the fun of teleporting its safe to delete.",
            date = "2007-02-21T20:55:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10409#comments:id=40154",
        },
        {
            id = 128047,
            score = 18,
            author = "32973",
            text = "Ok.. the full story would be,\n3 Aldor NPCs spawn, and you tell one of them that \"I'm ready.\"\n\nNPCs will proceed to Socrethar. They will start talking, after a while Kaylaan will spawn and Socrethar will cast a spell on him and make him fight us.\n\nKaylaan will cast \"Heal\" when he is low on HP, can be interrupted. Just simply take him down.\n\nSoon after, Ishanah will spawn and start talking again.\nIshanah and the other 2 Aldor NPCs will attack Socrethar, and the main point is, Ishanah will be tanking Socrethar.\nSocrethar will cast a \"fireball\" spell which is an AoE, avoid this by attacking it from behind or ranged. Also a \"Shadowbolt Volley\" but this can be interrupted, and you better interrupt it if you dun have a healer in group.\n\nIshanah is an uber tank and she can heal herself, there are more than one way to do this without a full group -\n\n1. A warrior taunts Socrethar with shield wall when Ishanah is about to die. So she will have time to heal back to about 80%.\n\n2. Shaman lays Earth Elemental Totem, same function as a warrior, being a soap :p\n\n3. Warlock's banish.\n\nafterall, it's a DPS fight.\n\nOne more point to add in, Scyers have the same quest on killing Socrethar, which they will have an item to weaken Socrethar(damage done lowered by 3/4 & damage taken increased by 400%).\nCombining the Aldor NPCs with Scryers' weakening buff.\nYou can certainly auto-attack on Socrethar and go for a sleep.. lol",
            date = "2007-07-28T01:02:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10409#comments:id=128047",
        },
        {
            id = 1639924,
            score = 18,
            author = "reiahart",
            text = "For those now doing this quest for transmog items, in order to acquire these quests you need to be friendly/honored with Aldor and NOT Scryer.\n\nOnce you make sure you are able to do Aldor quests you start doing quests that Anchorite Karja (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19467) gives you until the quest giver Exarch Orelis (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19466) starts offering you quests. He will offer the three quests or so and choose Sunfury Briefings (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10328). Complete this quest until Socrethar's Shadow (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=10407) becomes available from Karja.\n\nNote: If you are unsure of where to become Honored with Aldor go to around the center of Shattrath and find Haggard War Veteran (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=19684#starts). He will start the chain quest to allow you to choose which opposing faction you wish.\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2012-03-15T14:29:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10409#comments:id=1639924",
        },
    },
