    [10411] = {
        {
            id = 24041,
            score = 74,
            author = "12403",
            text = "64, 46 for the seeping sludges, then drink your \"Navuud's Concoction\" and seeping sludge globules come out.\n\n57,45 for the void waste, drink and the void waste globule come after an attack.",
            date = "2007-01-24T21:49:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10411#comments:id=24041",
        },
        {
            id = 2019647,
            score = 57,
            author = "whecks",
            text = "1. find a nice high ledge to stand on\n2. disarm your weapons\n3. jump off ledge and die\n4. take the resurrection sickness\n5. return to mob area\n6. punch mobs into weakness\n7. apply tag/net/lasso/electric/etc.\n\nYes, it will cost you to repair your armor.\nYes, you will be sick for 10 minutes.",
            date = "2014-10-26T22:55:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10411#comments:id=2019647",
        },
        {
            id = 136655,
            score = 30,
            author = "73537",
            text = "=========================================================\nHorde Report – The Kaoethiel Experience\n=========================================================\n\nQuest Giver Location: 59.3, 32.5\nActual Quest Location:\n55.6, 42.5 – Void Waste Globules\n57.9,39.3 – Seeping Sludge (You find many pools scattered around the Mana Forge Ultris, this is one of many.)\n\nQuest Giver Name: Researcher Navuud – Consortium Humanoid\nQuest Chain – Starting Quest: None – Non-Chain\nFollowing Quest: None – Return to Quest Giver\nRecommended Level: 70\n\n=========================================================\n\nQuest Notes: The quest giver gives you a potion of charges called “Navuud’s Concotion” (Looks like a jar of water ((yes blue)) with a cap on top)  You drink this, and it gives you a 1 hour buff (that disappears when you die, but no fear, Its reusable as much as you like, unlimited charges).\n\nYou go out and find the parental unit of these globules, (Seeping Sludges, and Void Wastes) and engage in a fight… MAKE SURE THE POTION BUFF IS ON!  Shortly after the engagement, the parental sludge/waste bursts into a ton of tiny guys that run around like crazy.  You are required to kill them.  As a Mage, 2 arcane explosions (maybe 3 depending on your spec) should kill the little ones.  Each parental unit explodes in to approximately 6-10 little guys.  You’re required to kill 30 of each kind to complete the quest.  Simple in Theory.\n\nHaving a buff like Thorns, Molten Armor, Retaliation, etc that causes damage when you’re hit makes life A LOT easier downing the little ones.\n\n=========================================================\n\nAlliance Watch: MODERATE – Many quests in this area for the Consortium faction. I ran into a few, all questing, so they didn’t bother me.  They also have quests in this area, so odds of attack are low, but hey, who can predict human nature.\nQuest Rank of Ease: Average – AOE Class has it the easiest, but with the Agro in the area and the fairly quick respawn rate, this isn’t necessarily an easy task.\n\nQUESTIONS? COMMENTS? WANT A QUEST REVIEW POSTED NOT YET DONE BY KAOETHIEL? PLEASE FEEL FREE TO EMAIL! Chrism0221@gmail.com",
            date = "2007-08-12T19:01:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10411#comments:id=136655",
        },
        {
            id = 2573394,
            score = 21,
            author = "Blackbeardswe",
            text = "Shoft foam shword dont work, but if you drink the given potion and then just melee swing them with an auto attack they will split (like a banana).",
            date = "2018-06-11T06:11:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10411#comments:id=2573394",
        },
        {
            id = 5593952,
            score = 21,
            author = "Dalers",
            text = "After banging my head against this as a lvl 70 (dragonflight) paladin, getting nekkid and hitting them was not working, i found that what did work was just hitting them with a RANGED spell (judgement in this case), got them to break apart.",
            date = "2023-04-24T05:40:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10411#comments:id=5593952",
        },
    },
