            author = "113053",
            text = "Please note: if you are a druid, you cannot use the Phase Disruptor while in flight form.  You get an error saying \"Can't use items while shapeshifted.\"  And there's no place to perch to lob the bombs that is close enough to the Void Conduit. Druids will have to use the drake or have their own separate flying mount.",
            date = "2007-12-30T13:22:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10438#comments:id=209905",
        },
        {
            id = 2298445,
            score = 7,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N1_mLcUoUas\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10438\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10438, from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20907 at coords 60.0, 31.8 (Protectorate Watch Post).\n•\009Click on the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20903, next to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20907, and select \"I am ready to fly…\"\n•\009While on your trip to the top of Manaforge Ultris, you will see a https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20899.  Use the https://www.wowhead.com/item=29778, you were provided to neutralize it.\n•\009Your https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20903 will return you to Protectorate Watch Post.\n•\009Turn in the quest to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=20907 (coords 60.0, 31.8).",
            date = "2016-01-15T14:44:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10438#comments:id=2298445",
        },
    },
    [10439] = {
        {
            id = 23579,
            score = 63,
            author = "Tehdew",
            text = "Soled this with my 68 warlock. Just stood in the hallway, he ain't able to attack me there, took some minutes, but still soloable for a ranged class ;)",
            date = "2007-01-24T08:46:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10439#comments:id=23579",
        },
        {
            id = 297079,
            score = 44,
            author = "xaratherus",
            text = "Ensure that you do ~30% of the total damage to Dimensius; otherwise you will not \"tag\" him, and when he dies it does not count for you whether you're in the building or not when he dies.\n\nI confirmed this with a GM via ticket after soloing this twice as a 70 Holy Paladin, healing the Captain and only occasionally damaging Dimensius, and failing to complete the quest both times.",
            date = "2008-05-30T11:48:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10439#comments:id=297079",
        },
        {
            id = 44492,
            score = 28,
            author = "29175",
            text = "You really only need 2 people and can do this very simply if they both have the quest.  Have one talk with Captain Saeed and go up the hill.  Work Dim over (from ranged) until almost all of the NPCs are dead.  Then have the other player fly down and talk with the Captain again and bring him up again.  We did this quest in about 8 minutes.",
            date = "2007-03-01T10:26:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10439#comments:id=44492",
        },
        {
            id = 29092,
            score = 22,
            author = "19237",
            text = "It's possible to solo as a holy paladin, just keep the npcs up (esp the captain) and the NPCs will dps the boss down for you. The dps near the end gets really slow however as npcs start dying so watch ur mana.\n\nIn theory then any healer should be able to solo this.",
            date = "2007-02-01T18:34:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10439#comments:id=29092",
        },
        {
            id = 1516922,
            score = 21,
            author = "Lovestar",
            text = "I just solo'd him down as a fresh 68 DK for the tanking trinket. Here is my advice for any melee classes. :>\n\nAttempting to do the fight \"properly\" — attacking him, killing the adds — simply overwhelmed me with damage due to his unavoidable Shadow Vault (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=37412) spam. Even using all my CDs and playing Rune Tetris to maximize DS couldn't keep up.\n\nThe comment above saying to not kill the adds is simply smashing, and it was the key to victory for me. If you ignore the adds, Dimensius will ONLY channel Shadow Rain (basically green laser beams) — he'll do NO other attacks. The damage from these beams works in two ways — one, it hits random spots in a circular area surrounding Dimensius. And two, this circular area keeps periodically expanding away from Dimensius, and then collapsing back towards him.\n\nWhat this means is that if you leave the adds up, suddenly all the damage Dimensius does is completely avoidable. Just wait for the circular range of the beams to expand out from him, then run in next to him when you see a gap/hole in the laser beam spread. You'll then have a good 20-30s to DPS him, totally uninterrupted. When the beams start getting uncomfortably close again, wait for another gap in their coverage and run out. Now just wait for the beams to expand back away from Dimensius, run back in, and repeat this process until he's dead. You will take literally zero damage once you get the hang of it!\n\nNOTE: Stay out of the fight — a good long distance away — until the NPCs bring Dimensius' health down far enough for him to yell and start channeling Shadow Rain. Being in the room pre-Shadow Rain is basically suicide without a healer or outleveling the content.\n\n---\n\nPoor Saeed and those brave, beautiful, super-hot smooth-voiced Ethereal hunks will... will ... (fans self) ... Ahem. Anyway, your NPC helpers will die, but that's OK. You don't need them. Just keep doing the Laser Dance and beating away at the giant blue linoleum-coated pillow.\n\nAnd finally, I would like to note that the only loot Dimensius had on his body was a pair of Decaying Leather Pants (http://www.wowhead.com/item=25363). I'll let your imagination take it from there.",
            date = "2011-09-13T06:59:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10439#comments:id=1516922",
        },
    },
