            score = 4,
            author = "66097",
            text = "They also have a teleport ability so just keep it in mind if your fighting at range they might warp into melee with you, if your already in melee they warp behind you.",
            date = "2007-08-31T16:18:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10487#comments:id=147221",
        },
    },
    [10488] = {
        {
            id = 22899,
            score = 19,
            author = "13604",
            text = "Use on Thunderlord Dire Wolves, which can be found directly south of Thunderlord Stronghold (ie: 51,62). May turn some hostile (2 out of 5 for me)",
            date = "2007-01-22T17:39:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10488#comments:id=22899",
        },
        {
            id = 434807,
            score = 12,
            author = "63891",
            text = "ROFL too bad we can't rate screenshots, the one from this quest is priceless; go fetch dem bones! XD",
            date = "2008-11-07T23:29:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10488#comments:id=434807",
        },
        {
            id = 718179,
            score = 10,
            author = "337142",
            text = "Tip for priests: The buff Ointment gives is DISPELLABLE.\n\nYou can do all the 5 charges on same wolf, just dispel the buff they get and re-apply the ointment. :)",
            date = "2009-05-16T16:43:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10488#comments:id=718179",
        },
        {
            id = 373653,
            score = 9,
            author = "Smilodon",
            text = "This quest makes no sense. It reads: \"I want you to take this ointment and apply it to our dire wolf friends. The Alliance will get a rude surprise the next time that they send one of their hunting parties. Be aware though that some of the wolves may not like this, and will turn on you.\"\n\nThis may as well read: \"I want you to go slap, poke and prod these animals with a whooping stick and make them really really angry. The Alliance will get a rude surprise the next time that they send one of their hunting parties. Be aware though that some of the wolves may not like this, and will turn on you.\"\n\nPersonally, I think Gor'Drek should be reported to PETA, as the point of this quest is clearly just to torture innocent, non agressive animals before brutally killing them.",
            date = "2008-09-11T07:00:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10488#comments:id=373653",
        },
        {
            id = 1867853,
            score = 8,
            author = "madcowman42",
            text = "Amazing screen shot. Just sayin...",
            date = "2013-06-18T02:01:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10488#comments:id=1867853",
        },
    },
    [10489] = {
        {
            id = 24213,
            score = 42,
            author = "15577",
            text = "I found him @ 37,72\n\nLooks like he patrols the North-South path right there below Sylvannaar",
            date = "2007-01-25T06:24:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10489#comments:id=24213",
        },
        {
            id = 69821,
            score = 15,
            author = "10100_",
            text = "This guy, despite his size, is really easy. I think he has a bit more HP than what you fight in the surrounding area, but he doesn't swing for much and he doesn't have any real special abilities. Just the usual, dps him down.",
            date = "2007-04-19T20:41:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10489#comments:id=69821",
        },
        {
            id = 815526,
            score = 13,
            author = "384637",
            text = "My biggest challenge with this was reading the instructions. As a 67 hunter with a behind-the-curve 62 Sporebat pet, I skim the quest, only process the words \"Kill,\" \"tree\" and \"Sylvanaar\" and head off there to kill the first tree I see. How many could there be? It turns out that there are two, and the one I found first was the Level 70 Elite Ancient Protector that guards the place.\n\nThe worst part was that I didn't even notice — not while I was busy killing Sylvanaar guards, not while lying in wait for the Protector and hiding from some Ally PCs (since I was now flagged for PVP from killing all the guards), not while getting my face stomped by the tree while thinking to myself, \"this seems hard for a level 66 quest,\" not even while I flew back to the Horde camp to pick up my level-appropriate Gorilla, return to Sylvanaar, kill some more guards and burn down the Ancient. No, I finally noticed when I looked around for the stump and it wasn't there.\n\nThen, I actually read the quest, cursed, flew off to the south and got fried by a Griffon Rider, my body falling amid the tallest peaks of the mountains. Hello resurrection sickness.\n\nAfter all that? The guy's easy. Clear a couple cats/fey dragons while he's pacing and -- assuming you can read better than I --  you won't have trouble.",
            date = "2009-08-18T09:32:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10489#comments:id=815526",
        },
        {
            id = 29966,
            score = 10,
            author = "19809",
            text = "Spawn point is as mentioned above - or for those without the co'ords, if u head directly south from Sylvanaar, you come to a cave, he will spawn a few paces north up the path from the cave entrance.",
            date = "2007-02-03T10:14:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10489#comments:id=29966",
        },
        {
            id = 33206,
            score = 4,
            author = "18555",
            text = "What's up with the \"I soloed this EASY\" comments? The quest doesn't even say you should do this in group, and who cares on what server you play on :P\n\nBy the way, confirmed that he is patrolling the road south of Sylvanaar. Watch out for Alliance ^^",
            date = "2007-02-09T15:10:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10489#comments:id=33206",
        },
    },
    [10502] = {
        {
            id = 33358,
            score = 14,
            author = "18459",
            text = "A good quest to pair this with is: A Strange Brew. The brew and ogres can be found at this location (45, 75) http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10511",
            date = "2007-02-09T22:51:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10502#comments:id=33358",
