        {
            id = 3186171,
            score = 1,
            author = "TerribleAtGames",
            text = "I picked up all available quests at Stardust Spire and went ahead with https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13913, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13979 and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25607 in the dummy-horde forest location north of Silverwind Refugee. I thought this Silverwind Refugee was yet another dummy horde camp, and began to slaughter my way through it for reaching Mystral Lake. Being a lvl 99, it would be a piece of cake. Until it became obvious that the third guard in my pull was not going to let himself be killed by me, and actually killed both my voidtank and myself.\n\nSo this is a warning to every [faction=469]-questers: Silverwind Refugee is actually taken over by the filthy Horde. Do not go near this occupied post unless you have a raid group or wanna test your luck!",
            date = "2020-01-25T23:36:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26470#comments:id=3186171",
        },
        {
            id = 1498927,
            score = -2,
            author = "arabian",
            text = "One of the quests that show the actual truth about the Horde, and that the Orcs never changed, even after getting \"cured\" from their demonic blood.",
            date = "2011-08-19T22:24:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26470#comments:id=1498927",
        },
    },
    [26472] = {
        {
            id = 1402169,
            score = 46,
            author = "Rooibos",
            text = "I was kinda baffled by the quest description.\n\nI can feel the corruption even from here and I dare go no further.\n\nWhile I am too well attuned to Ashenvale and the Forest Heart, you... you could descend into the barrow den and do what must be done.\n\nSo he can't - for some reason, likely being afraid of getting corrupted as well  - descent into the den, but:\n\nI've laid down breadcrumbs for you in there.\n\nWhen? How?",
            date = "2011-04-27T23:46:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26472#comments:id=1402169",
        },
        {
            id = 1202510,
            score = 36,
            author = "Whiterock",
            text = "Questtwig: Forest Purification\n\nReclaiming Felfire Hill (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26446)\nClosure is Only Natural (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13766)\nThe Shadewalker (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13792)\nInsane Druids (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26472) and The Forest Heart (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13796)",
            date = "2010-12-02T15:51:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26472#comments:id=1202510",
        },
        {
            id = 1352442,
            score = 24,
            author = "773774",
            text = "the \"breadcrumbs\" spoken of above are florescent green diamond shapes. ...hopin' that helps.",
            date = "2011-02-27T20:17:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26472#comments:id=1352442",
        },
        {
            id = 1211121,
            score = 10,
            author = "715246",
            text = "After running around throughout the den/barrow trying to locate each druid, I almost went insane too. There's a chance that these directions might be slightly off, but hopefully the cords are right.\n\nThe path leading to the den starts at 72.3,68.8 off of the main road. Gaivan Shadewalker is located right in front of the entrance to the den/barrow (75.6, 75.6). Note: Gavian is in spirit cat form (he was a druid) and therefore pretty much invisible. He can be hard to see.\n\nTaneel's the easiest druid to locate; after you enter the den and follow the path, you'll come to an opening. There's 2 bridges (I think); one that's in the center and one that's to your right. There is also a ramp, to your left. Taneel is located across the center bridge.\n\nNext, take the ramp that is to your left (the one that is next to the two bridges). This will lead you to Uthil, Mavoris and the The Forest Heart (if you're doing that quest the heart is located in front of Mavoris).\n\nThis is where I started to get turned around a bit. So to avoid confusion, here's what helped me find the remaining two druids and the heart: Be sure to follow the \"breadcrumbs\" that are on the ground. On my computer, the \"breadcrumbs\" actually looked more like sugar cubes, but whatever lol. If you're following a path that has no \"breadcrumbs\", you're going the wrong way.\n\nUthil - 78.1, 72.9\nMavoris - 75.1, 74.2",
            date = "2010-12-07T02:32:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26472#comments:id=1211121",
        },
        {
            id = 1714213,
            score = 7,
            author = "MustaCWN",
            text = "Whiterock is still rigth. You need the other quests in order to get any fom Gaivan Shadewalker:\n\nForest Purification\nReclaiming Felfire Hill\nClosure is Only Natural\nThe Shadewalker",
            date = "2012-09-15T19:06:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26472#comments:id=1714213",
        },
    },
