            author = "L0vel0rn",
            text = "The story of the Mantle of Predation reminds me of the story of the Deathly Hallows in Harry Potter. In The Tales of Beedle the Bard, the eldest of the three brothers who have defeated Death chooses to possess a wand like no others, that would never lose a duel. He fights with the wand and of course wins, only to be killed in his sleep by the next power-hungry wizard. Whoever owns it, is destined to be stabbed in the back by the next person/entity seeking power.",
